{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter","id":1536501,"title":"Matter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-29T06:02:14-07:00","id":1536501,"title":"Matter","content":"Im looking for a way to give different qalities to matter but i dont know that sphere level RAW is used for that.<br /> Some sources say that making something harder is matter 3.<br /> But if that is so then whats the difference between this and creating new materials with matter 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T07:07:27-07:00","id":1536505,"title":"","content":"Which qualities are you looking for?<br /> <br /> For material hardness, I interpret the Sphere levels as:<br /> <br /> Matter 2: Turn soft steel into carbon steel<br /> Matter 3: Increase density to increase hardness<br /> Matter 5: Turn material into Unbreakium (or increase density permanently)<br /> <br /> I reserve Matter 5 for material with really outlandish (ie magic) properties - Kryptonite, Vibranium, Unobtainium etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T07:23:48-07:00","id":1536507,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>. <br /> <br /> In a more general sense, with Matter 2 you can alter one substance into another (of the same phase, for... reasons). With Matter 3 you can alter the common properties of matter, like density, hardness, conductivity, shape, phase, etc. Matter 5 lets you give the less common properties (like radioactivity for some reason) and create &quot;impossible&quot; properties or substances (this brick passes through glass, but not stone).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T07:48:17-07:00","id":1536508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536507#post1536507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a>.<br /> <br /> In a more general sense, with Matter 2 you can alter one substance into another (of the same phase, for... reasons). With Matter 3 you can alter the common properties of matter, like density, hardness, conductivity, shape, phase, etc. Matter 5 lets you give the less common properties (like radioactivity for some reason) and create &quot;impossible&quot; properties or substances (this brick passes through glass, but not stone).</div> </div> </div> </div>So how much harder can something get? 1 armor per success?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T10:32:47-07:00","id":1536514,"title":"","content":"Sounds about right to me for a rule of thumb, although I would tie the effect to the purpose instead of attributes. If your goal is armor, there is an example Trinket in M20 that transforms a jacket into armor which adds 4L soak for impact weapons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536507#post1536507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(of the same phase, for... reasons)<br /> (like radioactivity for some reason)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think those restrictions were well meant but futile attempts by the writers to prevent player shenanigans, and so seem pretty arbitrary. Turning something into plasma or BE-condensate is on paper a simple change of phase. With a little math you can discover that creating baby black holes is just a question of density to which the answer isn't all that unattainable on small scales. Degenerate neutron star matter may be a simple Matter 2 effect away. Or anti-matter, strange matter, and a multitude of other things from the Book of Bad Ideas.<br /> It's easier to invoke the anthropic principle of &quot;it doesn't work because you are still here to try it, as it didn't work for the idiot who tried it before you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T11:53:46-07:00","id":1536516,"title":"","content":"I think the limit for radiation has more to do with old pop culture ideas about radiation, which also informed its meaning in WtA.<br /> <br /> Personally I rule that with conjunctional Forces 3 or Prime 4 you can create radioactive materials, if for no other reason because that represents the natural transmutation of their mass into energy (actually it is stored energy, but it works).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T15:06:44-07:00","id":1536537,"title":"","content":"Game books are also generally not written by physicists.<br /> <br /> Whenever a game book talks about radiation I mentally insert &quot;ionizing&quot; in front of it unless the text gives me good reason not to. While it doesn't completely resolve everything, it's a more meaningful distinction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-29T16:01:35-07:00","id":1536539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536537#post1536537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Game books are also generally not written by physicists.<br /> <br /> Whenever a game book talks about radiation I mentally insert &quot;ionizing&quot; in front of it unless the text gives me good reason not to. While it doesn't completely resolve everything, it's a more meaningful distinction.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. If we take the books literally mages would have a tough time making glow in the dark novelty items and anything stone they made would read as older than the planet with uranium dating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T12:39:01-07:00","id":1536577,"title":"","content":"To be fair, physics doesn't really apply when magic gets involved. The whole point of using a sphere is to bypass consensus inertiaSpeak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T15:07:05-07:00","id":1536588,"title":"","content":"So again what would altering the hardness or density or mass mean in game terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T15:54:37-07:00","id":1536591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536588#post1536588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again what would altering the hardness or density or mass mean in game terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to make something more dense (and thus harder and with greater mass) while keeping it the same material it started as, that would be Matter 3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-30T16:13:47-07:00","id":1536592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536577#post1536577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, physics doesn't really apply when magic gets involved. The whole point of using a sphere is to bypass consensus inertiaSpeak</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is more in how things are phrased by the authors to us the players of the game. While many people read &quot;radiation,&quot; and think weird green glowing stuff, a decent number of people know that radiation is a broad term that covers a lot of stuff. Plus lots of positions in between. Everything is radioactive. It's just that most things aren't radioactive in a fashion that doesn't cause ionization in other particles. We have things like carbon dating because carbon undergoes radioactive decay, and we can use carbon decay's process as a constant to base calculation of the passage of time from.<br /> <br /> When the book says that radioactivity is a Matter 5 issue, it creates a bunch of oddities that don't seem to be what the text really cares about. I think most people would feel that magically creating a text that would stand up to scientific scrutiny as being two thousand years old should not need to rely on Matter 5... but technically the rules say it should because radioactive decay is a simple way to tell a modern reproduction from an ancient item. I highly doubt Brucato really meant that fooling decay-based-dating is a Matter 5 issue. But when the rules make such functions a variable in which level to use, it does matter to how we apply them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536588#post1536588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again what would altering the hardness or density or mass mean in game terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever makes sense? Hardness and density can be positives or negatives depending on your goal and intentions. Altering such properties could grant soak dice, or something wildly different. If you make someone's clothing incredibly hard, you could be leveling penalties to physical actions as the clothing becomes too stiff to move properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-31T01:15:02-07:00","id":1536611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536588#post1536588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So again what would altering the hardness or density or mass mean in game terms?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if it is what you are asking, but if you are looking for something like a table that would translate a dice roll into hard values that quantify the effect you are out of luck. Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> mentioned, the system shorthands attributes you would also have to consider outside of the general scope of the spell.<br /> <br /> That's what I meant when I said earlier that I would tie the effect to the purpose: If you want to make something harder to protect yourself, your effect is 'armor', not 'harder material' per se. The resulting effect in game (soak) is something different than, say, you want to make a plank of wood stronger to carry more weight. It's a lot easier to translate a roll into whatever the spell 'wants' rather than trying to simulate an effect with hard values.<br /> <br /> Edit: An exception might be an Enlightened Scientist whose Focus is tied to such things as concrete physical values. If they study an effect, they would likely have tests that measure what it does- but even in that case, it would still be more practical to abstract those values into game values that match how the result is used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 05-31-2024, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T23:21:46-07:00","id":1538466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1536592#post1536592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue is more in how things are phrased by the authors to us the players of the game. While many people read &quot;radiation,&quot; and think weird green glowing stuff, a decent number of people know that radiation is a broad term that covers a lot of stuff. Plus lots of positions in between. Everything is radioactive. It's just that most things aren't radioactive in a fashion that doesn't cause ionization in other particles. We have things like carbon dating because carbon undergoes radioactive decay, and we can use carbon decay's process as a constant to base calculation of the passage of time from.<br /> <br /> When the book says that radioactivity is a Matter 5 issue, it creates a bunch of oddities that don't seem to be what the text really cares about. I think most people would feel that magically creating a text that would stand up to scientific scrutiny as being two thousand years old should not need to rely on Matter 5... but technically the rules say it should because radioactive decay is a simple way to tell a modern reproduction from an ancient item. I highly doubt Brucato really meant that fooling decay-based-dating is a Matter 5 issue. But when the rules make such functions a variable in which level to use, it does matter to how we apply them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, on the other hand, am perfectly on board of &quot;radioactive decay&quot; being under the purview of Matter 5. And under a strict &quot;sCientific&quot; Paradigm. The attribute of &quot;old&quot; is something that is exotic enough to be under the purview of the lvl 5. I think that, under a scientific paradigm, determining the rate of carbon decay in an item is something only possible at the most diminutive atomic level, while under a mystic view, &quot;young&quot; or &quot;old&quot; aren't commonly attributes that are associated with the Transmutation of matter. In my view, creating a computer that has the atomic age of a dinosaur is as exotic as any kind of Unobitaniums around.<br /> <br /> Not that I agree with the whole &quot;radioactive&quot; stuff in general. But in this specific case, I do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-13T19:28:29-07:00","id":1538548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538466#post1538466\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, on the other hand, am perfectly on board of &quot;radioactive decay&quot; being under the purview of Matter 5. And under a strict &quot;sCientific&quot; Paradigm. The attribute of &quot;old&quot; is something that is exotic enough to be under the purview of the lvl 5. I think that, under a scientific paradigm, determining the rate of carbon decay in an item is something only possible at the most diminutive atomic level, while under a mystic view, &quot;young&quot; or &quot;old&quot; aren't commonly attributes that are associated with the Transmutation of matter. In my view, creating a computer that has the atomic age of a dinosaur is as exotic as any kind of Unobitaniums around.<br /> <br /> Not that I agree with the whole &quot;radioactive&quot; stuff in general. But in this specific case, I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that by not creating radioactive materials, what you're creating is already things that read as &quot;old as all Hell&quot; to any radio-dating method.<br /> <br /> So, your brand-new synthetic metal laptop? It <b><i>does</i></b> have the atomic age of a <i>T. Rex</i>, <b>precisely </b>because you can't make the naturally occurring radioactive isotopes used to assess age.<br /> <br /> I'm not completely against the idea that age, as measured by the best methods, should be hard to fake with magic. We could have as a rule that you need Matter 5 to alter the natural occurrence of radioactive materials on your creations. The problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> points is that by saying that you can't create any such material, the result if taken literally would be wildly different from the intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T23:15:42-07:00","id":1538597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538548#post1538548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that by not creating radioactive materials, what you're creating is already things that read as &quot;old as all Hell&quot; to any radio-dating method.<br /> <br /> So, your brand-new synthetic metal laptop? It <b><i>does</i></b> have the atomic age of a <i>T. Rex</i>, <b>precisely </b>because you can't make the naturally occurring radioactive isotopes used to assess age.<br /> <br /> I'm not completely against the idea that age, as measured by the best methods, should be hard to fake with magic. We could have as a rule that you need Matter 5 to alter the natural occurrence of radioactive materials on your creations. The problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> points is that by saying that you can't create any such material, the result if taken literally would be wildly different from the intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Yeah, what I had in my mind was different, what I had in my mind is that, whenever you create anything with Matter it just reads as &quot;brand new!&quot; by anyone trying to carbon date it, because that's the &quot;natural state of newly created stuff&quot;. So, you don't actually create &quot;radioactive stuff&quot; out of some though through proccess, but rather just out of some &quot;cosmic expectations&quot; (or just &quot;Consensus&quot;) for how that matter should behave.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I agree that all of this requires a bit of mental gymnastics to make it work, but I do think that, since we are limiting enriched uranium to Matter 5 (which I gotta say I am not personally against), then likewise we should limit age forgeries to higher levels of Matter (maybe also Matter 5, but definitely more than just 2)<br /> <br /> Edit: or, better saying, we should have a better explanation about the &quot;radioactive&quot; green glowing stuff, but common, we more or less know that the intent behind the text was not that technocrats can easily any conjured stuff because they appear older than Earth itself every single time... We know that was not intentional, just some thing created by artists rather than by physicists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-15-2024, 02:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T16:47:07-07:00","id":1538636,"title":"","content":"By all means, we know the literal interpretation isn't the intended result, it's just an observation of how the rules sometimes say stupid things because the authors didn't knew what they were talking about.<br /> <br /> The problems are two-fold, though. First, this does results in eventual conflicts because many players and STs have a reasonable grasp of those concepts, and modern internet exacerbates this aspect.<br /> <br /> Second, and specially in this case, it creates limits based on misconceptions of how things work. Lets take Uranium as an example: it doesn't dish enough ionizing radiation to be an immediate hazard without ridiculous amounts of material and highly advanced prep. Even as ammunition it is useless for anything less than modern heavy artillery. It's just a heavier steel, hard to work, crappy for most jobs, and whose only other regular use is to die glass. It isn't even expensive (if natural. Enriched it is expensive as hell).<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, Uranium doesn't glow green in black light because of radiation. All versions (enriched, depleted and natural) glow just the same. This glow is a chemical property of the material that shouldn't require Forces, unless you think that making any glowing toy requires Forces.<br /> <br /> Why Mages can't create Uranium? Because the setting buys into a mythos around radiation and atomic fuel that still lingered in the 90's. It sees radiation as &quot;special&quot; in an undefined way. But the result is that while your Mage needs Matter 5 to create some green dye for glass, they only need Matter 3 and some Google-Fu to replicate the technology that can actually turn ugly rocks, beach sand and water into a Hydrogen Bomb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-15T17:05:50-07:00","id":1538640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538636#post1538636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By all means, we know the literal interpretation isn't the intended result, it's just an observation of how the rules sometimes say stupid things because the authors didn't knew what they were talking about.<br /> <br /> The problems are two-fold, though. First, this does results in eventual conflicts because many players and STs have a reasonable grasp of those concepts, and modern internet exacerbates this aspect.<br /> <br /> Second, and specially in this case, it creates limits based on misconceptions of how things work. Lets take Uranium as an example: it doesn't dish enough ionizing radiation to be an immediate hazard without ridiculous amounts of material and highly advanced prep. Even as ammunition it is useless for anything less than modern heavy artillery. It's just a heavier steel, hard to work, crappy for most jobs, and whose only other regular use is to die glass. It isn't even expensive (if natural. Enriched it is expensive as hell).<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, Uranium doesn't glow green in black light because of radiation. All versions (enriched, depleted and natural) glow just the same. This glow is a chemical property of the material that shouldn't require Forces, unless you think that making any glowing toy requires Forces.<br /> <br /> Why Mages can't create Uranium? Because the setting buys into a mythos around radiation and atomic fuel that still lingered in the 90's. It sees radiation as &quot;special&quot; in an undefined way. But the result is that while your Mage needs Matter 5 to create some green dye for glass, they only need Matter 3 and some Google-Fu to replicate the technology that can actually turn ugly rocks, beach sand and water into a Hydrogen Bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div>i wouldn\u2019t say that it is undefined. The explanation is because objects with considerable radioactivity are a fusion of Matter and Forces patterns. So if you want to make uranium, Matter 2 Forces 3 would provably be what is required.<br /> <br /> i am sure one can make the argument that \u201ceverything is radioactive at least a little\u201d to which I would counter that in Mage, the real world explanations of science are simply a paradigm of the technocracy built in to the consensus. They hold little sway over the basic elements of how patterns behave. In fact, unless something is common knowledge, I\u2019d go so far as to argue most of the scientific explanations for why or how things work is just a fiction initially that only becomes true because it sounds plausible enough for a few people to believe it. It sits at the border of sorcery and consensus, but does not necessarily need to be factored in at all for awakened magic<br /> <br /> This is why I usually advise that when magic is involved the laws of physics can become very loosely applied. Especially if one does not have a scientific paradigm upon which they make their transmutations.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T06:54:21-07:00","id":1538652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538636#post1538636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why Mages can't create Uranium? Because the setting buys into a mythos around radiation and atomic fuel that still lingered in the 90's. It sees radiation as &quot;special&quot; in an undefined way. But the result is that while your Mage needs Matter 5 to create some green dye for glass, they only need Matter 3 and some Google-Fu to replicate the technology that can actually turn ugly rocks, beach sand and water into a Hydrogen Bomb.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538640#post1538640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i wouldn\u2019t say that it is undefined. The explanation is because objects with considerable radioactivity are a fusion of Matter and Forces patterns. So if you want to make uranium, Matter 2 Forces 3 would provably be what is required.<br /> <br /> i am sure one can make the argument that \u201ceverything is radioactive at least a little\u201d to which I would counter that in Mage, the real world explanations of science are simply a paradigm of the technocracy built in to the consensus. They hold little sway over the basic elements of how patterns behave. In fact, unless something is common knowledge, I\u2019d go so far as to argue most of the scientific explanations for why or how things work is just a fiction initially that only becomes true because it sounds plausible enough for a few people to believe it. It sits at the border of sorcery and consensus, but does not necessarily need to be factored in at all for awakened magic<br /> <br /> This is why I usually advise that when magic is involved the laws of physics can become very loosely applied. Especially if one does not have a scientific paradigm upon which they make their transmutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here. I don't think you need Matter 5 to conjure Uranium. You can create Uranium with Matter 2.<br /> <br /> What you do need Matter 5 for is to create ENRICHED Uranium.<br /> <br /> The properties of matter patterns are the metaphysical properties rather than the physical/chemical scientific properties.<br /> <br /> Because, we must not forget that we are talking about a world upon which &quot;da sCience&quot; is a conspiracy.<br /> <br /> I find it absolutely hilarious that this is a game played mostly by progressives upon which they play with rednecks that claim that science is a &quot;CIA conspiracy&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this is the truth of the setting. Bla bla bla Uranium bla bla bla U235 bla bla bla isotopes. Technobabble. In the game, all of that is as good as the 4 humourous or saying that everything is made out of Earth, Wind and Fire (and Water).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. Yeah, what I had in my mind was different, what I had in my mind is that, whenever you create anything with Matter it just reads as &quot;brand new!&quot; by anyone trying to carbon date it, because that's the &quot;natural state of newly created stuff&quot;. So, you don't actually create &quot;radioactive stuff&quot; out of some though through proccess, but rather just out of some &quot;cosmic expectations&quot; (or just &quot;Consensus&quot;) for how that matter should behave. </div> </div> </div>That's what I was talking about. What is considered &quot;normal&quot; has nothing to do with the periodic table of elements from physics and chemistry. It is, instead, a matter of &quot;metaphysical expectations&quot; from reality. Enriched Uranium never happens naturally, it is the result of a highly technological and complicated process of heavy industry (aka this means A LOT of Technocratic Sorcery involved into bringing this process into the Consensus).<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bI think that it could be made clear that newly created matter won't register as billions of years old, because that's not how the metaphysics of matter work; but I'm not against the ban on &quot;radioactive&quot; material - yes, we all know what they meant here, they meant the comic books style of &quot;radioactive&quot; here. So, we understand their meaning, but ok, it could've been made clearer to avoid nitpicking, and also to dissociate the Matter Sphere from just simple chemistry and explain it in more metaphysical ways (like the Alchemists of old would)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T14:08:15-07:00","id":1538673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538640#post1538640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i wouldn\u2019t say that it is undefined. The explanation is because objects with considerable radioactivity are a fusion of Matter and Forces patterns. So if you want to make uranium, Matter 2 Forces 3 would provably be what is required.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The amount of radiation found in natural Uranium and most other radioactive materials is negligible for game effects, it can only be harnessed under very strict conditions.<br /> <br /> Coal has more readily available energy, yet you don't need Forces to make coal, do you?<br /> <br /> Either way, the rule doesn't say you need Matter 5 to create natural materials that also have Forces patterns. They say you need Matter 5 to create magical materials or radioactive ones. This is pretty blatant on my opinion as making radiation undefined special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T15:05:13-07:00","id":1538680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538673#post1538673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The amount of radiation found in natural Uranium and most other radioactive materials is negligible for game effects, it can only be harnessed under very strict conditions.<br /> <br /> Coal has more readily available energy, yet you don't need Forces to make coal, do you?<br /> <br /> Either way, the rule doesn't say you need Matter 5 to create natural materials that also have Forces patterns. They say you need Matter 5 to create magical materials or radioactive ones. This is pretty blatant on my opinion as making radiation undefined special.</div> </div> </div> </div>Coal does not contain a Forces pattern, so the comparison is a bit strange. It isn't about whether or not the object in question is flammable, it is about whether a Forces pattern is being shed from the Matter pattern.<br /> <br /> And I assure you, the rules are quite explicit about radioactive matter patterns requiring mastery because of the Forces pattern they shed off, and this has been the case in every edition of the game.<br /> <br /> M20 Pg 518<br /> 'Matter 2 Basic Transmutation....(On a related note, the mage cannot yet fabricate radioactive materials. Such elements merge their essence into the Sphere of Forces, and thus demand a greater level of expertise.)'<br /> <br /> M20 Pg 519<br /> 'Matter 5 Alter Properties With Mastery, the crafter can create substances that transcend the limitations of scientific possibility, conjure materials unknown to Earthly reality, or share the deadly legacies of radioactive matter.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> Mage Revised Pg 172<br /> 'Matter 2....Only simple and inert forms of Matter can be transformed at this level. The mage cannot make radioactive elements. Doing so requires Mastery, as such Patterns shed their essence in the form of Forces.'<br /> \u200b<br /> Mage Revised Pg 174<br /> 'Matter 5, Matter Association....With a few successes, he might tweak the weight and interactive properties a bit, while many successes would allow the mage to reverse fundamental properties, make an inert substance radioactive or vice-versa.'<br /> <br /> \u200bMage 2e Pg 204<br /> 'Matter 2, Basic Transmutation...With difficulty, a stick of plastique could be conjured (but not the detonator), though a couple plutonium spheres are out of the question (the highly radioactive elements cannot be created until Rank 5).<br /> <br /> Mage 2e Pg 205<br /> 'Matter 5 Alter Properties...The rare prizes of Technocratic science, such as the manmade radioactive elements, are also reserved for this level.'<br /> <br /> Mage 1e Pg 201-202 (less specific to radioactivity, but still relevant on a conceptual level)<br /> 'Matter 2 Create Unified Patterns, The Mage can only create patterns that are stable in the environment in which they are created (e.g., she could not create a pool of liquid nitrogen in a room-temperature environment; such would first require knowledge of Forces to freeze the nitrogen).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T16:38:00-07:00","id":1538682,"title":"","content":"So, can I create a lodestsone (a naturally occurring piece of magnetized iron) with Matter 2 or Matter 5? A magnet is a Matter pattern &quot;shedding&quot; a Forces Pattern.<br /> <br /> If I can create a magnet at Matter 2, then radioactivity being exclusive to Matter 5 doesn't hold as the logic of Forces Patterns isn't being applied evenly.<br /> <br /> If I can't create a magnet with Matter 2, what can I create that isn't shedding Forces Patterns? Any substance that isn't at absolute zero is interacting with heat; a Forces Pattern. Any fluid created would be having kinetic Forces Patterns that interact with its environment. Etc. etc. etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-16T18:12:01-07:00","id":1538685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538682#post1538682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can I create a lodestsone (a naturally occurring piece of magnetized iron) with Matter 2 or Matter 5? A magnet is a Matter pattern &quot;shedding&quot; a Forces Pattern.<br /> <br /> If I can create a magnet at Matter 2, then radioactivity being exclusive to Matter 5 doesn't hold as the logic of Forces Patterns isn't being applied evenly.<br /> <br /> If I can't create a magnet with Matter 2, what can I create that isn't shedding Forces Patterns? Any substance that isn't at absolute zero is interacting with heat; a Forces Pattern. Any fluid created would be having kinetic Forces Patterns that interact with its environment. Etc. etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, here's the thing. Obviously the writers didn't write that piece with the uttermost scientific rigour. I think we should look at it more from a metaphysical point rather than a scientific one. &quot;Enriched Uranium&quot; (or any other elements used for nuclear fission) is NOT the isotope 235 of Uranium.<br /> <br /> In fact, in MtA, Uranium is NOT Uranium.<br /> <br /> We might as well call it &quot;Technobium&quot; material.<br /> <br /> Heck, a Hermetic could even summon a &quot;Hellstonium&quot; rock that causes death and decay.<br /> <br /> What I mean by this is that all of this &quot;technobabble&quot; that in the real world is REAL science, in MtA is just as BS (or just as real, depends on your pov) as astrology or tarot.<br /> <br /> That means that what we call as &quot;dangerous radioactive material&quot; that in the real world is enriched Uranium or Cesium or Plutonium and that the technobabble bullshittery of the Technocracy has the same names, in reality could just as well be classified as &quot;Hell's stones&quot;. <br /> <br /> So, let's try it again:<br /> <br /> &quot;You need Matter 5 in order to create Hell's Stones&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, all of a sudden, all the confusion is gone.<br /> <br /> What are &quot;Hell's Stones&quot; you ask?<br /> <br /> Those are cursed rocks from Hell that can be used to create apocalyptic explosions and that cause a magic curse of decay on those close.<br /> <br /> Sure, the techie boys bs call it &quot;radioactive&quot; and say that is emanates a sort of energy that causes &quot;cancer&quot;. Don't listen to that nonsense.<br /> <br /> Radioactive decay yadda yadda yadda is just technobabble.<br /> <br /> Matter 5 creates green glowing rocks that goes Boom! on entire towns and cause cancer. That's it.<br /> <br /> Creating a magnet is Matter 2.<br /> <br /> And yes, the writers dropped the ball on this one. Instead of all that &quot;forces patterns from matter&quot; and whatnot, they should just add &quot;enriched Uranium has a special place on the Tellurian and on the Consensus, thus it is Matter 5&quot;.<br /> <br /> Because that's the spirit of rule, or &quot;rule as intended&quot;.<br /> <br /> PS: yes, of course that the reason is for game balance; nobody wants neonate Mages giving Plutonium teas left and right to everybody, unless that person's name is Vladimir Putin.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> But even disregarding that, I'd say that enriched radioactive material is hard enough to get and never occur naturally and requires such massive industries to create small doses of, that it perfectly entails being under the domain of Matter 5, even without game balance justifications.<br /> <br /> In here, I think it has the same reasoning behind on why you also need Matter 5 in order to create anti-matter. Yes, human industry can create it. But it is something so unnatural that it should be the domain of the Masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:13:27-07:00","id":1538710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538682#post1538682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can I create a lodestsone (a naturally occurring piece of magnetized iron) with Matter 2 or Matter 5? A magnet is a Matter pattern &quot;shedding&quot; a Forces Pattern.<br /> <br /> If I can create a magnet at Matter 2, then radioactivity being exclusive to Matter 5 doesn't hold as the logic of Forces Patterns isn't being applied evenly.<br /> <br /> If I can't create a magnet with Matter 2, what can I create that isn't shedding Forces Patterns? Any substance that isn't at absolute zero is interacting with heat; a Forces Pattern. Any fluid created would be having kinetic Forces Patterns that interact with its environment. Etc. etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The iron you create would not be \u2018magnetic\u2019, but it could be attracted by other magnetic objects.<br /> <br /> in WoD, magnetism would be a Forces effect which was locked in to a matter pattern. So you could make something magnetic with Matter 2 Forces 2, or create a magnet directly with Matter 5. Arguably, however, if you make iron in a permanent way, it may over time accumulate these forces patterns, as the metal conforms to the expectations of the consensus.<br /> <br /> Fluids do not contain Forces patterns inherently, that is a silly extrapolation. Gravity pulls all things down to earth as a Force independent of whatever Matter is doing. The liquid produced would be reacting to that external force, and from there momentum would be simply applied.<br /> <br /> a liquid that was shedding of Momentum as a forces pattern would be a liquid that would act like a conveyor belt even when completely still.<br /> <br /> Matter makes the most generic version of the substance you are making, in the most stable form. Forces patterns may interact with it, but it won\u2019t produce any Forces patterns upon its conception. So Heat might attach to it, Cold might attach to it, momentum might attach to it, magnetism might attach to it, etc, but these external forces wouldn\u2019t be originating from the object, but from the environment.<br /> <br /> and yes, in Mage, Cold, Darkness, Stillness, are all Forces patterns with their own behaviour independent of Light, Heat, and Momentum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:19:08-07:00","id":1538711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538710#post1538710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The iron you create would not be \u2018magnetic\u2019, but it could be attracted by other magnetic objects.<br /> <br /> in WoD, magnetism would be a Forces effect which was locked in to a matter pattern. So you could make something magnetic with Matter 2 Forces 2, or create a magnet directly with Matter 5. Arguably, however, if you make iron in a permanent way, it may over time accumulate these forces patterns, as the metal conforms to the expectations of the consensus.<br /> <br /> Fluids do not contain Forces patterns inherently, that is a silly extrapolation. Gravity pulls all things down to earth as a Force independent of whatever Matter is doing. The liquid produced would be reacting to that external force, and from there momentum would be simply applied.<br /> <br /> a liquid that was shedding of Momentum as a forces pattern would be a liquid that would act like a conveyor belt even when completely still.<br /> <br /> Matter makes the most generic version of the substance you are making, in the most stable form. Forces patterns may interact with it, but it won\u2019t produce any Forces patterns upon its conception. So Heat might attach to it, Cold might attach to it, momentum might attach to it, magnetism might attach to it, etc, but these external forces wouldn\u2019t be originating from the object, but from the environment.<br /> <br /> and yes, in Mage, Cold, Darkness, Stillness, are all Forces patterns with their own behaviour independent of Light, Heat, and Momentum</div> </div> </div> </div>The week point of the argument is that every object is bound by forcess, magnetic is not a special case. Object obey gravity, have kinetic and potential energy, interact with temperature and so on. We dont need forces for that if its part of the consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:24:01-07:00","id":1538712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538711#post1538711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The week point of the argument is that every object is bound by forcess, magnetic is not a special case. Object obey gravity, have kinetic and potential energy, interact with temperature and so on. We dont need forces for that if its part of the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did address this.<br /> <br /> forces from the environment act upon the object, and that is fine. The object themselves simply isn\u2019t generating new Forces patterns","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:38:44-07:00","id":1538714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538712#post1538712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I did address this.<br /> <br /> forces from the environment act upon the object, and that is fine. The object themselves simply isn\u2019t generating new Forces patterns</div> </div> </div> </div>but that makes no sense, all materials have inherited forcess properties. Everything is magnetic (on a scale), everything has heat isolation/distribution properties and so on.<br /> Your interpretation would make Matter the most vulgar sphere of all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:49:25-07:00","id":1538715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538714#post1538714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> but that makes no sense, all materials have inherited forcess properties. Everything is magnetic (on a scale), everything has heat isolation/distribution properties and so on.<br /> Your interpretation would make Matter the most vulgar sphere of all.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explanation of the world is simply part of the fiction the technocrats have instilled into their explanation of the nature of reality, one which shapes the consensus.<br /> <br /> it is how they rationalise how Forces and Matter interact, but isn\u2019t how patterns actually function.<br /> <br /> in terms of vulgarity, not at all, if it is not measurable by the outside observer at the point of creation, then it is just as coincidental as any other form of magic. And over time, unless the matter pattern has been blessed with Entropy to avoid such things, a permanently made matter pattern will eventually interact with many of the environmental Forces patterns, becoming more in line with what the consensus expects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:52:20-07:00","id":1538716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538715#post1538715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That explanation of the world is simply part of the fiction the technocrats have instilled into their explanation of the nature of reality, one which shapes the consensus.<br /> <br /> it is how they rationalise how Forces and Matter interact, but isn\u2019t how patterns actually function.<br /> <br /> in terms of vulgarity, not at all, if it is not measurable by the outside observer at the point of creation, then it is just as coincidental as any other form of magic. And over time, unless the matter pattern has been blessed with Entropy to avoid such things, a permanently made matter pattern will eventually interact with many of the environmental Forces patterns, becoming more in line with what the consensus expects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of us use omnipotent observer might i remind you<br /> <br /> As for the technocratic fiction. Its not technocratic fiction its the existing consensus. Matter as the most mundane sphere should strictly adhere to the consensus.<br /> Thats why creating materials not supported by the consensus is matter 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-17-2024, 03:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T00:58:18-07:00","id":1538717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538716#post1538716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Some of us use omnipotent observer might i remind you<br /> <br /> As for the technocratic fiction. Its not technocratic fiction its the existing consensus. Matter as the most mundane sphere should strictly adhere to the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use omnipotent observer, then any form of Transmutation or creation is vulgar regardless of how it changes, so I don\u2019t see how this would change anything.<br /> <br /> and to the outside observer, Matter does indeed conform to the consensus. What difference does it make if Iron reacts to a magnet because it produces a magnetic field that pulls itself towards the magnet, or because it is simply being pulled towards another magnet\u2019s magnetic force?<br /> <br /> in both scenarios the Iron moves to the magnet. Everything else is just explanation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T01:05:09-07:00","id":1538718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538717#post1538717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you use omnipotent observer, then any form of Transmutation or creation is vulgar regardless of how it changes, so I don\u2019t see how this would change anything.<br /> <br /> and to the outside observer, Matter does indeed conform to the consensus. What difference does it make if Iron reacts to a magnet because it produces a magnetic field that pulls itself towards the magnet, or because it is simply being pulled towards another magnet\u2019s magnetic force?<br /> <br /> in both scenarios the Iron moves to the magnet. Everything else is just explanation</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not just about magnets. Its about nitroglicerine, burning, its about termoisolation properties and so on. Literally half of creative matter uses would in this case require forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T01:23:58-07:00","id":1538720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538718#post1538718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its not just about magnets. Its about nitroglicerine, burning, its about termoisolation properties and so on. Literally half of creative matter uses would in this case require forces.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitroglicerine you would not be able to make with Matter 2 alone as it is so unstable, in the same way you can\u2019t make liquid nitrogen at room temperature.<br /> <br /> you could make liquid nitrogen with Matter 2 and Forces 3, though it would take a lot of successes.<br /> <br /> flammable things do not require Forces, they simply go on fire when an external Force ignites them. The matter pattern is just very Fire forces friendly, while other matter patterns are not friendly to Fire patterns, in the same way that glue is not friendly to momentum and mirrors are not friendly to light (or extremely friendly to light depending on how you describe it)<br /> <br /> you could think of nitroglycerine as imbuing an explosion in to a matter pattern (the liquid), and holding it in place with Entropy. Without entropy the explosion may explode the moment the liquid is disturbed, allowing the explosion to release, what Entropy does is provide some stability.<br /> <br /> making an alloy of forces imbued matter like this would likely require Matter 4, Forces 3 (2 if you can convert another explosive force, higher if you want a really big explosion) and Entropy 3 as optional ti enhance the stability of the pattern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-17-2024, 04:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T02:19:35-07:00","id":1538722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538720#post1538720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitroglicerine you would not be able to make with Matter 2 alone as it is so unstable, in the same way you can\u2019t make liquid nitrogen at room temperature.<br /> <br /> you could make liquid nitrogen with Matter 2 and Forces 3, though it would take a lot of successes.<br /> <br /> flammable things do not require Forces, they simply go on fire when an external Force ignites them. The matter pattern is just very Fire forces friendly, while other matter patterns are not friendly to Fire patterns, in the same way that glue is not friendly to momentum and mirrors are not friendly to light (or extremely friendly to light depending on how you describe it)<br /> <br /> you could think of nitroglycerine as imbuing an explosion in to a matter pattern (the liquid), and holding it in place with Entropy. Without entropy the explosion may explode the moment the liquid is disturbed, allowing the explosion to release, what Entropy does is provide some stability.<br /> <br /> making an alloy of forces imbued matter like this would likely require Matter 4, Forces 3 (2 if you can convert another explosive force, higher if you want a really big explosion) and Entropy 3 as optional ti enhance the stability of the pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>See thats just a unneeded sphere bloat. It makes way more sense for pattern spheres to create things that fit the consensus. So if vibranium existed you should be able to create vibranium with just matter. If vibranium exists on another material plane then it would not be possible to create it without matter 5 on our earth but if you go to where it exists you would be able to with just 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T04:10:47-07:00","id":1538724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538722#post1538722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See thats just a unneeded sphere bloat. It makes way more sense for pattern spheres to create things that fit the consensus. So if vibranium existed you should be able to create vibranium with just matter. If vibranium exists on another material plane then it would not be possible to create it without matter 5 on our earth but if you go to where it exists you would be able to with just 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>What lies within the purview of the spheres is less to do with the consensus and more to do with the fundamental aspects of reality that one is trying to alter.<br /> <br /> for example, just because the consensus might say that darkness is the absence of light does not mean you can\u2019t coincidentally move the shadows about to cloak yourself. Similarly just as the consensus might argue that Time and Space are the same thing does not then mean you can travel through time with Correspondence alone.<br /> <br /> it is the same reason why you can\u2019t use Forces 3 alone to turn subatomic forces (strong and weak nuclear force) in to fire. You need Prime 2 still. It is just that subatomic forces are how you describe what Quintessence is and works. If your paradigm speaks of a force which is everywhere and important for the foundation of reality, that is basically their paradigmatic explanation for Quintessence. Regardless of how much it might agree with the consensus, it is still a Prime 2 reliant effect<br /> <br /> The same is the case with mundane patterns. If it cannot fit within the limitations of the single sphere, then it either would require a higher rank to affect or would need the assistance of other spheres achieve.<br /> <br /> people throw around the term sphere bloat without really knowing what it means. If you mean that extra spheres are added where they weren\u2019t needed before, this is not an example of this as the Matter has always had this limitation. Matter 2 cannot transmute patterns that are unstable. If it could then it wouldn\u2019t be necessary to have Matter 3 to change state, or disperse a pattern. You can make explosives with matter 2, depending on the explosive in question. But not to unstable explosives such as nitro glycerine.<br /> <br /> Matter 2 alone can only make stable patterns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T04:52:55-07:00","id":1538726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538685#post1538685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, here's the thing. Obviously the writers didn't write that piece with the uttermost scientific rigour.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I made this specific point in post 12 of the thread. I'm responding to Saikou's specific assertions about how interpreting Matter 5 around the &quot;shedding&quot; of Forces Patterns by the Matter Pattern created as what makes the delineation have meaning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think we should look at it more from a metaphysical point rather than a scientific one. &quot;Enriched Uranium&quot; (or any other elements used for nuclear fission) is NOT the isotope 235 of Uranium. </div> </div> </div>The problem is, we're not talking about the setting, we're talking about the game rules. The game rules say that you need Matter 5 to make &quot;radioactive&quot; materials. It doesn't matter how a given mage views the effect via their Focus, whether it requires Matter 2 or Matter 5 is defined in the rules using real world terms so the players can understand them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;You need Matter 5 in order to create Hell's Stones&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, all of a sudden, all the confusion is gone. </div> </div> </div>Not really. Using different jargon doesn't clarify, at all, what level of involvement of Forces Patterns steps something up from a Matter 2 effect to mix Matter/Forces effect or a Matter 5 effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even disregarding that, I'd say that enriched radioactive material is hard enough to get and never occur naturally and requires such massive industries to create small doses of, that it perfectly entails being under the domain of Matter 5, even without game balance justifications. </div> </div> </div>OK... what about radioactive materials that don't require enrichment? Radon is extremely radioactive in it's most common natural form. It's just a gas, so it's not concentrated enough to cause serious health concerns (until it is, as human buildings turn into radon concentration chambers that can pose actual heath risks if not mitigated with proper ventilation systems). Radon is &quot;rare&quot; but eats up between 5% to 20% of the &quot;safe&quot; amount of background radiation for an adult human being (the range is so large because a lot of factors get involved).<br /> <br /> Naturally occurring radon is just as dangerous as enriched radioactive materials under the proper conditions.. so if a Mage can make radon gas easily as a naturally occurring substance that doesn't require massive industries to create, it wouldn't be hard to toss around radiation poisoning.<br /> <br /> Hanging your argument on the difficult of production leaves you open to these sorts of examples.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538710#post1538710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The iron you create would not be \u2018magnetic\u2019, but it could be attracted by other magnetic objects.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lodestone is naturally magnetic, why can't I make it? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in WoD, magnetism would be a Forces effect which was locked in to a matter pattern. </div> </div> </div>By this logic Matter can't do anything by itself until Matter 5 because all Matter Patterns have Forces effects &quot;locked&quot; in them. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fluids do not contain Forces patterns inherently, that is a silly extrapolation. </div> </div> </div>Yes they do. Keep in mind I said fluids, not liquids.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gravity pulls all things down to earth as a Force independent of whatever Matter is doing. </div> </div> </div>Gravity is pulling everything with mass towards everything else with mass. Exerting gravity is a fundamental property of all matter. You don't experience it as a normal person on Earth because Earth's mass is large it overwhelms almost all other natural gravitation effects. The moon is an example of something that can overcome the dominance of Earth's gravity as the gravity between the moon and the Earth is a direct contributor to tidal forces. If you sail out into the middle of the ocean during high tide, gravity is pulling you away from the Earth ever so slightly (and of course it doesn't last long)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The liquid produced would be reacting to that external force, and from there momentum would be simply applied. </div> </div> </div>Most liquids are also fluids. If they don't have natural kinetic energy, they'd solidify or exist in an unstable transition state between solid and liquid until ambient energy pushes one way or the other.<br /> <br /> A fundamental problem of all of this, is that the properties of matter are a direct result of the energy in the system the matter is part of. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> a liquid that was shedding of Momentum as a forces pattern would be a liquid that would act like a conveyor belt even when completely still. </div> </div> </div>Which is fairly normal in fluid liquids, yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Matter makes the most generic version of the substance you are making, in the most stable form. </div> </div> </div>Citation needed. Are you claiming that Matter can only create hematite with Matter 2 as the most abundant and a highly stable form of iron? You can't create metallic iron or steel?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Forces patterns may interact with it, but it won\u2019t produce any Forces patterns upon its conception. </div> </div> </div>So Matter 2 can't generate gases even if naturally occurring and stable, as all gases produce kinetic force on their environment (aka gases naturally expand to fit the volume of their container).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So Heat might attach to it, Cold might attach to it, momentum might attach to it, magnetism might attach to it, etc, but these external forces wouldn\u2019t be originating from the object, but from the environment. </div> </div> </div>This is nonsensical by any reading of the rules. You're directly arguing that Matter can deal in basic common substances without having to &quot;absorb&quot; Forces Patterns from their environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T04:57:55-07:00","id":1538727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538720#post1538720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nitroglicerine you would not be able to make with Matter 2 alone as it is so unstable, in the same way you can\u2019t make liquid nitrogen at room temperature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitroglycerine is quite stable. It's sold as a medicine. It sits on a shelf just fine. It's only if sufficient external forces act on it that it does anything special.<br /> <br /> Lecturing people about &quot;bloat&quot; when you seem to have a very limited grasp on &quot;stable&quot; isn't really a great method of arguing that the rules are clear and coherent about this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T05:44:06-07:00","id":1538729,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> you\u2019ve made too many comments to respond to each one in turn. So I\u2019ll just respond to a few points where I believe something has been misunderstood. If you wish for me to respond to a specific point you have made, I am happy for that to be highlighted.<br /> <br /> <br /> To clarify the point of a liquid acting like a converyor belt, I mean that there is a puddle on the floor, and anything that steps to it is immediately shifted in a direction, and as you try to walk in the opposite direction, you are still being pulled in the puddle\u2019s preferred direction.<br /> <br /> regarding the point \u201cexerting gravity is a fundumental property of all matter\u201d<br /> in our reality, yes. In Mage, this is not the case. This is simply a scientific explanation designed to instil people with an answer as to why things remain drawn to the ground. It is a technocratic paradigm and need not actually be the capital T Truth behind what a substance actually is, what properties it holds, and as such what spheres might affect it. Gravity instead functions as its own seperate Force, independent of any matter pattern. This is in part why a Mage out in etherspace can simply walk to other planets.<br /> <br /> Personally I find that recognising that most of physics is just a description/explanation, not a limitation or even a hard law, is very helpful to understanding the logic behind much of the pattern spheres. Heaviness is a property of a matter pattern, but how the matter pattern responds to gravity is most to do with that ever present force that seems to pull things to earth.<br /> <br /> the distinction between liquids and fluids I would say is fairly arbitrary in regards to what the Matter sphere affects. The point is more that if you make something a liquid, it will be influenced by the Forces patterns around it.<br /> <br /> as for citations<br /> <br /> M2e Pg 204 specifies creation of substances can only be a simple basic homgenous substance with Matter 2, anything more complex requires matter 4<br /> <br /> Mage Revised Pg172 states that at the level of Matter 2 you can only make \u2018simple and inert\u2019 forms of matter<br /> <br /> I point to my previous citation for 1e that references how Matter 2 can only make stable forms of a pattern<br /> <br /> and there is nothing in M20 to suggest a departure from what has been established prior.<br /> <br /> as an aside, I\u2019m not sure the ability to discuss sphere bloat is reliant on a comprehensive understanding of what stability entails. I would be reluctant to dismiss an argument on the subject on that criteria.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T05:59:56-07:00","id":1538734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538726#post1538726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK... what about radioactive materials that don't require enrichment? Radon is extremely radioactive in it's most common natural form. It's just a gas, so it's not concentrated enough to cause serious health concerns (until it is, as human buildings turn into radon concentration chambers that can pose actual heath risks if not mitigated with proper ventilation systems). Radon is &quot;rare&quot; but eats up between 5% to 20% of the &quot;safe&quot; amount of background radiation for an adult human being (the range is so large because a lot of factors get involved).<br /> <br /> Naturally occurring radon is just as dangerous as enriched radioactive materials under the proper conditions.. so if a Mage can make radon gas easily as a naturally occurring substance that doesn't require massive industries to create, it wouldn't be hard to toss around radiation poisoning.<br /> <br /> Hanging your argument on the difficult of production leaves you open to these sorts of examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about it?<br /> <br /> That's Matter 2. (Or rather, it should be)<br /> <br /> Look, you can easily produce all sorts of poison with Matter 2. Lead. Arsenic. Being poisoned by lead or by radiation won't be much of a difference for the victim.<br /> <br /> Besides, &quot;radiation&quot; is a property of the matter. Everything has it. That's not the point, and I wish the writers hadn't gone with that. Also, all that &quot;forces patterns from matter&quot; has been an awful explanation.<br /> <br /> And yes, I was being very specific about enriched stuff. Nothing more. Poisoning people is fine (just don't let the FBI read these talks, I don't think they would understand). The real problem is creating A bombs in your backyard, that's what was tried to be avoided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-17-2024, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T06:21:48-07:00","id":1538736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538720#post1538720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nitroglicerine you would not be able to make with Matter 2 alone as it is so unstable, in the same way you can\u2019t make liquid nitrogen at room temperature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Errr... What?<br /> <br /> I won't even discuss nitroglycerin because in this case you're so clearly wrong BUT... Where does it say, anywhere, that you can't make &quot;highly unstable&quot; substances like liquid nitrogen?<br /> <br /> Granted, at room temperature liquid nitrogen will just turn into gas rapidly... But where does it say you can't do it with Matter?<br /> <br /> Done with Matter 2, the Liquid Nitrogen will remain liquid for as long as the effect last. Then it will simply revert to what it once was.<br /> <br /> You're equivocate here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you could make liquid nitrogen with Matter 2 and Forces 3, though it would take a lot of successes. </div> </div> </div>No, you don't need Forces 3. It's just that the nitrogen wont do much.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you could think of nitroglycerine as imbuing an explosion in to a matter pattern (the liquid), and holding it in place with Entropy. Without entropy the explosion may explode the moment the liquid is disturbed, allowing the explosion to release, what Entropy does is provide some stability. </div> </div> </div>No, I cannot think of that at all. All that I can think of is that nitroglycerin is a simple matter (and it actually is pretty simple in real life chemical composition and fabrication) and that can be made with Matter 2, and everything else is bollocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-17-2024, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T06:31:46-07:00","id":1538738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538736#post1538736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errr... What?<br /> <br /> I won't even discuss nitroglycerin because in this case you're so clearly wrong BUT... Where does it say, anywhere, that you can't make &quot;highly unstable&quot; substances like liquid nitrogen?<br /> <br /> Granted, at room temperature liquid nitrogen will just turn into gas rapidly... But where does it say you can't do it with Matter?<br /> <br /> You're equivocate here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, you don't need Forces 3. It's just that the nitrogen will quickly evaporate. In fact, it could be a good way to &quot;evaporate&quot; solid stuff.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> No, I cannot think of that at all. All that I can think of is that nitroglycerin is a simple matter (and it actually is pretty simple in real life chemical composition and fabrication) and that can be made with Matter 2, and everything else is bollocks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding the points on liquid nitrogen, I have sourced these where it says that matter 2 makes stable or inert substances, and the point on liquid nitrogen needing Forces was taken straight from 2e on the same page.<br /> <br /> i don\u2019t mind how you prefer rule it, I am simply showing what the book says so you can be confident that you are deliberately changing how it works to better fit how you wish to run it.<br /> <br /> regarding nitro glycerine, I am speaking very specifically about a substance which explodes when submitted to enough force. You can identify a failure in understanding, and that is fair, but I did hope it would be less of a distraction to the point than it has turned out to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:12:28-07:00","id":1538741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538738#post1538738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding the points on liquid nitrogen, I have sourced these where it says that matter 2 makes stable or inert substances, and the point on liquid nitrogen needing Forces was taken straight from 2e on the same page.<br /> <br /> i don\u2019t mind how you prefer rule it, I am simply showing what the book says so you can be confident that you are deliberately changing how it works to better fit how you wish to run it.<br /> <br /> regarding nitro glycerine, I am speaking very specifically about a substance which explodes when submitted to enough force. You can identify a failure in understanding, and that is fair, but I did hope it would be less of a distraction to the point than it has turned out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right about them needing to be &quot;stable&quot;. Yes, liquid nitrogen at room temperature would be a no no, but that's not the case of nitroglycerin. The property of being &quot;stable&quot; refers to no reaction unless subjected to external energy. In that sense, both nitroglycerin and a bar of steel are stable, it's just that steel is far more stable than nitroglycerin. In Venus however, the steel would also become unstable. In Uranus, liquid nitrogen would be stable too. Alcohol is less stable than water, hence why it evaporates faster. But both water and alcohol are stable liquids at room temperature.<br /> <br /> Regardless, that whole &quot;forces patterns on matter&quot; is bollocks. It should be about naturally or effortlessly created matter. Enriched Uranium could very well be considered as &quot;technocratic sorcery&quot;, and I'm full onboard on considering it a special exception that only exists due to the Consensus. But there are several materials that already have properties like magnetism or phosphorescence naturally and that have nothing to do with Consensus (some have been know since antiquity). I know you're a hardcore &quot;devil's advocate&quot; of the RAW, but common, that really doesn't hold to scrutiny when we look a bit under the surface.<br /> <br /> There are substances that are exothermic and substances that are endothermic - aka they increase or decrease heat. And many of those are fairly simple substances, even naturally occurring substances. Are those also in the purview of Matter 5? That makes no sense.<br /> <br /> Matter 5 should specifically be the domain of &quot;exotic&quot; substances, and by &quot;exotic&quot; I mean the proverbial &quot;Unobitaniums&quot; of life, and here I make the claim that enriched Uranium (or Cesium or Plutonium) are special cases of that same category of Unobitanium that we just don't envision as such simply because technocratic sorcery has pushed that into the Consensus - but are Unobitaniums nonetheless. And I think the text of Matter would be greatly improved by having those exact descriptions.<br /> <br /> Let's imagine for a second that we live in the world of Marvel Comics. So, now we have Vibranium as a &quot;technocratic sorcerous marvel&quot;. Ok, Vibranium is part of the Consensus, and we can industrialize that. We can make spoons of Vibranium, and it is now part of our everyday lives. Cool. But it is still Unobitanium nonetheless.<br /> <br /> &quot;Matter 5: the Master of Matter can create &quot;Unobitanium&quot;, aka materials that shouldn't really exist and with exotic properties. Enriched radioactive materials are also forms of Unobitanium, that have been pushed into the Consensus by the Technocracy, but are Unobitaniums nonetheless&quot;<br /> <br /> That's what the description of Matter should say.<br /> <br /> Now, having a piece of silicon glow should either have Forces or Matter 5, but that's because this is an exotic property to silicon; it's not something that silicon naturally does, just like an armor of steel is not supposed to magnetically repel bullets.<br /> <br /> Now, I have to admit that this opens up to the possibility of an entire bag of worms here. Is Kevlar Matter 2 or 5? What about plastic?<br /> <br /> I think Matter may be a Sphere that is much more prone to bend under Consensus than any other<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T07:51:57-07:00","id":1538749,"title":"","content":"Matter 2 restricts changes in state or temperature, but turning room temperature water into room temperature liquid Nitrogen is possible. Adding Forces 2 means the mage could change room temperature water into standard temperatures of liquid nitrogen. It might be Forces 3 but I think that's a HDYDT thing.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 takes off the restrictions of Matter 2 which I've generally read as allowing temperature changes appropriate to the new substance and state. Temperature may not be specifically mentioned, but there are a lot of stated abilities of Matter 3 that dramatically change the energy in the system, temperature is just the most obvious. So turning ambient gaseous nitrogen into cold liquid nitrogen with just Matter 3 should be possible. <br /> <br /> That said, it wouldn't be an unreasonable interpretation that Matter 3 still can't change temperature, though it is a rather arbitrary restriction that carves out a special rule for temperature among the other energies, and is just as subject to exploits as the alternative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:21:06-07:00","id":1538751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538749#post1538749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matter 2 restricts changes in state or temperature, but turning room temperature water into room temperature liquid Nitrogen is possible. Adding Forces 2 means the mage could change room temperature water into standard temperatures of liquid nitrogen. It might be Forces 3 but I think that's a HDYDT thing.<br /> <br /> Matter 3 takes off the restrictions of Matter 2 which I've generally read as allowing temperature changes appropriate to the new substance and state. Temperature may not be specifically mentioned, but there are a lot of stated abilities of Matter 3 that dramatically change the energy in the system, temperature is just the most obvious. So turning ambient gaseous nitrogen into cold liquid nitrogen with just Matter 3 should be possible.<br /> <br /> That said, it wouldn't be an unreasonable interpretation that Matter 3 still can't change temperature, though it is a rather arbitrary restriction that carves out a special rule for temperature among the other energies, and is just as subject to exploits as the alternative.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no such thing as room temperature liquid nitrogen, not unless you change the boiling point of nitrogen which is a matter 5 effect. And the books are very clear Matter 2 cannot change the temperature of the target.<br /> <br /> And this has been the case since second edition. In fact liquid nitrogen is specifically discussed in the write up of Matter in the core book<br /> <br /> Going by the same write up of 2e, you need Prime and Forces to heat up or cool down along with Matter 3 to change the state of an object. While Revised allows a combination of Forces and Matter 2 to change an object\u2019s state. But with Matter alone it seems restricted to Matter 5<br /> <br /> Mrev pg172<br /> M2e Pg206<br /> <br /> M20 does state a temporary change of state is possible with Matter 3. But that is more an extension of transmutation, steel to fog or water to glass, where temperature change is not essential for fog or glass to maintain its state<br /> <br /> To clarify I am not arguing how the game should be played at your table, just explaining that these rules are in fact written up quite clearly. If you don\u2019t think they make sense, do it the way that makes sense to you. I am only trying to explain why the rules provided make sense to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-17-2024, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:38:10-07:00","id":1538754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538751#post1538751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no such thing as room temperature liquid nitrogen, not unless you change the boiling point of nitrogen which is a matter 5 effect. And the books are very clear Matter 2 cannot change the temperature of the target.<br /> <br /> And this has been the case since second edition. In fact liquid nitrogen is specifically discussed in the write up of Matter in the core book<br /> <br /> Going by the same write up of 2e, you need Prime and Forces to heat up or cool down along with Matter 3 to change the state of an object. While Revised allows a combination of Forces and Matter 2 to change an object\u2019s state. But with Matter alone it seems restricted to Matter 5<br /> <br /> Mrev pg172<br /> M2e Pg206<br /> <br /> M20 does state a temporary change of state is possible with Matter 3. But that is more an extension of transmutation, steel to fog or water to glass, where temperature change is not essential for fog or glass to maintain its state<br /> <br /> To clarify I am not arguing how the game should be played at your table, just explaining that these rules are in fact written up quite clearly. If you don\u2019t think they make sense, do it the way that makes sense to you. I am only trying to explain why the rules provided make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats why Matter 2 and 3 should be switched. That way you can both controll the substance AND its state.<br /> As for temperature. Matter cant controll temperature but it can controll at what temperature the state of the object changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-17-2024, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:47:14-07:00","id":1538756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538754#post1538754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thats why Matter 2 and 3 should be switched. That way you can both controll the substance AND its state.<br /> As for temperature. Matter cant controll temperature but it can controll at what temperature the state of the object changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I already wrote why I do not believe Matter 2 and 3 can should be switched. So in the interest of not repeating myself I\u2019ll refer back to earlier in this thread for my reasoning. The summary is that changing a substance\u2019s material is far more subtle a change than changing it\u2019s shape, with Melt and Reform rote being a good example of how Matter 3 really is an increase on the capabilities of Matter 2<br /> <br /> and yes, Matter 5 can change what temperature and object\u2019s state changes. I don\u2019t believe this point was in dispute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T08:47:40-07:00","id":1538757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538751#post1538751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is no such thing as room temperature liquid nitrogen, not unless you change the boiling point of nitrogen which is a matter 5 effect. And the books are very clear Matter 2 cannot change the temperature of the target.<br /> <br /> And this has been the case since second edition. In fact liquid nitrogen is specifically discussed in the write up of Matter in the core book<br /> <br /> Going by the same write up of 2e, you need Prime and Forces to heat up or cool down along with Matter 3 to change the state of an object. While Revised allows a combination of Forces and Matter 2 to change an object\u2019s state.<br /> <br /> Mrev pg172<br /> M2e Pg206<br /> <br /> To clarify I am not arguing how the game should be played at your table, just explaining that these rules are in fact written up quite clearly. If you don\u2019t think they make sense, do it the way that makes sense to you. I am only trying to explain why the rules provided make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very presence of Prime in that example limits how much credence I\u2019m going to give 2nd edition when it comes to interpreting M20. It\u2019s clearly using a different line of reasoning. M20 doesn\u2019t need Prime for temperature changes.<br /> <br /> State changes are the explicit power of Matter 3 in M20 Whether or not that includes temperature changes is a matter of interpretation, but if we are getting far enough into the details to consider state diagrams I consider that a strong sign that it <i>does</i>. It means we are deep enough to be considering the enthalpies of fusion and vaporization and that state changes, even without temperature changes, take a surprising amount of energy.<br /> <br /> If Matter 3 can ignore that heat/energy requirement to change one physical property of Matter (state), we can easily ignore the same requirement to change another property (temperature).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:04:34-07:00","id":1538759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538757#post1538757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very presence of Prime in that example limits how much credence I\u2019m going to give 2nd edition when it comes to interpreting M20. It\u2019s clearly using a different line of reasoning. M20 doesn\u2019t need Prime for temperature changes.<br /> <br /> State changes are the explicit power of Matter 3 in M20 Whether or not that includes temperature changes is a matter of interpretation, but if we are getting far enough into the details to consider state diagrams I consider that a strong sign that it <i>does</i>. It means we are deep enough to be considering the enthalpies of fusion and vaporization and that state changes, even without temperature changes, take a surprising amount of energy.<br /> <br /> If Matter 3 can ignore that heat/energy requirement to change one physical property of Matter (state), we can easily ignore the same requirement to change another property (temperature).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Temperature is heat - a force not a quality of matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:16:53-07:00","id":1538761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538759#post1538759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Temperature is heat - a force not a quality of matter</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the same type of energy whether you are talking about state changes or temperature changes. I don't remember the exact numbers, but it takes roughly the same heat/energy to melt a block of ice as it does to take the resulting water from 0C to around 80C. If Matter 3 cannot change that energy in an object, it can't change states, which is one of its signature abilities.<br /> <br /> We don't have to go this far into the technical details of matter and energy, of course, but if we do this is what we have to consider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:17:12-07:00","id":1538762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538757#post1538757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very presence of Prime in that example limits how much credence I\u2019m going to give 2nd edition when it comes to interpreting M20. It\u2019s clearly using a different line of reasoning. M20 doesn\u2019t need Prime for temperature changes.<br /> <br /> State changes are the explicit power of Matter 3 in M20 Whether or not that includes temperature changes is a matter of interpretation, but if we are getting far enough into the details to consider state diagrams I consider that a strong sign that it <i>does</i>. It means we are deep enough to be considering the enthalpies of fusion and vaporization and that state changes, even without temperature changes, take a surprising amount of energy.<br /> <br /> If Matter 3 can ignore that heat/energy requirement to change one physical property of Matter (state), we can easily ignore the same requirement to change another property (temperature).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would say it is short sighted to throw out 2e when using it to contextualise the rulings of M20, especially since there is precious little written about what Matter is capable of doing in most of the 20th edition content. Especially Matter 4 and 5, which if taken RAW would leave one to interpret that these ranks of matter can\u2019t really do much without other spheres.<br /> <br /> the general trend across all editions, however, is Matter 2, 3, and 4 cannot create impossible substances without the aid of other spheres. You cannot cause wood to melt, you can\u2019t have solid smoke, and you can\u2019t have hot liquid nitrogen just by using Matter.<br /> <br /> the rank required to make impossible substances with Matter alone has always been Matter 5. Considering that M20 also say \u201cWith Mastery, the crafter can create substances that transcend the limitations of scientific possibility\u201c (M20 Pg 519), it is not hard to consider that this follows through for M20 too.<br /> <br /> in short, because the substance of hot liquid nitrogen transcends the limitations of scientific possibility, to create it is a Matter 5 effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:29:11-07:00","id":1538763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538762#post1538762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say it is short sighted to throw out 2e when using it to contextualise the rulings of M20, especially since there is precious little written about what Matter is capable of doing in most of the 20th edition content. Especially Matter 4 and 5, which if taken RAW would leave one to interpret that these ranks of matter can\u2019t really do much without other spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, but you yourself showed that previous editions are unhelpful here when you cited 2nd Ed and Revised handling things differently.<br /> <br /> When M20 is unclear it may help to consult previous editions, but that's only going to work when those editions 1) are themselves clear and consistent and 2) don't contradict M20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the general trend across all editions, however, is Matter 2, 3, and 4 cannot create impossible substances without the aid of other spheres. You cannot cause wood to melt, you can\u2019t have solid smoke, and you can\u2019t have hot liquid nitrogen just by using Matter.<br /> <br /> the rank required to make impossible substances with Matter alone has always been Matter 5. Considering that M20 also say \u201cWith Mastery, the crafter can create substances that transcend the limitations of scientific possibility\u201c (M20 Pg 519), it is not hard to consider that this follows through for M20 too. </div> </div> </div>That works to a point, but the writers are not always up to speed on what is actually impossible. For instance, in M20 Matter 3 can change density, which pretty quickly starts violating the properties of matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> in short, because the substance of hot liquid nitrogen transcends the limitations of scientific possibility, to create it is a Matter 5 effect. </div> </div> </div>And again, if we are considering the properties of nitrogen in that detail, there are a lot of other things we need to consider. It means Matter is doing more than it seems when it exercises its signature abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:34:26-07:00","id":1538764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538761#post1538761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's the same type of energy whether you are talking about state changes or temperature changes. I don't remember the exact numbers, but it takes roughly the same heat/energy to melt a block of ice as it does to take the resulting water from 0C to around 80C. If Matter 3 cannot change that energy in an object, it can't change states, which is one of its signature abilities.<br /> <br /> We don't have to go this far into the technical details of matter and energy, of course, but if we do this is what we have to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>You forget that state can be altered by preasure and properties of matter so it requires no &quot;energy&quot;<br /> <br /> The whole premise is bad. The fact that you can do similar things with different methods does not mean you can use all those methods. Matter allows shaping of matter thats it. It has nothing to do with temperature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-17-2024, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:43:24-07:00","id":1538765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538763#post1538763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly, but you yourself showed that previous editions are unhelpful here when you cited 2nd Ed and Revised handling things differently.<br /> <br /> When M20 is unclear it may help to consult previous editions, but that's only going to work when those editions 1) are themselves clear and consistent and 2) don't contradict M20.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That works to a point, but the writers are not always up to speed on what is actually impossible. For instance, in M20 Matter 3 can change density, which pretty quickly starts violating the properties of matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And again, if we are considering the properties of nitrogen in that detail, there are a lot of other things we need to consider. It means Matter is doing more than it seems when it exercises its signature abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter 3 has always been able to change an object\u2019s density, that\u2019s been consistent across every edition of the game.<br /> <br /> To clarify, when it states creating substances beyond the usual scientific limits, this is specifically talking about the end product.<br /> <br /> a dense rock being transformed in to a hollow rock does not create a substance that breaks scientific limits, both a dense rock and a hollow rock can exist quite happily in our reality.<br /> <br /> hot liquid nitrogen on the other hand, cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T09:58:44-07:00","id":1538766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538764#post1538764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You forget that state can be altered by pressure and properties of matter so it requires no &quot;energy&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>When players envision using Matter 3 to change water into ice, they are generally not considering pressure changes. They're envisioning turning water into ice and nothing else changing. Pressure is certainly a method some mages might use, but not most of them. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, if Matter 3 can change the properties of nitrogen so that it doesn't take energy to change state, it can change the properties of nitrogen so that it doesn't take energy to change temperature. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T10:03:48-07:00","id":1538767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538765#post1538765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matter 3 has always been able to change an object\u2019s density, that\u2019s been consistent across every edition of the game.<br /> <br /> To clarify, when it states creating substances beyond the usual scientific limits, this is specifically talking about the end product.<br /> <br /> a dense rock being transformed in to a hollow rock does not create a substance that breaks scientific limits, both a dense rock and a hollow rock can exist quite happily in our reality.<br /> <br /> hot liquid nitrogen on the other hand, cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's changing form. How about changing the density of water at room temperature and 1 atmosphere of pressure?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T10:42:44-07:00","id":1538769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538767#post1538767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's changing form. How about changing the density of water at room temperature and 1 atmosphere of pressure?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean changing the water\u2019s density to resemble sludge or syrup? Certainly possible with Matter 3. And the transmutation should be fine as long as effect is held. Though it will diffuse again <br /> <br /> you could even disperse the water in to a fine mist without changing the temperature too, though over time this water will condense.<br /> <br /> But if you wish to argue that such things are not possible, then you would only lead me to conclude it only possible at Matter 5, with density changes at Matter 3 being limited to solid objects, such as changing the strength of clothing by making the material more dense.<br /> <br /> for now I don\u2019t think this is the case, but I am open to being informed otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T11:31:39-07:00","id":1538772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538769#post1538769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean changing the water\u2019s density to resemble sludge or syrup? Certainly possible with Matter 3. And the transmutation should be fine as long as effect is held. Though it will diffuse again<br /> <br /> you could even disperse the water in to a fine mist without changing the temperature too, though over time this water will condense.<br /> <br /> But if you wish to argue that such things are not possible, then you would only lead me to conclude it only possible at Matter 5, with density changes at Matter 3 being limited to solid objects, such as changing the strength of clothing by making the material more dense.<br /> <br /> for now I don\u2019t think this is the case, but I am open to being informed otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. The most obvious use for Alter Density I can think of (and the first use I thought of for it) is altering the density of water to change what sinks or floats. Floatation is the first practical example of density I can remember from when I was a kid. If Alter Density can't do this, it is beyond misleading to call it Alter Density.<br /> <br /> Of course the specific gravity of water (or any liquid) is constant for a given temperature and pressure, so to actually alter the density of water involves changing the properties of water to something they cannot naturally be.<br /> <br /> My point is not that Alter Density should be Matter 5. My point is that Matter 3 explicitly has the ability to Alter Density, which means that Matter 3 is altering substances in impossible ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T12:07:45-07:00","id":1538773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538772#post1538772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. The most obvious use for Alter Density I can think of (and the first use I thought of for it) is altering the density of water to change what sinks or floats. Floatation is the first practical example of density I can remember from when I was a kid. If Alter Density can't do this, it is beyond misleading to call it Alter Density.<br /> <br /> Of course the specific gravity of water (or any liquid) is constant for a given temperature and pressure, so to actually alter the density of water involves changing the properties of water to something they cannot naturally be.<br /> <br /> My point is not that Alter Density should be Matter 5. My point is that Matter 3 explicitly has the ability to Alter Density, which means that Matter 3 is altering substances in impossible ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, you simply increase the amount of water compressed in to an area for a time, removing the natural trend of pressure for the while the effect is active.<br /> <br /> It would not be unlike transmuting a section of water into salt water.<br /> <br /> as Matter 3 is capable of breaking things apart and dispersing matter patterns, it stands to reason it can hold them together for a time. Though how difficult this would be will depend on the environment. In this way you could potentially condense nitrogen gas to a liquid form, but it would not hold for very long. The melting point of nitrogen is just far too low for this to be possible to do with Matter 3 at anything close to a sensible number of successes.<br /> <br /> so if you would like I can say \u201cyes, but you would likely need 200 successes before you could force nitrogen close enough together that a small amount can condense into a liquid at room temp for longer than a few seconds\u201d<br /> <br /> But I think it\u2019s a lot simpler to acknowledge where things leave the realm of feasibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T13:18:22-07:00","id":1538781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538773#post1538773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, you simply increase the amount of water compressed in to an area for a time, removing the natural trend of pressure for the while the effect is active.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most liquids, including water, are incompressible fluids and their density does not change much with pressure. The density of water at the lowest point of the ocean is almost the same as the density at sea level, 1025 kg/m^3.<br /> <br /> Changing the density of water to the point that a person cannot float in it is a significantly greater change of density.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would not be unlike transmuting a section of water into salt water. </div> </div> </div>That would work, but that would be replacing the water, not altering its density. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> as Matter 3 is capable of breaking things apart and dispersing matter patterns, it stands to reason it can hold them together for a time. Though how difficult this would be will depend on the environment. In this way you could potentially condense nitrogen gas to a liquid form, but it would not hold for very long. The melting point of nitrogen is just far too low for this to be possible to do with Matter 3 at anything close to a sensible number of successes.<br /> <br /> so if you would like I can say \u201cyes, but you would likely need 200 successes before you could force nitrogen close enough together that a small amount can condense into a liquid at room temp for longer than a few seconds\u201d<br /> <br /> But I think it\u2019s a lot simpler to acknowledge where things leave the realm of feasibility. </div> </div> </div>Neither one is scientifically feasible at all. Which is fine because Mage doesn't really have to be scientifically feasible. By rank 3, most spheres are breaking hard from what we know of the natural laws. <br /> <br /> We're not supposed to need this level of scientific rigor to interpret the rules. There's nothing wrong with bringing it in if we want to, especially when we want to work out some unintended consequences of an effect, but sooner or later (usually sooner) Mage is going to violate a basic principle and laugh wildly while doing it. <br /> <br /> In short, if you are going to get strict with impossible substances you will rapidly find most effects migrating to Matter 5. If we were seriously going to alter the abilities of the spheres to conform to natural law we would have to gut the entire system. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:14:53-07:00","id":1538786,"title":"","content":"What I take from all this, including the snippets from the books:<br /> <br /> 1- You need Matter 5 to make unobtanium and radiation. It doesn't say anything about any other special material, only radiation;<br /> <br /> 2- By the book, making a radioactive material is not a conjunctional effect, it is Matter 5, even if the reason is it being a Forces pattern;<br /> <br /> 3- There are materials that naturally: explode easily; burn spontaneously; have strong constructive magnetic fields; the list goes on. The book says you can make them out of any other material with Matter 2. A guy says you need a conjunctional Forces effect. Somehow only radiation needs Matter 5, though;<br /> <br /> 4- Earthly Foundations and the actual low-case science done in the setting apparently have nothing to do with anything anymore;<br /> <br /> 5- All the while, you can make a fucking Black Hole with Matter 3. Out of water, if you want.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a>, I understand your point, but it is exactly what I was talking of radiation being a special case because reasons. As a matter of fact, even Enriched Uranium don't surpass safe radiation levels easily by itself (it isn't deemed safe, but that's because it can be a problem when combined with background radiation and/or other sources of exposure).<br /> <br /> Atomic bombs don't need to be made of Enriched Uranium, and their complexity and number of successes would be a far better way to control things than making them Matter 5 arbitrarily. A Mage with Arete 3 has many, many ways to acquire and use an A Bomb without magicking it out of thin air, so there's no real balance involved.<br /> <br /> What actually happened is that radiation was a ghost on the collective imagination of authors that grew in the later half of the Cold War, and were already marked in Werewolf as special-bad-wrong. Despite its actual effects not being really all that more terrible than many other things we can do (specially in the game) with similar amounts of resources and persistence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":". 07-18-2024, 09:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:28:35-07:00","id":1538788,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a><br /> going to say this right now<br /> <br /> you can\u2019t make a black hole at matter 3<br /> <br /> Arguing \u201cbut density\u201d is just\u2026silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:29:36-07:00","id":1538789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538781#post1538781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most liquids, including water, are incompressible fluids and their density does not change much with pressure. The density of water at the lowest point of the ocean is almost the same as the density at sea level, 1025 kg/m^3.<br /> <br /> Changing the density of water to the point that a person cannot float in it is a significantly greater change of density.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That would work, but that would be replacing the water, not altering its density.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Neither one is scientifically feasible at all. Which is fine because Mage doesn't really have to be scientifically feasible. By rank 3, most spheres are breaking hard from what we know of the natural laws.<br /> <br /> We're not supposed to need this level of scientific rigor to interpret the rules. There's nothing wrong with bringing it in if we want to, especially when we want to work out some unintended consequences of an effect, but sooner or later (usually sooner) Mage is going to violate a basic principle and laugh wildly while doing it.<br /> <br /> In short, if you are going to get strict with impossible substances you will rapidly find most effects migrating to Matter 5. If we were seriously going to alter the abilities of the spheres to conform to natural law we would have to gut the entire system.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I almost turned a corner, but the comment on black holes got me to snap right back<br /> <br /> liquid nitrogen with Matter 3 is just too much for that level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:31:46-07:00","id":1538790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538788#post1538788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> is just\u2026silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>You use this &quot;argument&quot; a lot, usually missing the whole point of the thing you're trying to counter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:36:55-07:00","id":1538791,"title":"","content":"If I had been arguing for black holes, I'd understand. I wasn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T14:49:08-07:00","id":1538793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538790#post1538790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You use this &quot;argument&quot; a lot, usually missing the whole point of the thing you're trying to counter.</div> </div> </div> </div>What exactly is the point you wished to make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T17:14:36-07:00","id":1538801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538790#post1538790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You use this &quot;argument&quot; a lot, usually missing the whole point of the thing you're trying to counter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that you won't be able to create black holes with Matter 3 unless you get, I don't know, at least 1.000.000 successes. Something like that. The density of a black hole is pretty much insane. It's the kind that a full spoon of black hole cereal would weight more than planet Earth","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T18:05:21-07:00","id":1538804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538801#post1538801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that you won't be able to create black holes with Matter 3 unless you get, I don't know, at least 1.000.000 successes. Something like that. The density of a black hole is pretty much insane. It's the kind that a full spoon of black hole cereal would weight more than planet Earth</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with the generous calculation of each success <i>doubles</i> the density, it would take 20 successes to give water the density of a white dwarf star and almost 50 successes to reach the density of a neutron star. Actually getting enough successes to reach the density of a black hole would be impossible as they theoretically have infinite density.<br /> <br /> Technically, getting matter past the density of a neutron star would probably push it to collapse into a black hole on its own. However, also technically, anything past white dwarf is very exotic matter (no atomic structure) and would clearly be the domain of Matter 5. What I\u2019m saying is, if taking the density past white dwarf doesn\u2019t take Matter 5, taking it past neutron star isn\u2019t going to make a black hole.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T18:18:04-07:00","id":1538806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538804#post1538804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we go with the generous calculation of each success <i>doubles</i> the density, it would take 20 successes to give water the density of a white dwarf star and almost 50 successes to reach the density of a neutron star. Actually getting enough successes to reach the density of a black hole would be impossible as they theoretically have infinite density.</div> </div> </div> </div>Physicists don't like that thing of &quot;infinite&quot;. They say that when that happens or when you're dividing stuff by 0, it's just math being funny. They would answer that the density of a black hole is &quot;I dunno, but probably bigger than you and I could expect&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Technically, getting matter past the density of a neutron star would probably push it to collapse into a black hole on its own. However, also technically, anything past white dwarf is very exotic matter (no atomic structure) and would clearly be the domain of Matter 5. What I\u2019m saying is, if taking the density past white dwarf doesn\u2019t take Matter 5, taking it past neutron star isn\u2019t going to make a black hole. </div> </div> </div>I would say that White Dwarf density is already &quot;Unobitanium&quot; enough to merit it being under Matter 5 by itself... I mean, it's not like we see White Dwarf &quot;Compressium&quot; metals being dug out of mines everyday...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T18:26:22-07:00","id":1538807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538806#post1538806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Physicists don't like that thing of &quot;infinite&quot;. They say that when that happens or when you're dividing stuff by 0, it's just math being funny. They would answer that the density of a black hole is &quot;I dunno, but probably bigger than you and I could expect&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>. <br /> <br /> From a gaming perspective it doesn\u2019t matter if it requires infinite successes or only Graham\u2019s Number of successes. If it would take us longer than the expected lifespan of the universe to roll that high, it\u2019s unreachable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538806#post1538806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that White Dwarf density is already &quot;Unobitanium&quot; enough to merit it being under Matter 5 by itself... I mean, it's not like we see White Dwarf &quot;Compressium&quot; metals being dug out of mines everyday...</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but the changeover from atomic matter to whatever the technical term is is for neutron star material is such a clear and easy place to put that divider. It fits so well.<br /> <br /> Either way, though, we clearly cross into Matter 5 well before a black hole could form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-17T21:19:38-07:00","id":1538813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538807#post1538807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Either way, though, we clearly cross into Matter 5 well before a black hole could form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. Jupiter has a core made of &quot;metallic Hidrogen&quot; due to the massive gravity. I'd say that &quot;metallic Hidrogen&quot; is definitely Matter 5. And this is way way less than White Dwarf, let alone Neutron Star, and definitely nowhere comparable to black hole","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T00:08:42-07:00","id":1538818,"title":"","content":"Just for fun:<br /> <br /> The formula for the Schwarzschild Radius of a black hole is r = 2GM / c\u00b2<br /> G and c are constants. Density is implicit, with a smaller radius for a larger mass (M). That also means you need less mass the smaller your black hole is. For a micro-black hole with a Schwarzschild Radius of 0.1 mm you would still need the mass equivalent of the Moon or a large asteroid. So I guess you could make really, really tiny black holes with Matter 3 - which would evaporate in a few picoseconds, but hey.<br /> <br /> I think that Sphere levels all have and need implicit effects from other Spheres (or properties outside their scope) to function. A chorister who turns water to wine or lets it rain manna from heaven doesn't care about physical intricacies that prerequisite or accompany those effects. A hermetic might care about the temperature of liquid nitrogen, and I have no problem with Paradigm making some effects simpler or more difficult to achieve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T02:06:19-07:00","id":1538820,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m actually inclined to say that density here is, in praxtical terms, more a question of hardness for solids, i.e. how structurally solid something is. You\u2019re essentially compressing as much of it together as you can, but it will be within reason.<br /> <br /> for gases this will be a question of thickness, creating a dense fog vs a diffuse mist.<br /> <br /> for water I can see this as sort of like imposing a temporary change in local atmospheric pressure in a specific part of the water. The scale of which dependent on the magical feats table.<br /> <br /> as a point, I don\u2019t see pressure as a Forces pattern but more a consequence of how much matter is around, just as falling isn\u2019t a force, bur a consequence of gravity. You could increase or decrease pressure with Forces, but also just with Matter.<br /> <br /> But when quintessence gets involved, I\u2019d say that these sort of things get easily mitigated as a result of incorporating the essence of reality. The object simply manifests itself as though it had always been there, no displacement needs be considered.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I now realise why 2e suggested changing state required Prime 2 along with Forces. If you want to increase density while maintaining volume as the thing changes state, you may need to create more matter.<br /> <br /> this would certainly be necessary for Liquid Nitrogen.<br /> <br /> this would mean another application for homogenous objects though would also be to shrink them down or expand them. They would weigh the same amount of course, but would be a way to carry things in a more covert manner (complex matter patterns such as guns, machines, or buildings would probably require Matter 4)<br /> <br /> the black hole argument though\u2026I would say simply no. Especially if we consider that, in Mage, Forces patterns are distinct from Matter patterns.Gravity is a distinct thing not dependent on mass, gravity is only the thing that makes down the direction that it is. In fact you could replace the force with \u2018directionality\u2019 if it helps. For everything you are likely to create with Matter on earth, the difference is essentially non existence. On that note, making something more dense by magic does not affect how hot it is. In fact temperature is stated as specifically something that goes unaffected by Matter. So unless you apply Forces the matter pattern simply does not affect the forces patterns around it. Instead it might be affect by the forces patterns around it. Physics need not be considered.<br /> <br /> use of the spheres very much bypasses the impact the physics might otherwise expect.<br /> <br /> and I would be very reluctant to allow paradigms to change this, mainly because such a thing easily leads to paradigm specific sphere requirements such as the ever loathed Chi Healing rote which mixes up how Focus and Spheres interact in the first place.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-18-2024, 05:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T07:02:38-07:00","id":1538827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538820#post1538820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m actually inclined to say that density here is, in praxtical terms, more a question of hardness for solids, i.e. how structurally solid something is. You\u2019re essentially compressing as much of it together as you can, but it will be within reason.<br /> <br /> for gases this will be a question of thickness, creating a dense fog vs a diffuse mist.<br /> <br /> for water I can see this as sort of like imposing a temporary change in local atmospheric pressure in a specific part of the water. The scale of which dependent on the magical feats table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, changing atmospheric pressure does not change the density of liquid water. That's not a way it could work. Altering the density of water in any meaningful way involves changing its physical properties. That's not an unreasonable ability for Matter 3.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But when quintessence gets involved, I\u2019d say that these sort of things get easily mitigated as a result of incorporating the essence of reality. The object simply manifests itself as though it had always been there, no displacement needs be considered.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I now realise why 2e suggested changing state required Prime 2 along with Forces. If you want to increase density while maintaining volume as the thing changes state, you may need to create more matter. </div> </div> </div>Mage does not maintain conservation of mass or energy. Forces 2 can increase the size of a fire and accelerate objects and Life 2 can shrink and enlarge simple creatures and they don't need Prime to do this. In fact they can't use Prime to do this since it takes Forces 3 to convert free quintessence into energy and Life 3 to convert free quintessence into living substances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> use of the spheres very much bypasses the impact the physics might otherwise expect. </div> </div> </div>This is how I approach it. Matter is not particularly concerned with specific gravity or enthalpies or state diagrams. It can alter those things without much problem. It has to because by the time you reach Matter 3, most of the signature abilities of the rank are impossible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T17:53:54-07:00","id":1538881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538801#post1538801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that you won't be able to create black holes with Matter 3 unless you get, I don't know, at least 1.000.000 successes. Something like that. The density of a black hole is pretty much insane. It's the kind that a full spoon of black hole cereal would weight more than planet Earth</div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally infinite, it has no size as we understand it. We can talk about the boundaries, like the Event Horizon, but that's misleading.<br /> <br /> Of course the amount of successes needed would be staggering and prohibitive, that's the idea, see?<br /> <br /> The developers put radiation on Matter 5 because they thought it so special and unbalanced, but the game has already plenty of ways to A) do broken shit and B) keep them from happening casually through number of successes.<br /> <br /> You can make Black Holes with Matter 3, at least in theory. If you can compress/increase density, then you have all you need for the task. Or put another way, you can make objects that for all intents and purposes are so dense they should collapse into miniature stars and/or black holes. What that entails depends on paradigm, and the sheer number of successes is more than enough for that to not be tried casually.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, that's a thought exercise. Making an actual Black Hole should be done with Matter 5 and still take a shitton of successes. A micro black hole with the mass of a puddle of water would be of completely negligible size and duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T23:00:25-07:00","id":1538888,"title":"","content":"We keep talking like black holes would be an actual conesnsus phenomenon. All the while they exist only theoretically and only in space (umbra). We could assume black holes dont exist and those are just the parts of the labirynth around the abyss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-18T23:57:29-07:00","id":1538890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538888#post1538888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We keep talking like black holes would be an actual conesnsus phenomenon. All the while they exist only theoretically and only in space (umbra). We could assume black holes dont exist and those are just the parts of the labirynth around the abyss.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, only if you make that your WOD canon. They have been observed since the 70s, in 2022 we even got a nice radio image of one (the blurry <a href=\"https://eventhorizontelescope.org/blog/astronomers-reveal-first-image-black-hole-heart-our-galaxy\" target=\"_blank\">donut</a>).<br /> Yes, direct observation is impossible and no-one ever looked inside one, but when the theoretical data and observation match up consistently as they do I would consider it a consensus phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T00:10:21-07:00","id":1538891,"title":"","content":"I honestly don\u2019t know how we go from \u201cMatter 3 can be used to thickening your clothes to armor\u201d to \u201cI can create a singularity\u201d<br /> <br /> to me this just reeks of munchkin like behaviour.<br /> <br /> If you really really want this, I would say creating a singularity fits better as a Forces 5 effect","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-19-2024, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T00:24:11-07:00","id":1538892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538890#post1538890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, only if you make that your WOD canon. They have been observed since the 70s, in 2022 we even got a nice radio image of one (the blurry <a href=\"https://eventhorizontelescope.org/blog/astronomers-reveal-first-image-black-hole-heart-our-galaxy\" target=\"_blank\">donut</a>).<br /> Yes, direct observation is impossible and no-one ever looked inside one, but when the theoretical data and observation match up consistently as they do I would consider it a consensus phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>WOD cannon is that outer space = umbra, so its not a part of the consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T03:03:22-07:00","id":1538895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538891#post1538891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don\u2019t know how we go from \u201cMatter 3 can be used to thickening your clothes to armor\u201d to \u201cI can create a singularity\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anyone is seriously entertaining this, it's just a hyperbole example to illustrate how the literal wording of Sphere effects allow all kinds of extreme usecases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538892#post1538892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WOD cannon is that outer space = umbra, so its not a part of the consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is a difference between physical deep space and umbral deep space. The Void Engineers are just a bit confused about the matter. That's at least how I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T06:31:17-07:00","id":1538898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538891#post1538891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don\u2019t know how we go from \u201cMatter 3 can be used to thickening your clothes to armor\u201d to \u201cI can create a singularity\u201d<br /> <br /> to me this just reeks of munchkin like behaviour.<br /> <br /> If you really really want this, I would say creating a singularity fits better as a Forces 5 effect</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need to read what people are saying again, because the main two arguments are:<br /> <br /> 1) Making a black hole is at least Matter 5<br /> <br /> 2) Making a black hole is technically possible at Matter 3, but the number of successes needed is either infinite or so large as to be functionally impossible at the gaming table. So really, making a black hole is functionally Matter 5 or more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T10:26:30-07:00","id":1538906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538890#post1538890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, only if you make that your WOD canon. They have been observed since the 70s, in 2022 we even got a nice radio image of one (the blurry <a href=\"https://eventhorizontelescope.org/blog/astronomers-reveal-first-image-black-hole-heart-our-galaxy\" target=\"_blank\">donut</a>).<br /> Yes, direct observation is impossible and no-one ever looked inside one, but when the theoretical data and observation match up consistently as they do I would consider it a consensus phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that what he means is that &quot;sCience&quot; in WoD is just a conspiracy from a powerful secret cabal that rules the world. Black Holes can just as well be just a technocratic Psyop","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 07-19-2024, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-19T12:36:40-07:00","id":1538915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538906#post1538906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that what he means is that &quot;sCience&quot; in WoD is just a conspiracy from a powerful secret cabal that rules the world. Black Holes can just as well be just a technocratic Psyop</div> </div> </div> </div>But is it? Once the phenomenon starts to be consistently observed and predicted by unAwakened scientists with mundane equipment, it does seem to me it has become a part of the Consensus, even if it wasn't an Earthly Foundation at first.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Consensus is real. Being created by belief don't change it is real. Reality for a Sleeper works by its rules regardless.<br /> <br /> We also have the Earthly (and maybe Cosmic) Foundations to content with. There <b>is</b> an objective reality, even if it's hard as hell to test where does it begin and the Consensus start.<br /> <br /> How far the Foundations go is something for each ST to decide, but keep in mind that everything that may be just a Consensus thing, or a Paradigm thing, may also actually be a Foundation, which means it is objectively true.<br /> <br /> So do Black Holes actually exist? Is science real? Is there such a thing as Enriched Uranium? Well, while all of those may be fictions, you can't say for sure. You can't say it is defined as such in the setting.<br /> <br /> And the fact that Sleeper scientists and technicians work with such things regularly and in scale does seems to indicate they're already a part of the Consensus. Which goes back to the question of where they should be on the Matter rankings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T08:54:59-07:00","id":1538945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538915#post1538915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But is it? Once the phenomenon starts to be consistently observed and predicted by unAwakened scientists with mundane equipment, it does seem to me it has become a part of the Consensus, even if it wasn't an Earthly Foundation at first.<br /> <br /> Remember, the Consensus is real. Being created by belief don't change it is real. Reality for a Sleeper works by its rules regardless.<br /> <br /> We also have the Earthly (and maybe Cosmic) Foundations to content with. There <b>is</b> an objective reality, even if it's hard as hell to test where does it begin and the Consensus start.<br /> <br /> How far the Foundations go is something for each ST to decide, but keep in mind that everything that may be just a Consensus thing, or a Paradigm thing, may also actually be a Foundation, which means it is objectively true.<br /> <br /> So do Black Holes actually exist? Is science real? Is there such a thing as Enriched Uranium? Well, while all of those may be fictions, you can't say for sure. You can't say it is defined as such in the setting.<br /> <br /> And the fact that Sleeper scientists and technicians work with such things regularly and in scale does seems to indicate they're already a part of the Consensus. Which goes back to the question of where they should be on the Matter rankings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of this is contingent on the presence of unawakened scientists in the first place. Some could say that if one is a scientist in WoD, they are either a sleeper, meaning they would likely only to technician work or general dogs-body things, carrying out the experiments at the behest of others; sorcerers the technocracy refer to as extraordinary citizens, at which point they are simply using paths which are essentially procedure based wonders designed by the technocracy; or awakened technocrats, in which case all bets are off.<br /> <br /> We could extrapolate this further and say any cutting edge technology which has yet to become available to casual consumers is a form of technocratic sorcery, with the use by extraordinary citizens required to normalise the idea so that it can be accepted by the public not just as a form of linear magic, but as a simple way in which the world operates, becoming one with the consensus in a way that forgoes the need for belief entirely.<br /> <br /> How this would break down is like this. In the victorian era, using a microscope would absolutely be an act of magic which was slowly becoming a sorcery path, enabling anyone with the correct understanding to operate one. These days however, the concept of a microscope has become so widely accepted and the things one would see through it so certain that anyone who uses it would see what the consensus expects them to see. But if you went back to the dark ages with a microscope in hand, it simply would not work, no one would see anything through it unless you, as an awakened individual, prepared it for them as a way of enacting your will on to what they see, you would essentially be casting the spell for them.<br /> Any analysis these days which relies on genetic analysis, mass spectrometry, quantum physics, etc, all would be sphere magic with a few of these applications turned in to paths. PCR to determine the presence of viral DNA would be an example of a sorcery path, one which is only fairly recent, about 50 years ago it was full on sphere magic. <br /> <br /> Regarding the consensus being real, yes, it absolutely is. But only in so far as things done using the rules of the consensus. Doing awakened magic specifically subverts the consensus and creates a result that sits beyond what the consensus usually enables. The only difference between coincidental and vulgar magic in this regard is whether or not one could easily come up with an explanation that fit the consensus, but both types of effects are indeed subverting the consensus, even sensory magic subverts the consensus as to gain such insights you are generally looking beyond what people believe is possible to see. But the consensus is not the same thing as capital R Reality, at least not yet. The umbra, the periphery, spirits, and many other aspects of the other worlds exist regardless of sleeper consensus, but the consensus does affect how much they can interact with particular areas or people. Similarly there are elements of Reality which shine through beyond the consensus such as the nature of the Avatar, and actions of Paradox, the machinations of death, the permanence of quintessence, the existence of the mind, the fact that the consensus exists and that it can be manipulated. All of these elements persist regardless of popular belief, beyond the thing veil that the consensus provides.<br /> <br /> What the Earthly Foundations refers to are elements of reality which seem so shared across humanity that they are consistent across local beliefs. This includes the idea that everyone is drawn towards the ground, that night is dark and day is bright, that water flows from high to low and always in one direction, that time too flows in one direction, that death is not reversible, that spatial dimensions are conserved across places, etc. All of which are things that magic can subvert, but cannot be explained away by any belief system to the point of becoming coincidental, they are not, however, indicators of what is true Reality, more things that are so strongly embedded in to the daily existence of people that, as of the current era, no reality zone exists which would make such things possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T09:35:03-07:00","id":1538946,"title":"","content":"My point, which you seem to ignore, is that you can't simply say the setting works like that. You can say it <b>maybe </b>is like that, but not for certain.<br /> <br /> I personally think that regarding every single scientist in the world as a Technocrat (even &quot;just&quot; an Extraordinary Citizen) is ridiculous. More importantly, though, the setting doesn't say this, in any capacity. It is vague enough that you can go with this interpretation, but that's it.<br /> <br /> On the same way, Earthly Foundations have no explanation. They're not specially common beliefs, this is a you thing. They're aspects of reality that remain constant, and to each their own on explaining this away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-20T10:50:20-07:00","id":1538948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538946#post1538946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point, which you seem to ignore, is that you can't simply say the setting works like that. You can say it <b>maybe </b>is like that, but not for certain.<br /> <br /> I personally think that regarding every single scientist in the world as a Technocrat (even &quot;just&quot; an Extraordinary Citizen) is ridiculous. More importantly, though, the setting doesn't say this, in any capacity. It is vague enough that you can go with this interpretation, but that's it.<br /> <br /> On the same way, Earthly Foundations have no explanation. They're not specially common beliefs, this is a you thing. They're aspects of reality that remain constant, and to each their own on explaining this away.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I am approaching this is to present an outlook that lets things work together. Something that makes sense given what is presented. When people find an inconsistency or some way where the world doesn't seem to make sense, I like to imagine what would need to be the case for it to have made sense, and use that as the model going forwards. To be clear, you do not have to use this, and you especially shouldn't consider this the only option available. And I do encourage people throw away the aspects of the game that do not work for their own conception of the world. But for me, it's more fun to try and figure out what the implications of it are, and see if those assuage the feelings of it initially not making sense. I don't mind if you dislike what I come up with, that's fine. But I want to make sure I am at least being internally consistent, and explain how it is I come up with what I come up with, to show there is precedent for the ideas.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I'll now present how it is I came up with the answers<br /> Going off of what the book says, Earthly foundations is cited as &quot;The core reality zone&quot; M20 Pg 615. Which is why I say they aren't elements of capital R reality so much as elements that lay the foundation of belief for the consensus.<br /> <br /> <br /> M20 Sorcerer has this section on Page 16<br /> <br /> &quot;While most new Paths are created by hedge magicians themselves, mages can also create them. The process is arduous and resembles the creation of a Talisman (Mage 20p. 652-653,Book of Secrets p. 151-158). However, the \u201cTalisman\u201d in this instance has an ephemeral form: the concept of the Path. The mage must spend a similar amount of effort defining the Path as they would creating a Talisman\u2019s physical form, and then they must use Prime 5 to infuse this ephemeral Pattern with magick. The Technocratic Union particularly favors this method. They\u2019ve built a pipeline 2wherein Enlightened Scientists create fundamentally new science and then formalize it into Paths for Extraordinary Citizens. Those Citizens then bring the Path out into the world, making the new techniques first coincidental, and then mundane&quot;<br /> <br /> This pipeline is the process of introducing things to the consensus via scientific means. in the modern world, Scientific advancements come from 3 places, Univeristies, Research institutions, For-profit companies. All universities are under the control of the NWO, for-profit companies are under Syndicate control, and research institutions could be Progenitor lead, Iteration X lead, or any other convention depending on the focus, it is said as much within each conventions revised book, which also talks about the rise of the Extraoridnary Citizen as a great success for the union. Scientific development is very much in the hands of the technocracy. Where else would scientists be within the setting of Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T08:31:58-07:00","id":1538967,"title":"","content":"As for how the technocracy shapes consensus i always thought it like this<br /> 1. Technocracy experiments with their magic<br /> 2. They form a stable theory<br /> 3. They publish it and promote it as a theory<br /> 4. they wait untill someone (sleeper scientists) disproves it (making it a fail) or proves it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T09:15:00-07:00","id":1538973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538967#post1538967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for how the technocracy shapes consensus i always thought it like this<br /> 1. Technocracy experiments with their magic<br /> 2. They form a stable theory<br /> 3. They publish it and promote it as a theory<br /> 4. they wait untill someone (sleeper scientists) disproves it (making it a fail) or proves it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s part of the process, yes, but they also seed popular culture and consciousness with potential technology ideas to get them to catch on.<br /> <br /> Did you know that, in the real world, a big reason we have facial recognition technology is that it appeared in a Bond film and the CIA started wondering if it was possible.<br /> <br /> Now obviously the movie didn\u2019t make it possible in our world. In Mage, though, movies are a way of seeding the consensus. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T09:38:30-07:00","id":1538975,"title":"","content":"So essentially you have two options. Either most scientists are extraordinary citizens and are in fact working for or under the technocracy, knowingly or not<br /> <br /> or there are sleeper scientists, but their discoveries are simply technocratic creations which they have &quot;leaked&quot; to them, or perhaps published a few papers with the idea that these sleepers will 'discover' for themselves the things they already put in to place.<br /> <br /> But either way, all elements of science as we understand it are technocratic in origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-21-2024, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T10:05:59-07:00","id":1538976,"title":"","content":"Or not, because the Union is not actually in that much control in mid-to-late 2e and beyond.<br /> <br /> The Etherites, for example, claim responsibility for getting quantum mechanics into the Consensus behind the Technocracy's back. One of the advantages the Technocratic defector-factions have, is they know to play the Union's games. Even if they can't do things at the same scale, they can do targeted scientific discoveries as a form of guerrilla warfare Reality manipulation: one relatively small insertion designed specifically to waste decades of Technocratic efforts trying to deal with the fallout of the changes to its Time Table.<br /> <br /> If the Technocracy has complete control over sleeper science, then the non-Technocratic science focused factions have not function in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T11:26:19-07:00","id":1538978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538976#post1538976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the Technocracy has complete control over sleeper science, then the non-Technocratic science focused factions have not function in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn\u2019t necessarily the case. The etherites champion old science and outdated theories. They are the ones who maintain practices like homeopathy and seances, their method of science us as they say \u2018holistic\u2019 where they must test their theories not just in one practice, but in as many as they can. They are mystics through and through.<br /> <br /> and the VAs are equally mystical in their approach, exploiting the glitches in reality or trying to hack in to the universal source code. They actually have far more in common with the Hermetics than they do the technocrats.<br /> <br /> and every single tradition has its own brand of technomancers, none of which are any less mystical. Be it the ghost wheel society, the Alexandrian society, house Thig, members of the Li-Hai, etc. all of them make use of tech while maintaining mysticism.<br /> <br /> <br /> there\u2019s also the role that pop culture takes in the popularisation of the science elements made. Quantum physics was initially rejected by the scientific community, but as enough hype developed that it gained a foothold in the zeitgeist, the technocracy may have found reason to adapt it to their timetable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-21-2024, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T12:31:36-07:00","id":1538986,"title":"","content":"Since 2nd edition, and specially Guide to the Technocracy, it is said time and again that the Union doesn't have this level of complete control and micromanagement over all institutions. It is directly said that Sleeper scientists are a thing and do sometimes even make discoveries ahead of the Union.<br /> <br /> To say that all and every science is a direct product of the Technocratic Union isn't just a heavy claim, it has been directly against the canon setting for more than 25 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-21T23:32:18-07:00","id":1539004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538986#post1538986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since 2nd edition, and specially Guide to the Technocracy, it is said time and again that the Union doesn't have this level of complete control and micromanagement over all institutions. It is directly said that Sleeper scientists are a thing and do sometimes even make discoveries ahead of the Union.<br /> <br /> To say that all and every science is a direct product of the Technocratic Union isn't just a heavy claim, it has been directly against the canon setting for more than 25 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, then just look to the second option in regards to how scientific discovery is simply sleepers seeing what was set up by the crats or possibly other traditions.<br /> <br /> Though I will point out that all unawakened scientists doing actual science being extraordinary citizens is not predicated on technocrats being in absolute control. To be an extraordinary citizen all you need is to be practices in the crafts, in this case, advanced scientific procedures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-22-2024, 02:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T08:30:36-07:00","id":1539021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1538986#post1538986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since 2nd edition, and specially Guide to the Technocracy, it is said time and again that the Union doesn't have this level of complete control and micromanagement over all institutions. It is directly said that Sleeper scientists are a thing and do sometimes even make discoveries ahead of the Union.<br /> <br /> To say that all and every science is a direct product of the Technocratic Union isn't just a heavy claim, it has been directly against the canon setting for more than 25 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Union doesn't need that level of micromanagement over scientific production. They only need to guide the process. It is true that they don't have as much control as the Traditions themselves believe or as the Union would desire to have, but the truth is that this much control is not really needed; even if some flaws slip through the cracks, it ultimately serve their designs, and they just have to adjust.<br /> <br /> The NWO doesn't need to spy every single social media post in the world or falsify every single scientific paper; the Union has shaped society in such a way that the sleepers themselves do it for them. The social engineering of society is as big of an achievement as what the magazine &quot;Nature&quot; publishes. The sleeper institutions work on behalf of the Union even without any involvement from their shadow illuminati organization. The CIA, FBI, NSA, KGB, Stasi, governments, judicial systems, laws, all of those work perfectly well for their designs even if they don't meddle in those. And when they do need to meedle, all they need is a simple Entropy 1 effect to know where to push and in which direction in order to achieve maximum effect with minimum effort. That's how the Union achieves all it does and have a hand at the wheel, not by filling the car with goblins at every engine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T08:41:48-07:00","id":1539023,"title":"","content":"Getting back on topic thou, if &quot;Enriched Uranium&quot; was just a mythical hermetic &quot;Hellstonium&quot; material in middle ages but now is just a &quot;simple component&quot;, meaning that it would be Matter 5 in Medieval Period but now is just a simple substance due to Consensus, that has very large ramifications for the setting at large. It implies heavy consequences to how the Spheres work and a direct connection to the power of Consensus. This would mean not only that, if tomorrow the Union decides to push some other new &quot;Unobitanium&quot; into Consensus, it automatically becomes &quot;simple stuff&quot;. &quot;Adamantium&quot; (maybe rebranding it to &quot;Super Steel&quot;, just like we could claim that &quot;Enriched Uranium&quot; is just rebranded &quot;Hellstonium&quot;) could become exactly that.<br /> <br /> Take Kevlar for example. Is this a simple substance or is this some sort of &quot;Unobitanium&quot; that was pushed through Consensus?<br /> <br /> Would you have to use Matter 5 to create plastic in the medieval times? (And probably call it &quot;Divine Leather&quot;).<br /> <br /> But those considerations don't cease for Matter alone. It could extend to many other Spheres. What happens in a distant future Star Trek style where teleportation becomes mundane?<br /> <br /> What's more, this also have severe implications for Reality Zones. What if I create Adamantium inside of my Sanctum, where the local reality zone accepts it as a mundane material? Can I then be creating Adamantium in my Lab with mere Matter 2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T09:14:44-07:00","id":1539029,"title":"","content":"This a personal interpretation, but I consider this exact realization - that Spheres are limited only by convention and the way a Mage perceives reality - as step towards Ascension.<br /> In a way Marauders are very, very close to this, but they lack the consciousness and control of their own reality superseding conventional reality. It's one thing to read &quot;transcend reality&quot; in a book and be truly able to do it, which is the more difficult part. It requires the Mage to let go of some very fundamental concepts ingrained in their mind and personality.<br /> <br /> I think in-game, Spheres are crutches established by convention. Their architecture makes sense as something to learn and master, but the division and progression is ultimately arbitrary.<br /> <br /> So yes, I consider that scenario completely feasible. It becomes even clearer the longer you go back in time: consider a bronze age Mage vis-a-vis carbon steel. Meteor Swords. I don't think anyone would consider carbon steel a Matter 5 effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-22T16:35:20-07:00","id":1539064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539023#post1539023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It implies heavy consequences to how the Spheres work and a direct connection to the power of Consensus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why, whatever flaws the rules have in phrasing, the books don't actually endorse this, it's theory crafting from this thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take Kevlar for example. Is this a simple substance or is this some sort of &quot;Unobitanium&quot; that was pushed through Consensus? </div> </div> </div>What properties does Kevlar have that would have ever qualified it as some sort of Unobtanium? Polymer sciences weren't nearly as advanced, but it's not like the concepts involved would be hard to explain to past humans. Kevlar is just a synthetic material instead of a naturally sourced material. &quot;If you carefully mix this thing, and that thing just right, and then dry it, it turns into fluffy fibers you can then spin into threads instead of gathering wool, processing flax, or harvesting loose silk.&quot;<br /> <br /> Seriously. Look at a flax plant. If people thousands of years ago were fine with the idea that you could turn that in to linen, which can be everything from a fine light handkerchief to body armor if used correctly, how is Kevlar supposed to do anything that qualifies as Matter 5?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would you have to use Matter 5 to create plastic in the medieval times? (And probably call it &quot;Divine Leather&quot;). </div> </div> </div>They had plastics in Medieval times. European and Asian culture learned how to form early natural plastics from purifying polymer chains derived from keratin via animal horns. Shellac was also something we know was in use earlier. The first recognized natural plastic processed by humans was early rubber over 3600 years ago. Humans are also very used to the discovery of a new material leading to a lot of experimentation in what uses it could have or better ways to make it. Resins of various sorts were used since pre-history for a huge number of applications we use synthetic plastics for now.<br /> <br /> The massive revolution in plastics in the Industrial areas was in synthetic plastics and thus the ability to customize polymer chains for specific properties. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What happens in a distant future Star Trek style where teleportation becomes mundane? </div> </div> </div>See this is why Matter is written poorly. And theory-crafting in consensus based Sphere ranks for Matter effects doesn't actually make the game better.<br /> <br /> The Spheres necessary to teleport don't change if a Sleeper usable teleporter is invented. Teleportation just becomes coincidental (or at least much easier to do coincidentally).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T04:14:57-07:00","id":1539095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539064#post1539064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See this is why Matter is written poorly. And theory-crafting in consensus based Sphere ranks for Matter effects doesn't actually make the game better.<br /> <br /> The Spheres necessary to teleport don't change if a Sleeper usable teleporter is invented. Teleportation just becomes coincidental (or at least much easier to do coincidentally).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the Spheres aren't tied directly to Consensus, but recursively by the Mage's perception of possibilities that reflect the baseline of progress of the status quo. That is, the factor that limits some Sphere powers is (subconsciously) the Mages themselves.<br /> Spheres are evidently not the only way to work Magick. They are a system designed to make Magick easier to comprehend by categorization, but nothing prevents a Mage from using a different system to do the same thing (ie alternative Spheres, or Pillars, etc). That does of course not remove the need for a certain proficiency to pull them off, and I agree that the main difference would be in how vulgar an effect would be considered.<br /> <br /> From a game perspective, I absolutely agree with you that introducing a Sphere system that reflects this would make them catastrophically complex and would be detrimental to the game. On a meta level however I would have no problem reflecting progress by differentiating what a medieval Mage or a contemporary Mage would consider possible with certain Sphere levels. It's not like working Magick is a static thing that doesn't change over time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T14:49:04-07:00","id":1539113,"title":"","content":"The thing is, a Mage <i><b>always </b></i>believes what they do is possible. From the character standpoint, the distinction between Matter 2 and Matter 5 is the level of knowledge and skill necessary to synthesize the material, not if it is a real and naturally possible substance. It <b>is</b>, by definition.<br /> <br /> And for medieval Mages? Nothing in the game says they can't use Matter 2 to obtain modern materials. And just as modern Mages can use Matter 2 to obtain substances that are very hard to synthesize by mundane means, so could medieval Mages use it to obtain substances that were too hard to get for any regular use back them.<br /> <br /> Now, surely there could be times when a medieval Mage would have used Matter 5 to synthesize something we see as mundane now. But that would be less due to the Mage not trying it at Matter 2 than it not being possible, and it would be useful anyway, as Matter 5 would give him finer control over the result's properties.<br /> <br /> The whole thing of distinguishing Matter between &quot;real&quot; and &quot;fantastical&quot; materials is bad writing as it actually makes the power of the Sphere very dependent on how much the player knows material sciences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T00:26:56-07:00","id":1539131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539113#post1539113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, a Mage <i><b>always </b></i>believes what they do is possible. From the character standpoint, the distinction between Matter 2 and Matter 5 is the level of knowledge and skill necessary to synthesize the material, not if it is a real and naturally possible substance. It <b>is</b>, by definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I wasn't trying to argue that. Let me rephrase: I believe there is a difference in the perceived difficulty of an effect for the Mage that depends on how established a mundane solution for the effect is, because it is a lot easier to conceive of something in the first place if you follow an existing example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539113#post1539113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And for medieval Mages? Nothing in the game says they can't use Matter 2 to obtain modern materials. And just as modern Mages can use Matter 2 to obtain substances that are very hard to synthesize by mundane means, so could medieval Mages use it to obtain substances that were too hard to get for any regular use back them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, and in most cases it would be irrelevant anyways because a medieval Mage wouldn't use Matter 2 to create tungsten carbide because they would have no clue that is something that exists, they would use the effect to make 'ye harde metal'.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539113#post1539113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNow, surely there could be times when a medieval Mage would have used Matter 5 to synthesize something we see as mundane now. But that would be less due to the Mage not trying it at Matter 2 than it not being possible, and it would be useful anyway, as Matter 5 would give him finer control over the result's properties.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's closer to what I mean, with the difference that Matter 2 wouldn't be an actual option because said Mage would consider the properties of the result too exotic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539113#post1539113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThe whole thing of distinguishing Matter between &quot;real&quot; and &quot;fantastical&quot; materials is bad writing as it actually makes the power of the Sphere very dependent on how much the player knows material sciences.</div> </div> </div> </div>No disagreement there. I have to admit though that I would struggle to write down the Matter Sphere levels as intended other than make it an ST decision on what goes into Matter 2 or Matter 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T01:24:35-07:00","id":1539133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539113#post1539113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, a Mage <i><b>always </b></i>believes what they do is possible. From the character standpoint, the distinction between Matter 2 and Matter 5 is the level of knowledge and skill necessary to synthesize the material, not if it is a real and naturally possible substance. It <b>is</b>, by definition.<br /> <br /> And for medieval Mages? Nothing in the game says they can't use Matter 2 to obtain modern materials. And just as modern Mages can use Matter 2 to obtain substances that are very hard to synthesize by mundane means, so could medieval Mages use it to obtain substances that were too hard to get for any regular use back them.<br /> <br /> Now, surely there could be times when a medieval Mage would have used Matter 5 to synthesize something we see as mundane now. But that would be less due to the Mage not trying it at Matter 2 than it not being possible, and it would be useful anyway, as Matter 5 would give him finer control over the result's properties.<br /> <br /> The whole thing of distinguishing Matter between &quot;real&quot; and &quot;fantastical&quot; materials is bad writing as it actually makes the power of the Sphere very dependent on how much the player knows material sciences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Games that encourage learning are a good thing.<br /> <br /> I would argue that the consensus still decides what is more comlex to do (higher sphere lvl) and what is easy. So in medieval times plastic would be complex (5) and now in modern times it is easy (2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T02:38:09-07:00","id":1539134,"title":"","content":"Except, as I just pointed out, humans were producing plastics over 3500 years ago, and plastics were in regular production during Medieval times. There weren't as good as modern plastics, but lots of material sciences have advanced drastically based on a number of factors. You're putting making bouncy balls out of the sap of rubber plants into the same category as anti-gravity rocks.<br /> <br /> The problem is that no other Sphere really works this way. The fact that statistics and probability fields of math are far more advanced now than a thousand years ago might influence a bit of coincidental vs. not with Entropy, but there's nothing that changes what level a given manipulation of the odds of something happening is. Forces does not care if I'm manipulating a magnetic field generated by a lodestone or an electromagnet. Life does care if an species has gone extinct when it comes to what levels of Life are needed to manipulate or reproduce something.<br /> <br /> There's also a big difference between a game that encourages learning, and a game that encourages collecting factoids to manipulate the game in their favor. Having an engrossing game of Mage that inspires you to go study a given subject after the session is over is fun. Having a session drag on because one player keeps going, &quot;Well actually...&quot; is not fun. It's less fun when that turns into how to push the ST around by multiple people. And it's even less fun when your ST cancels the game because they're tired of people trying to game the letter of the rules instead of just enjoying the spirit of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T07:50:05-07:00","id":1539143,"title":"","content":"<br /> I've always thought the &quot;Well, actually...&quot; part was part of the fun of Mage, to be honest. But mileage does vary.<br /> <br /> My hard and fast rule for something like matter has always been &quot;would your character know that?&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit, I don't know much about medieval plastics. But if my player knows about it and can convince me that his character would have likely learned about it or encountered it at some point, then I'd be fine with considering that &quot;Matter 2&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the player (Edited: I had meant to say &quot;character&quot; here. Not &quot;player&quot;.) has never heard of plastic or encountered/observed it, and wants to create a material with the same qualities as plastic, then I would consider it Matter 5, because he's basically inventing it from scratch. The fact that it has the same qualities as something that already exists in the world is not really relevant to me, since for HIM, it's a brand new invention. (If he ends up encountering real plastic later, then using the real material would be Matter 2, in my opinion.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-24-2024, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T12:22:20-07:00","id":1539159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539143#post1539143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought the &quot;Well, actually...&quot; part was part of the fun of Mage, to be honest. But mileage does vary.<br /> <br /> My hard and fast rule for something like matter has always been &quot;would your character know that?&quot;<br /> <br /> I admit, I don't know much about medieval plastics. But if my player knows about it and can convince me that his character would have likely learned about it or encountered it at some point, then I'd be fine with considering that &quot;Matter 2&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the player has never heard of plastic or encountered/observed it, and wants to create a material with the same qualities as plastic, then I would consider it Matter 5, because he's basically inventing it from scratch. The fact that it has the same qualities as something that already exists in the world is not really relevant to me, since for HIM, it's a brand new invention. (If he ends up encountering real plastic later, then using the real material would be Matter 2, in my opinion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, that's something to handle with skill rolls or magical research or some other paradigm related thing, not magic rank. Not a lot of modern materials even approach impossible or exotic, so there's no real issue with someone of a previous era being able to make them.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, when I think of Matter 5 materials I think of things that are really strange or impossible, like rocks that selectively pass through each other or metals that magnetically attract chickens (and only chickens). It's not for things that are &quot;Like X, but more...&quot; (like steel but harder, like plastic but more malleable, etc.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T14:11:45-07:00","id":1539163,"title":"","content":"I think that Matter 5 should be the stuff of &quot;impossible&quot;. Not just some &quot;exotic&quot; thing like carbon fiber or tungsten. It's more in the level of &quot;indestructible&quot; adamantium that could be thrown inside the Sun and be fine, or some Vibranium bs that doesn't abide to laws of physics. Not just &quot;simply&quot; some &quot;extra hard steel&quot;, but rather the mithril, orichalcum and similar nonsense, with properties like being incorporeal towards certain other materials, materials with 0 mass or some other type of shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T16:51:37-07:00","id":1539175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539143#post1539143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit, I don't know much about medieval plastics. But if my player knows about it and can convince me that his character would have likely learned about it or encountered it at some point, then I'd be fine with considering that &quot;Matter 2&quot;.<br /> <br /> If the player has never heard of plastic or encountered/observed it, and wants to create a material with the same qualities as plastic, then I would consider it Matter 5, because he's basically inventing it from scratch. The fact that it has the same qualities as something that already exists in the world is not really relevant to me, since for HIM, it's a brand new invention. (If he ends up encountering real plastic later, then using the real material would be Matter 2, in my opinion.)</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to the posts above...<br /> <br /> The character, not the player, is the one that needs to know things for them to happen in game.<br /> <br /> And again, it runs into &quot;No other Sphere works this way.&quot; Rubber plants aren't Life 4/5 to people that have never seen a rubber plant before to know it's sap's special qualities are natural. If a mage knows nothing about rubber plants, then they're not going know how to make one with Life and Prime. The idea that Matter ranks depend on player knowledge is just... not how the game is constructed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T17:09:38-07:00","id":1539176,"title":"","content":"I did misspeak there. I meant to say if the &quot;character&quot; had never heard of plastic. Not the player. I tend to assume most modern players have heard of plastic. I will edit accordingly.<br /> <br /> I've never agreed with the idea that a character is limited by player skills or knowledge. (A roll would be fine for that kind of thing, IMO, unless it's something so ubiquitous that it's not realistic for a character to never encounter it - i.e. plastic in the modern age.) The only issue, of course, is if neither player or storyteller realizes plastic was available in the middle ages, then it would likely not come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-24-2024, 08:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T18:41:50-07:00","id":1539179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539131#post1539131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's closer to what I mean, with the difference that Matter 2 wouldn't be an actual option because said Mage would consider the properties of the result too exotic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> The Mage already believes this material is possible. At most they would need an Ability roll to come up with the theoretical framework they need within their paradigm to create the material.<br /> <br /> A Mage that thinks this material can't exist is already incapable of making it with any rank of the Sphere.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that then we start to not only make the power of the Sphere depend on the player's knowledge of materials, it also starts to depend on knowledge of History of materials <br /> <br /> By the way: most modern materials have been known for a hell of a lot of time. What changed with modern technology is our ability to produce them reliably, at a low cost and the uses we can put them to. But even for the materials that are really new, why they should be a higher Sphere rank to create?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539131#post1539131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No disagreement there. I have to admit though that I would struggle to write down the Matter Sphere levels as intended other than make it an ST decision on what goes into Matter 2 or Matter 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the problem, at least this specific problem, is that it seems intuitive to read &quot;possible&quot; as &quot;something the character knows to be possible&quot;. After all, in most of the game we have to consider the character's knowledge and beliefs. But that's not how a Sphere rank work. In Matter, &quot;possible&quot; means &quot;possible&quot;, as simple as that (plus radiation shenanigans).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T03:02:30-07:00","id":1539192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539179#post1539179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By the way: most modern materials have been known for a hell of a lot of time. What changed with modern technology is our ability to produce them reliably, at a low cost and the uses we can put them to. But even for the materials that are really new, why they should be a higher Sphere rank to create?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth pointing out that in Mage, much of what we take for granted as human history is a semi-fabrication designed by the technocracy to cover up any existance of magic.<br /> <br /> so back in the dark ages we may have genuinely have things like dragonstone and starlight steel which were simply explained away as geological phenomena or strange alloys. For example Moonstone would have originally been stones which literally reflected aspects of the moon, but are now just reclassified as a form if silicate. Of Electrum which acted as natural wonders, enabling those who used it psychic capabilities, reclassified as simply an alloy of gold and silver, the psychic powers they contained reduced to little more than mystic beliefs.<br /> <br /> What they describe as simply unenlightened men misunderstanding uranium deposits might actually be a cursed agar stone which causes the blight of entropy on all those who touch it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T04:16:17-07:00","id":1539193,"title":"","content":"Correction: what we take for granted as <b>pre-history</b> is a semi-fabricated construct. By the time humans started to for historical records, history became far more solidified. There is a big difference between Reality Zones where differing magical principles governed local reality, and the growing power of Consensus. For most of the High Mythic Age most mages didn't even consider the idea of reality being subjective and mutable by Sleeper beliefs Magic worked based on a mage's personal beliefs. In the High Mythic Age traveling didn't put your magical works at risk; because everywhere was a Reality Zone where magic of multiple forms was possible. It was only after the Order of Reason discovered the power of manipulating Reality Zones did the setting see a wide-spread fracturing of magic and history that would necessitate the Technocracy to try to cultivate a since stable history. And even that had to account for all the deeply rooted aspects of history that humans already had in their brains.<br /> <br /> Electrum has always been a relatively simply alloy. What the Union aimed to surpess was any practice that treated it as potentially more than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T04:56:11-07:00","id":1539195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539179#post1539179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?<br /> <br /> The Mage already believes this material is possible. At most they would need an Ability roll to come up with the theoretical framework they need within their paradigm to create the material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because to me, if a Mage <i>thinks </i>they can not achieve something at a certain level, it means that they literally <i>can't</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539179#post1539179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Mage that thinks this material can't exist is already incapable of making it with any rank of the Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean a categorical exclusion, but rather &quot;I can't possibly create this at my level of knowledge, I need to get more proficient.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539179#post1539179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that then we start to not only make the power of the Sphere depend on the player's knowledge of materials, it also starts to depend on knowledge of History of materials</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that would just be meta-gaming. My point is that a <i>character </i>may have a different perception of what qualities count as exotic enough that it requires Matter 5 (or more generally, a higher level), and that their perception would be informed by the times and circumstances they live in.<br /> <br /> Maybe a silly example, but:<br /> <br /> Xochitl was born and raised on an island near the equator. She has seen rock turn to lava, wood to smoke, and clouds to rain. With Matter 3, she was able to extrapolate on that and turn wood liquid and water solid. However, due to her circumstances, she has never seen ice or snow, or even knows those exist. When she turns water solid, it is a literal solid block of water, not ice. One day a visitor from the mountains tells her about that white and cold powder that disappears if it warms up, but is kinda sticky and looks like small flowers when it falls from the sky.<br /> There is a chance that Xochitl can make the connection that this is just a special state of water, but more likely to her it is a very weird substance with strange properties that is beyond what she can do with Matter 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-25-2024, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T06:08:42-07:00","id":1539200,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a> <br /> I would not think liquid wood would be possible at Matter 3. That would almost certainly be a Matter 5 thing.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think being unaware that wood can\u2019t melt would not change the fact that mastery is required for this. Reality zones change what effects would be accepted, not necessarily the level at which they can be performed.<br /> <br /> they could turn the wood into water at matter 3, that would be fine and fits in with their understanding of how matter functions, though I think the concept of \u2018solid water\u2019 would be beyond them, since water is fundamentally not that. They may not even be able to produce ice as they have no concept of ice.<br /> <br /> to that point, making solid water (not ice) as in a solid cube of liquid water that you can pick up like a Minecraft block would absolutely be Matter 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T06:58:54-07:00","id":1539204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539195#post1539195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because to me, if a Mage <i>thinks </i>they can not achieve something at a certain level, it means that they literally <i>can't</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the sphere system changing though. It's changing what the mage will actually cast. A basic locked flight spell (Forces 2/Life 2) and a spell that gives someone wings and lets them fly (Life 3(4)/Forces 2) are two different effects. Some mages may not have a paradigm that allows flight without wings, so they won't cast the former version. The system didn't change, they just use a more complicated effect.<br /> <br /> Turning water to ice is Matter 3. It's still Matter 3 even if the mage doesn't know about ice, they just won't cast the spell. Instead your hypothetical mage is casting a different Matter 3 spell, one that transmutes water into a solid that shares a lot of other properties with liquid water but is actually a type of crystal or stone.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T08:01:36-07:00","id":1539210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539204#post1539204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the sphere system changing though. It's changing what the mage will actually cast. A basic locked flight spell (Forces 2/Life 2) and a spell that gives someone wings and lets them fly (Life 3(4)/Forces 2) are two different effects. Some mages may not have a paradigm that allows flight without wings, so they won't cast the former version. The system didn't change, they just use a more complicated effect.<br /> <br /> Turning water to ice is Matter 3. It's still Matter 3 even if the mage doesn't know about ice, they just won't cast the spell. Instead your hypothetical mage is casting a different Matter 3 spell, one that transmutes water into a solid that shares a lot of other properties with liquid water but is actually a type of crystal or stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually what I have been trying to say, but never thought of formulating it that way. Thank you<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539200#post1539200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would not think liquid wood would be possible at Matter 3. That would almost certainly be a Matter 5 thing.<br /> <br /> to that point, making solid water (not ice) as in a solid cube of liquid water that you can pick up like a Minecraft block would absolutely be Matter 5</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Yeah, it's far more likely that both turn into 'something' that resembles Xochitl's idea of liquid wood or solid water, rather than the actual thing. It was a flawed attempt to illustrate how she is able to utilize Matter 3 for something she doesn't know, but believes to be possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T08:23:24-07:00","id":1539212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539200#post1539200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27477_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27477\" data-vbnamecard=\"27477\">voidshaper</a><br /> I would not think liquid wood would be possible at Matter 3. That would almost certainly be a Matter 5 thing.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think being unaware that wood can\u2019t melt would not change the fact that mastery is required for this. Reality zones change what effects would be accepted, not necessarily the level at which they can be performed.<br /> <br /> they could turn the wood into water at matter 3, that would be fine and fits in with their understanding of how matter functions, though I think the concept of \u2018solid water\u2019 would be beyond them, since water is fundamentally not that. They may not even be able to produce ice as they have no concept of ice.<br /> <br /> to that point, making solid water (not ice) as in a solid cube of liquid water that you can pick up like a Minecraft block would absolutely be Matter 5</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing wood state to liquid is literaly Matter 3 as described","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T11:21:22-07:00","id":1539229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539212#post1539212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Changing wood state to liquid is literaly Matter 3 as described</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Matter 3 as described is changing wood in to water, not making wood melt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T11:35:37-07:00","id":1539230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539229#post1539229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Matter 3 as described is changing wood in to water, not making wood melt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its described as changing the state (liquid, stable, gas, plasma) changing the substance is matter 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T11:56:25-07:00","id":1539235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539229#post1539229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Matter 3 as described is changing wood in to water, not making wood melt.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539230#post1539230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its described as changing the state (liquid, stable, gas, plasma) changing the substance is matter 2</div> </div> </div> </div>What Matter 3 can do to wood is not stated directly. Matter 2 says it can change one substance into another as long as it doesn't change shape, temperature, or state. Matter 3 directly says it can change shape and state, but then gives examples of state changes that are both state and substance changes. Not water into ice, but water into glass. Not steel into gaseous steel but steel into fog. <br /> <br /> It never really describes an unusual substance and shape, so there's some ambiguity. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T12:01:11-07:00","id":1539236,"title":"","content":"There also seems to be a pretty big level of forgetting that Matter 1 exists. Even if someone has never seen natural forms of H20 in a solid state, they can easily use Matter 1 to observe what happens when liquids transitions to solids, and extrapolate. They can watch, whatever their Focus and how it colors these observations, what happens when solids melt, liquids freeze, and so on. Again frame it however you want in terms of Focus, but if you've watched water boil, wood carbonize, dew and condensation form on leaves, and all of that with Matter 1? Figuring it out for materials that aren't naturally in your environment is not hard. Humans figured this stuff out in our world without magic, and humans in the WoD are not inherently less intelligent or curious about how basic things in their surroundings work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T14:25:41-07:00","id":1539248,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting thought. What would a mage observe with matter 1 when water freezes? The actual substance isn't really changing. It's still H2O. The properties that do change are the temperature (which is an outside force acting upon it), or the interaction of its atoms and molecules, which would also, IMO, be more of a Forces thing than a Matter thing.<br /> <br /> My own thought is that the mage would get a snapshot of the water as it exists in the state of being water, and water as it exists in the state of being ice. They would be able to tell that, fundamentally, it's the same thing. But what would they observe about the process itself?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":".  changing a zero to an O. Sorry. 07-25-2024, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T14:58:53-07:00","id":1539253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539230#post1539230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its described as changing the state (liquid, stable, gas, plasma) changing the substance is matter 2</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;At this Rank (matter 3), the mage can alter the shape of materials in whatever ways she desires, and she can temporarily transform their essential state into a different one \u2013 steel, for example, into fog or water into glass.&quot; M20 Pg 518<br /> <br /> You only need to read the entry to see the examples are of transmutation that allows the changing of state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:11:12-07:00","id":1539255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539236#post1539236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There also seems to be a pretty big level of forgetting that Matter 1 exists. Even if someone has never seen natural forms of H20 in a solid state, they can easily use Matter 1 to observe what happens when liquids transitions to solids, and extrapolate. They can watch, whatever their Focus and how it colors these observations, what happens when solids melt, liquids freeze, and so on. Again frame it however you want in terms of Focus, but if you've watched water boil, wood carbonize, dew and condensation form on leaves, and all of that with Matter 1? Figuring it out for materials that aren't naturally in your environment is not hard. Humans figured this stuff out in our world without magic, and humans in the WoD are not inherently less intelligent or curious about how basic things in their surroundings work.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good point. If you allow &quot;What Sphere Level (or combination) would I need for Matter effect X?&quot; as a magically gained insight, that would resolve a lot of the conflicts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539248#post1539248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting thought. What would a mage observe with matter 1 when water freezes? The actual substance isn't really changing. It's still H20. The properties that do change are the temperature (which is an outside force acting upon it), or the interaction of its atoms and molecules, which would also, IMO, be more of a Forces thing than a Matter thing.<br /> <br /> My own thought is that the mage would get a snapshot of the water as it exists in the state of being water, and water as it exists in the state of being ice. They would be able to tell that, fundamentally, it's the same thing. But what would they observe about the process itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Matter 1 works like an electron microscope where you can actually observe molecules or atoms. Maybe for a Technocrat whose Focus is close to Consensus, but for most Tradition Mages I would imagine the insight is more abstracted. Like Kekul\u00e9 imagining an Ouroboros for the benzene ring.<br /> For my hypothetical mage, it could be something like a vision of a group dance where the dancers form patterns as an analogy for forming snow crystals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T15:59:14-07:00","id":1539261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539195#post1539195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, that would just be meta-gaming.</div> </div> </div> </div>What!?<br /> <br /> Knowing that a material exists and that it would be relatively common knowledge in the 12th century is meta-gaming?<br /> <br /> I'm talking about that precisely because the way to avoid meta-gaming would be to know history.<br /> <br /> Mages change reality and push it's limits, all the time. They had always been the ones to do the impossible, at any level of mastery they have.<br /> <br /> They've been exploring other planets way before Sleepers could decide if the Earth moves.<br /> <br /> A Mage with Matter 2 has pondered about this whole aspect of reality, through magic and preternatural insight, enough to transmute clay into diamonds.<br /> <br /> How's it that they can only create a material if the ST is convinced that people back in the day knew about this material (an ST that may be wrong in their assumptions)?<br /> <br /> Oh, and the example is more than a little racist. A lot of real people live in equatorial islands, this level of ignorance is not how someone is just because they're born on the equator and/or in an island.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a>, the problem is that you focus on showing how we can use a very strict interpretation of the setting to make all the inconsistencies solve themselves, and fail to grasp that the setting is open to interpretation, but the rules fall apart (to a degree) when taken seriously under other perfectly valid interpretations.<br /> <br /> Every paradigm should be supported without much of a problem. You insists that the problem don't exist because those paradigms are just wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T16:12:33-07:00","id":1539262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539255#post1539255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Matter 1 works like an electron microscope where you can actually observe molecules or atoms. Maybe for a Technocrat whose Focus is close to Consensus, but for most Tradition Mages I would imagine the insight is more abstracted. Like Kekul\u00e9 imagining an Ouroboros for the benzene ring.<br /> For my hypothetical mage, it could be something like a vision of a group dance where the dancers form patterns as an analogy for forming snow crystals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the imagery, but my thought actually is more that observing the motion of the molecules, or in your example's case, getting a vision of a group dance sounds more like a Forces 1 effect, not a Matter 1 effect, to me. I've always interpreted Matter as a very static sphere - you perceive the object as it is, very thoroughly - you see the effect of the force (or maybe the footprints of the dancer), but not the dance itself.<br /> <br /> To me, it makes sense that converting water to ice is actually a more difficult Matter effect than turning water into glass, because Matter is not the sphere that generally governs that process. The natural transformation from gas to water to ice is entirely a matter of Forces. (Both on a macro level, i.e. temperature control, or a micro level, i.e. forcing molecules to move faster or slower.)<br /> <br /> Obviously, it's still possible to turn water into ice using Matter, but what we perceive with Matter is the state as it is. So we'd need to be able to perceive what changed between states, and then be able to enact that transformation exactly. To me, that feels much more complicated than either using Forces to influence it the easy way, or to cheat and use Matter to transform the water into something else entirely (i.e. glass) and then turn that something else back to ice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T16:17:59-07:00","id":1539265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539261#post1539261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12193_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12193\" data-vbnamecard=\"12193\">Saikou</a>, the problem is that you focus on showing how we can use a very strict interpretation of the setting to make all the inconsistencies solve themselves, and fail to grasp that the setting is open to interpretation, but the rules fall apart (to a degree) when taken seriously under other perfectly valid interpretations.<br /> <br /> Every paradigm should be supported without much of a problem. You insists that the problem don't exist because those paradigms are just wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which paradigm am I saying is wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T16:30:09-07:00","id":1539269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539261#post1539261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What!?<br /> <br /> Knowing that a material exists and that it would be relatively common knowledge in the 12th century is meta-gaming?<br /> <br /> I'm talking about that precisely because the way to avoid meta-gaming would be to know history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I misunderstood you and apologize. I was thinking you were talking about a player having knowledge of modern materials who would use it for a character who doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539261#post1539261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and the example is more than a little racist. A lot of real people live in equatorial islands, this level of ignorance is not how someone is just because they're born on the equator and/or in an island.</div> </div> </div> </div>I chose an equatorial island as the first place that came to mind where ice and snow conceivably may not occur naturally, and in times before widespread information networks may only learn about it by word of mouth. I definitely wasn't trying to make a statement about the ignorance of people living in such places. If it came across as such, I again apologize.<br /> My first impulse was actually to construct something with drawings by medieval european monks of animals they have never seen and only knew by description, but that was outside the Matter Sphere so I dropped it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T17:23:55-07:00","id":1539273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539262#post1539262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like the imagery, but my thought actually is more that observing the motion of the molecules, or in your example's case, getting a vision of a group dance sounds more like a Forces 1 effect, not a Matter 1 effect, to me. I've always interpreted Matter as a very static sphere - you perceive the object as it is, very thoroughly - you see the effect of the force (or maybe the footprints of the dancer), but not the dance itself.<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div> At the atomic level Matter begins to resemble Forces one way or another, because every property of a material is ultimately a result of the forces at play at the quantum level.<br /> <br /> Once we accept Matter and Forces as distinct Spheres, it comes with accepting that internal motions are governed by Matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539265#post1539265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which paradigm am I saying is wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>The scientific one. Repeatedly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T17:59:43-07:00","id":1539276,"title":"","content":"Post deleted, sorry about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-25-2024, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T18:20:27-07:00","id":1539280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539273#post1539273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the atomic level Matter begins to resemble Forces one way or another, because every property of a material is ultimately a result of the forces at play at the quantum level.<br /> <br /> Once we accept Matter and Forces as distinct Spheres, it comes with accepting that internal motions are governed by Matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The scientific one. Repeatedly.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a difference between using a scientific paradigm to work the spheres and trying to fit the spheres to mundane science.<br /> <br /> The former is something a mage might do, it includes things like Quantum theory to explain quintessence, subatomic rearrangement to describe transmutation, Chao theory to explain a model for predicting the future via Entropy etc.<br /> <br /> The latter however is sleeper talk, it adheres to the idea that the reality that you are taught to expect is the only reality there is, and it is that which is simply toeing that Technocratic line. This is the consensus which one needs to push away from in order to achieve true magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T19:29:25-07:00","id":1539286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539273#post1539273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once we accept Matter and Forces as distinct Spheres, it comes with accepting that internal motions are governed by Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Additionally, Life relates to Matter and Forces the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T20:22:52-07:00","id":1539290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539280#post1539280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There is a difference between using a scientific paradigm to work the spheres and trying to fit the spheres to mundane science.<br /> <br /> The former is something a mage might do, it includes things like Quantum theory to explain quintessence, subatomic rearrangement to describe transmutation, Chao theory to explain a model for predicting the future via Entropy etc.<br /> <br /> The latter however is sleeper talk, it adheres to the idea that the reality that you are taught to expect is the only reality there is, and it is that which is simply toeing that Technocratic line. This is the consensus which one needs to push away from in order to achieve true magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the point.<br /> <br /> A big part of the setting is how the Ultimate Real Truth is unknowable, but ultimately any paradigm (or most, at least) could be right about it.<br /> <br /> It's not about your belief being able to produce magic. It's about your belief being Right. Ascension is many things, understanding the real workings of the universe is one of those things.<br /> <br /> For this aspect of the setting to work, it must be possible for every major paradigm to provide some evidence about itself. Not to prove they can do magic, but to prove they can explain the universe.<br /> <br /> Your take on it is that this one theory is actually true, it is the objective truth, based on the fact that it explains every inconsistency in the rules.<br /> <br /> But it ignores that this isn't the actual lore of the actual setting. The lore is open ended. Everything, <b>including science,</b> may be the actual, fundamental, truth (give or take necessary fine adjustments).<br /> <br /> Earthly Foundations are a core concept here. What are they? This should be <b>unknowable</b>. Any guess flies, <i>including actual scientific laws</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T20:23:04-07:00","id":1539291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539195#post1539195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe a silly example, but:<br /> <br /> Xochitl was born and raised on an island near the equator. She has seen rock turn to lava, wood to smoke, and clouds to rain. With Matter 3, she was able to extrapolate on that and turn wood liquid and water solid. However, due to her circumstances, she has never seen ice or snow, or even knows those exist. When she turns water solid, it is a literal solid block of water, not ice. One day a visitor from the mountains tells her about that white and cold powder that disappears if it warms up, but is kinda sticky and looks like small flowers when it falls from the sky.<br /> There is a chance that Xochitl can make the connection that this is just a special state of water, but more likely to her it is a very weird substance with strange properties that is beyond what she can do with Matter 3.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">Please avoid implications that any group lacks a basic understanding of the natural world based on geography</span></b><b><span style=\"color:#e74c3c\">.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T23:01:57-07:00","id":1539294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539253#post1539253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;At this Rank (matter 3), the mage can alter the shape of materials in whatever ways she desires, and she can temporarily transform their essential state into a different one \u2013 steel, for example, into fog or water into glass.&quot; M20 Pg 518<br /> <br /> You only need to read the entry to see the examples are of transmutation that allows the changing of state.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is never stated its not steel fog, steel in gas form that is. As for glass i always interpreted it as not cold ice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T01:07:35-07:00","id":1539295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539290#post1539290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not the point.<br /> <br /> A big part of the setting is how the Ultimate Real Truth is unknowable, but ultimately any paradigm (or most, at least) could be right about it.<br /> <br /> It's not about your belief being able to produce magic. It's about your belief being Right. Ascension is many things, understanding the real workings of the universe is one of those things.<br /> <br /> For this aspect of the setting to work, it must be possible for every major paradigm to provide some evidence about itself. Not to prove they can do magic, but to prove they can explain the universe.<br /> <br /> Your take on it is that this one theory is actually true, it is the objective truth, based on the fact that it explains every inconsistency in the rules.<br /> <br /> But it ignores that this isn't the actual lore of the actual setting. The lore is open ended. Everything, <b>including science,</b> may be the actual, fundamental, truth (give or take necessary fine adjustments).<br /> <br /> Earthly Foundations are a core concept here. What are they? This should be <b>unknowable</b>. Any guess flies, <i>including actual scientific laws</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it is the lore of the setting. Time and again all throughout the books it is stated that the consensus is a manufactured reality. Set up by the technocracy in order to make reality rigid. The point of it is to make it so \u2018magic\u2019 is achievable without ever having to awaken. That their version of ascension is to make it so there is no difference between what magic could do and mundane science, such that any act magic could accomplish is free from any paradox. They use tools such as media propaganda, education, history revisionism, and brute force to ensure that the sleepers never believe that reality can be anything more than what the technocracy tell it to be. This is part of the reason why the Etherites split off, their favourite theory of Ether was stricken from the timetable.<br /> <br /> Every single mage is aware of the consensus, including the technocracy. Their paradigm is how they explain how the mage gets around the consensus. Whether that be by accessing a higher power, pulling free from the illusion, having a will strong enough to overide the consensus, being able to porgramme your way out of the consensus, or using the powers that remained untainted in the old world when the consensus was not in place.<br /> <br /> the paradigm \u2018technology holds the answers\u2019 is built on the point that this idea is inverted, that technology is the key to understanding the world and each form of acientific advancement is building up on new theories. But there is an important distinction here between awakened use of science and sleeper mundane science. Awakened use of science seeks to consider the current consensus as a limiting factor, awakened scientists see the current tools of chemistry as similar to the tools of alchemy, limited in their scope. To do awakened science is to push for the impossible, and that requires dispelling much of the erroneous notions that are stuck within the consensus. For example, Einstein had to conclude that Newton was wrong. And so the modern scientific mage today goes on to conclude that Einstein was wrong. The current model of science as the sleepers understand it is limited and controlling, again, designed by the technocracy to be that way as they have their desire to slowly trickle down magic to the masses like an empire distributes wealth to its distant colonies.<br /> <br /> these are the mages harnessing quantum physics to see through time, using the theory of relativity to its full potential by converting matter in to energy, causing electromagnetic pulses to rip holes in space for quick transportation. All things which the consensus says is not yet possible, but the mage knows better. What the technocracy says is and isn\u2019t true or possible is simply propaganda designed to keep the sleepers reliant on them.<br /> <br /> and from the technocracy perspective, this is exactly the case. Their mantra is that of the Enlightened Anthropic Principle, which states that humanity rejects anything that they do not wish to accept. They reject magic because they can no longer accept magic, but they can accept the rationality their form of science allows. But not all of it, not yet. For them the process of introducing new theories is one of gently allowing the masses to get accustomed to the ideas so that it can become accepted and thus a part of reality itself. Their thoughts on tech holding the answers is on how they themselves can bring new areas of control over reality and slowly incorporate them in to the consensus. But make no mistake, anyone who uses awakened science, or even enlightened science, before the masses risks the entire operation, they risk humanity rejecting it and as a result the entire field is set back, and that is seen in both paradox and unbelief. In time the technocracy will shatter old ideas to make new ones more palatable, they have already done this a number of times as the etherites will tell you, and it may become necessary for ease of introduction<br /> <br /> So the mage can use mundane science as the basis for their belief, but by definition, if they are to do sphere magic, then they in some way violating the consensus, but to get to the truth of how the universe functions that does mean pushing past the accepted truths of reality. Such as the explanation of gravity which even real scientists today agree is a vast simplification.<br /> <br /> any sphere magic done by definition violates conventional science. For scientific mages, this too does not mean science is wrong, but that what the sleepers have accepted is a vast simplification, there is more, so much more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T01:11:22-07:00","id":1539296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539294#post1539294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is never stated its not steel fog, steel in gas form that is. As for glass i always interpreted it as not cold ice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, you\u2019ve revealed yourself to be beyond convincing.<br /> <br /> if your argument is that glass is actually ice, then you can argue anything written is whatever you want it to be to fit your house rule. So there is little point in discussing further with you.<br /> <br /> i hope you can at the very least understand what my argument is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T03:16:26-07:00","id":1539301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539296#post1539296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, you\u2019ve revealed yourself to be beyond convincing.<br /> <br /> if your argument is that glass is actually ice, then you can argue anything written is whatever you want it to be to fit your house rule. So there is little point in discussing further with you.<br /> <br /> i hope you can at the very least understand what my argument is.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest v20 writers werent the smartest people on the planet. Calling water in a solid state as ice would require temperature change. I still think matter cant change temperature so calling it glass makes emotional sense although i would go for cristal.<br /> And yes i get your argument. Still i believe each point of a sphere does a unique thing. Matter 2 is transformation, Matter 3 is shaping. You could change a block of concrete into water with Matter 2. You would not change its shape and it would disperse after the transformation. Doing the same with Matter 3 on your interpretation seems redundant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 07-26-2024, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:00:59-07:00","id":1539303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539301#post1539301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest v20 writers werent the smartest people on the planet. Calling water in a solid state as ice would require temperature change. I still think matter cant change temperature so calling it glass makes emotional sense although i would go for cristal.<br /> And yes i get your argument. Still i believe each point of a sphere does a unique thing. Matter 2 is transformation, Matter 3 is shaping. You could change a block of concrete into water with Matter 2. You would not change its shape and it would disperse after the transformation. Doing the same with Matter 3 on your interpretation seems redundant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok\u2026you can\u2019t change a block of concrete in to water with Matter 2. Regardless of anything else, this is specifically stated as not possible.<br /> <br /> \u201cWith advanced knowledge, the mage can transmute<br /> one substance into another, so long as she doesn\u2019t alter its essential shape, temperature, or basic state (gas, liquid, solid).<br /> Depending upon that mage\u2019s practice, she might reshape<br /> lead into gold through alchemy, wood into stone through a<br /> hyperpetrification process, or water into wine\u201d<br /> M20 Pg518<br /> <br /> it specifies you cannot change the matter target\u2019s basic state. If it sterted solid it must stay solid, this is also seen in revised with further examples provided<br /> <br /> \u201cThe mage may transmute one substance into another,<br /> without changing its shape, temperature or basic state (solid, liquid, gas). The object simply takes on a new composition, at the mage\u2019s whim. Complex creations are more difficult or in some cases impossible; usually, mages are limited to creating or transmuting homogenous substances \u2014 a block of wood into a brick of stone, for instance, but not into an alloy of gold and osmium. Naturally, the sorts of possible transmutations depend<br /> heavily on paradigm. A Hermetic mage might turn lead into gold alchemically, a Chorister could duplicate the miracle of turning water into wine but a Technocrat is more likely to convert simple elements like hydrogen to helium.\u200b<br /> MRev Pg172<br /> <br /> Revised even has the following rote to really show the limitations of Matter 2<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 Straw into Gold \u2014 Just like Rumpelstiltskin, the mage<br /> can weave base matter into a valuable substance. It remains a homogenous material, but it takes on qualities desired by the mage. Vulgar willworkers may literally turn tears into diamonds and straw into gold. More subtle magicians could improve the quality of an existing object, or \u201caccidentally discover\u201d that an object is more valuable than it first appeared. In this fashion, a mage can turn cheap beer into a decent stout, make generic brands seem of higher quality and cause an ordinary item to actually be made of something valuable.\u200b<br /> MRev Pg173<br /> <br /> So if your concrete was cold enough, you could indeed change it to ice, and then let it melt prior to the duration expiring to get a puddle shape of solid concrete if so desired. But you can\u2019t change it directly to water in the same way you can\u2019t change it directly to melted butter.<br /> <br /> mage 2e has essentially this line:<br /> <br /> \u201cMaking things hotter or colder than they were originally, or to change one substance into another with a higher or lower potential energy, requires a conjunctional Effect with Forces, though Matter alone can change ice into ice cream or boiling water into hot soup.<br /> Transmuting solids into liquids or liquids into gas requires either Matter 3 or the use of Forces 3/Prime 2 (or some mundane means) to boil or freeze the affected substance.\u200b<br /> M2e Pg204<br /> <br /> which specifically calls out liquid to solid transmutation as something Matter 3 is required for, and has not been contradicted in any other edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:20:22-07:00","id":1539304,"title":"","content":"Hmm missed that. Then i would have to agree its not posiible (although it makes matter 2 a very limited and sad sphere).<br /> <br /> As for 2e examples were not taking them to account here. It would be really strange for matter to impose power over forces domain.<br /> <br /> The thing that i think is really stupid is puting things like liquid wood or gas steel into matter 5. That would be probably the most underwelming 5 lvl sphere there is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:25:57-07:00","id":1539305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539304#post1539304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm missed that. Then i would have to agree its not posiible (although it makes matter 2 a very limited and sad sphere).<br /> <br /> As for 2e examples were not taking them to account here. It would be really strange for matter to impose power over forces domain.<br /> <br /> The thing that i think is really stupid is puting things like liquid wood or gas steel into matter 5. That would be probably the most underwelming 5 lvl sphere there is.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Mage 2e specifically states Matter 3 would require either mundane means to heat or cool, or use of forces for the changing of state of substances (something that Matter 5 can do without need by changing the melting point or boiling point of matter). But at Matter 3 level you could for example transform table salt in to oxygen<br /> <br /> as for liquid wood, I would say this is a similar thing to what Matter 5 does for making warm ice, you be changing the melting point of wood to be bellow the ignition point (which incidentally is another thing you can change in substances with Matter 5, creating flammable ice, as an example)<br /> <br /> you could also make liquid wood with Matter 4, which allows the creation of otherwise impossible alloys, here it would be an alloy of Wood and water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-26-2024, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:31:43-07:00","id":1539308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539305#post1539305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> you could also make liquid wood with Matter 4, which allows the creation of otherwise impossible alloys, here it would be an alloy of Wood and water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you invented that more than it is RAW but it is REALLY cool, im going to do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T17:45:40-07:00","id":1539347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539301#post1539301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling water in a solid state as ice would require temperature change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly.<br /> <br /> The state of matter is determined by the bonds between molecules, which is a distinct property from their temperature. Heat is just the most readily available means to change those bonds. We can achieve the same effect with enough pressure, after all.<br /> <br /> During a transition of state, temperature doesn't change, either. The heat is used/produced by the change in state. If you could force the material to assume a solid configuration, it would theoretically retain the new state even if at a distinct temperature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T17:49:52-07:00","id":1539349,"title":"","content":"As soon as you can shape matter magically, you would have all you need to change its state without changing temperature.<br /> <br /> Not saying that's how the rules do or should work (although I think it would be cool), just clarifying that state isn't as determined by temperature as it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T10:54:58-07:00","id":1539380,"title":"","content":"After all this discussion, I came to the realization that, indeed, Matter could use a rework. The way I would do it would be:<br /> <br /> 1 - Sense Matter (not much changed)<br /> 2 - Shape Matter (change the form or the state)<br /> 3 - Natural Transmutation (transmute NATURAL matter into other NATURAL matter)<br /> 4 - Artificial Transmutation (transmute matter into any sort of artificial creations; change properties)<br /> 5 - Impossible creations (create matter that breaks the laws of reality)<br /> <br /> And with that arrangement I would also go away with all the &quot;multiple parts&quot; thing which I've always disliked.<br /> <br /> And now, Enriched Uranium sits firmly under Matter 4, along with Napalm, Plastic, Kevlar and even steel. Gold however is Matter 3, and Vibranium, anti matter and black holes remain at Matter 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T12:29:55-07:00","id":1539382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539380#post1539380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After all this discussion, I came to the realization that, indeed, Matter could use a rework. The way I would do it would be:<br /> <br /> 1 - Sense Matter (not much changed)<br /> 2 - Shape Matter (change the form or the state)<br /> 3 - Natural Transmutation (transmute NATURAL matter into other NATURAL matter)<br /> 4 - Artificial Transmutation (transmute matter into any sort of artificial creations; change properties)<br /> 5 - Impossible creations (create matter that breaks the laws of reality)<br /> <br /> And with that arrangement I would also go away with all the &quot;multiple parts&quot; thing which I've always disliked.<br /> <br /> And now, Enriched Uranium sits firmly under Matter 4, along with Napalm, Plastic, Kevlar and even steel. Gold however is Matter 3, and Vibranium, anti matter and black holes remain at Matter 5</div> </div> </div> </div>You do you, but I don't think this solves anything.<br /> <br /> All this does not is shift the argument to what counts as an artificial creation or not. Like smelted alloys, is Steel harder to produce than Gold? And if you can't change the properties until Matter 4 but you can change state at Matter 2, then how does that work when it comes to temperature? Could you, for example, convert the nitrogen in the air into liquid nitrogen at Matter 2?<br /> <br /> And when can you do the Sculpture rote? Where you can make complex objects like a gun from a rock? Usually it's Matter 4, but that's also the lowest level of which I can turn a lump of plastic in to metal.<br /> <br /> Also, does that now mean I can't transmute anything made of plastic until the 4th rank? So copper armor is now harder to affect than a polyester suit?<br /> <br /> There is more I could complain about, like how this messed up the progression of transmutation I explained to you earlier, and you in fact agreed with. Or how this makes it so changing density is now not possible as you change something's shape, making it so you can't reinforce your clothing until Matter 4, unless you change it to a stronger material with Matter 3, or how removing parts means Matter 2 because ludicrously powerful since you could turn the ground beneath you into an dungeon complex with enough successes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T14:23:34-07:00","id":1539390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539382#post1539382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do you, but I don't think this solves anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. That's the beauty of the Golden Rule after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All this does not is shift the argument to what counts as an artificial creation or not. </div> </div> </div>Errrr.... No? &quot;Natural&quot; as opposed to &quot;artificial&quot; is pretty self explanatory - as in &quot;found in nature&quot; as opposed to &quot;modified by human interaction&quot;. There's no mistaking in here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like smelted alloys, is Steel harder to produce than Gold? </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is why I specifically and purposefully used both in my previous post as an example. Gold would be Matter 3, Steel Matter 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you can't change the properties until Matter 4 but you can change state at Matter 2, then how does that work when it comes to temperature? Could you, for example, convert the nitrogen in the air into liquid nitrogen at Matter 2? </div> </div> </div>Temperature isn't the only condition for the state of matter. There's also pressure.<br /> <br /> However, in what comes to Magik, it is the magic that keeps the matter in whatever state you so desire, for as long as the effect lasts. Not the temperature, not the pressure.<br /> <br /> - &quot;wow, is that liquid nitrogen? But how could nitrogen be liquid at room temperature?&quot;<br /> - &quot;It's simple my apprentice. It's MAGIC!&quot;<br /> <br /> As soon as the magic vanishes, the material will resume its natural properties: liquid iron will solidify, liquid nitrogen will evaporate and so on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And when can you do the Sculpture rote? Where you can make complex objects like a gun from a rock? Usually it's Matter 4, but that's also the lowest level of which I can turn a lump of plastic in to metal. </div> </div> </div>I always hated all that &quot;complex objects&quot;. It was always nonsensical to me. So, now you can create:<br /> - a bunch of rocks with Matter 3 (as opposed to having to create them one by one with several effects)<br /> - summon a computer with Matter 4<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, does that now mean I can't transmute anything made of plastic until the 4th rank? So copper armor is now harder to affect than a polyester suit? </div> </div> </div>Cooper is actually a naturally occurring element. I think you mistook it with Bronze, in which case yes, it would require Matter 4.<br /> <br /> And you can transmute anything into a naturally occurring element with Matter 3. You can turn plastic into leather with Matter 3, or you can turn paper into leather, but you can't turn leather into paper or plastic into paper until Matter 4.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is more I could complain about, like how this messed up the progression of transmutation I explained to you earlier, and you in fact agreed with. </div> </div> </div>I agreed in the context we have. Changing the premisses however, changes the angle upon which I look at it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or how this makes it so changing density is now not possible as you change something's shape, making it so you can't reinforce your clothing until Matter 4, unless you change it to a stronger material with Matter 3, or how removing parts means Matter 2 because ludicrously powerful since you could turn the ground beneath you into an dungeon complex with enough successes </div> </div> </div>You don't need Magic to make a dungeon under your Sanctum, all you need is a shovel and a lot of time and a lot of slaves. Magic in here will just save you time.<br /> <br /> This is one of the least impressive uses of Matter. The really powerful stuff is creating highly useful materials. Turning your clothes into as strong as steel or kevlar is much more useful and powerful than sculpting walls. <br /> <br /> As it is, you can summon walls of solid steel with just Matter 2 (well, with the need to add Prime 2 and 1 Quint to it, but still).<br /> <br /> This is INSANE. You can basically easily and effortlessly create your own &quot;personal portable bunker&quot; with Matter 2.<br /> <br /> Like I said before, you can turn the ground bellow enemies into TNT with just Matter 2. Again, ridiculously overpowered.<br /> <br /> And with those small tweaks, it all goes away, and the division is easy to understand, easy to apply and makes sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T14:36:23-07:00","id":1539393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539248#post1539248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting thought. What would a mage observe with matter 1 when water freezes? The actual substance isn't really changing. It's still H2O. The properties that do change are the temperature (which is an outside force acting upon it), or the interaction of its atoms and molecules, which would also, IMO, be more of a Forces thing than a Matter thing.<br /> <br /> My own thought is that the mage would get a snapshot of the water as it exists in the state of being water, and water as it exists in the state of being ice. They would be able to tell that, fundamentally, it's the same thing. But what would they observe about the process itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Matter 1, or Life 1, or Forces 1 or whatever sensorial magic tells the Mage is based on his Paradigm and his set of skills.<br /> <br /> A Mage with a PhD in chemistry would see Matter in a combination of molecular/ionic/metallic interactions, known substances and their chemical nomenclatures, beyond their physical properties (mass, density, resistance, elasticity and so on).<br /> <br /> A pre historic Mage would see things as a matter of comparison with something known, for instance &quot;as strong as rocks but as flexible as leather&quot;.<br /> <br /> And like already explained by many people above, temperature is NOT what defines the state of matter, it's just one of the contributors. What defines the state of matter is the molecular arrangements of it - which temperature can influence, but pressure also factors in.<br /> <br /> So, changing the state of matter is a simple process of changing their molecular interactions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T15:28:09-07:00","id":1539395,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> <br /> <br /> A shovel\u2026.really\u2026that\u2019s your argument against why matter 2 doing as you desire it do isn\u2019t moving to ridiculous levels? That is very much ignoring the point<br /> <br /> anyway, lets focus on the natural vs non natural argument, especially considering refinment counts as non natural <br /> <br /> To put more examples, pretty much all household objects are not immutable until matter 4<br /> <br /> Not just plastic, but glass, paper, leather (all of ehich are processed), crockery ( glazed), silk, wool (which is processed, cleaned and often dyed), rubber, conrete\u2026 all of these are non Natural as thry all require processing to reach the point of being a household good. And many of them can\u2019t be touched by Matter before they are processed because they would still be Life patterns.<br /> <br /> there are precious few things thar mater 3 actually let you manipulate. You\u2019re pretty much limited to certain metals (and then only in their raw ore form, not purified) crude oil, most geological stones and gems, air, river water, sea water, some underground gases, dirt, biomass, and that might be it.<br /> <br /> Especially if you consider refining materials as unnatural like with plutonium, it means no transmuting in to oxygen since the air is naturally a mix of different gasses or which oxygen is not even the largest component. Same with CO2 and Argon, you don\u2019t get natural occurrences of these gasses in a pure state.<br /> <br /> the same goes for Citric acid, it naturally occurs within fruits and so has a lot of impurities including sugars and cellulose, ignoring the fact that it is also a life pattern initially. The only hydrochloric acid you could make is essentially vomit, which is arguably a life pattern as well, And forget about sulfuric acid which doesn\u2019t occur naturally at all. Wine? Doesn\u2019t occur naturaly, cheese? Not possible till Matter 4.<br /> <br /> honestly this really does make Matter 3 look pretty useless, especially since there isn\u2019t a problem matter 3 could solve that Matter 2 wouldn\u2019t perform better.<br /> <br /> The only thing I could consider is turning things in to more precious things\u2026and that is such a weak power. Like cool, you do the lead in to gold thing\u2026.what does that actually accomplish in the heat of the moment? If you want something to be stronger you can just reinforce it with Matter 2, if you want to make something softer, just break it down with matter 2, if you need to put out a fire just sculpt it to smother the flame. The uses of matter 3 become so situational that most would just see it as a pointless step to get to the real transmutation of Matter 4","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T17:27:19-07:00","id":1539398,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of distinguishing between natural and artificial, either, but not nearly that much.<br /> <br /> Current Matter 2 is insanely overpowered in the hands of anyone with some chemistry knowledge or access to Google and/or Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> Magus Maximus is right in this: the ability to create the material you want is far more important and powerful than being able to magically shape the result. Current Matter 2 can transmute the ground below the enemy into a pool of hydrochloric acid with a few successes. What's the problem with being able to conjure a trench?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-27T18:55:41-07:00","id":1539403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539395#post1539395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> <br /> <br /> A shovel\u2026.really\u2026that\u2019s your argument against why matter 2 doing as you desire it do isn\u2019t moving to ridiculous levels? That is very much ignoring the point<br /> <br /> anyway, lets focus on the natural vs non natural argument, especially considering refinment counts as non natural<br /> <br /> To put more examples, pretty much all household objects are not immutable until matter 4<br /> <br /> Not just plastic, but glass, paper, leather (all of ehich are processed), crockery ( glazed), silk, wool (which is processed, cleaned and often dyed), rubber, conrete\u2026 all of these are non Natural as thry all require processing to reach the point of being a household good. And many of them can\u2019t be touched by Matter before they are processed because they would still be Life patterns.<br /> <br /> there are precious few things thar mater 3 actually let you manipulate. You\u2019re pretty much limited to certain metals (and then only in their raw ore form, not purified) crude oil, most geological stones and gems, air, river water, sea water, some underground gases, dirt, biomass, and that might be it.<br /> <br /> Especially if you consider refining materials as unnatural like with plutonium, it means no transmuting in to oxygen since the air is naturally a mix of different gasses or which oxygen is not even the largest component. Same with CO2 and Argon, you don\u2019t get natural occurrences of these gasses in a pure state.<br /> <br /> the same goes for Citric acid, it naturally occurs within fruits and so has a lot of impurities including sugars and cellulose, ignoring the fact that it is also a life pattern initially. The only hydrochloric acid you could make is essentially vomit, which is arguably a life pattern as well, And forget about sulfuric acid which doesn\u2019t occur naturally at all. Wine? Doesn\u2019t occur naturaly, cheese? Not possible till Matter 4.<br /> <br /> honestly this really does make Matter 3 look pretty useless, especially since there isn\u2019t a problem matter 3 could solve that Matter 2 wouldn\u2019t perform better.<br /> <br /> The only thing I could consider is turning things in to more precious things\u2026and that is such a weak power. Like cool, you do the lead in to gold thing\u2026.what does that actually accomplish in the heat of the moment? If you want something to be stronger you can just reinforce it with Matter 2, if you want to make something softer, just break it down with matter 2, if you need to put out a fire just sculpt it to smother the flame. The uses of matter 3 become so situational that most would just see it as a pointless step to get to the real transmutation of Matter 4</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so? I guess you're not really understanding the power of creating raw materials at scale and with easy. Not everything in a Mage's life revolves around the &quot;heat of the moment&quot;. Tell me how &quot;useless&quot; this is next time your Mage turns sand into water in the middle of a desert.<br /> <br /> I think you're lacking in imagination about the real possibilities. In pre industrial societies, this would create abundance, and in industrial societies, this could create at scale.<br /> <br /> You can also carve entire fortresses out of sand for example. This is far far away from being useless.<br /> <br /> Granted, it is much weaker than current Matter 2, but that's exactly the point, Matter 2 as it is, is absurdly overpowered. Turning the floor bellow your enemies into sulfuric acid is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Now, a medieval Mage that can turn the mountainous soil his tribe lives in into highly fertile soil, that can create a spring of water from rock, open the mountains to create an underground fortified city, turn useless silicates into iron ore, he would turn his backwards hillmen shepherds into conquerors.<br /> <br /> A Technocrat can use this to mine rare earth elements from mud.<br /> <br /> And this also gives an amazing economic power to the Mage. Mages are also social creatures, and money is also power. It's even one of the backgrounds, you actually have it on your sheets.<br /> <br /> The ability to &quot;conjure money&quot; should not be taken so lightly. &quot;Simply&quot; turning lead into gold is something massive! I cannot fathom how so many people treat this as just some minor thing.<br /> <br /> It is also much more within the spirit of the Sphere of Matter. That's the sphere of &quot;Stuff&quot;. With a capital &quot;S&quot;. It is literally the sphere for hoarding. Not the Sphere for &quot;at the heat of the moment&quot; being able to throw additional dices of damage on enemies.<br /> <br /> A Mage with Matter 3 is basically set for life; he could in fact forget about Ascension entirely and just focus on creating Stuff. Anything else he needs he could build himself or hire someone qualified to do it for him. Does he needs armors and weapons? Hire a blacksmith, here's the iron ore and take that gold as payment. Need food? My lands are the most fertile that are, hire the serf farmer and take this gold as payment. And the rival barons don't dare to invade me because mine are the best castles in the kingdom. I also produce tons of milk and honey, that pour out of rocks, which I use to export to the other barons (not that I really need anything from them). My baronate also has the best water in all the kingdom, because I simply turn sea water into &quot;volcanic mineral water&quot; with my &quot;holy purifier&quot;.<br /> <br /> Technocrats can turn pollutants into volcanic rocks for fertilizers. They can turn trash into soil, dangerous chemical wastes from industries into clean water and toxic fumes into clean air.<br /> <br /> With this you could breath toxic gases for example.<br /> <br /> There are many, many many uses for this, and it is a lot more balanced than what we have, and you can still do plenty of stuff with it - and getting rich is just one of the things, which is a very very hard thing to be able to do even with Magic - other than Matter, the only other ways to do it would be with Entropy to know how to do it and to get some helping hand into it, or with Mind to become the best &quot;con artist&quot; in the world, &quot;convincing&quot; people to throw their money into your feet.<br /> <br /> But Matter is still the best and easiest way to get rich.<br /> <br /> Again, it is still insanely powerful but not completely broken as it is.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T01:48:03-07:00","id":1539414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, so? I guess you're not really understanding the power of creating raw materials at scale and with easy. Not everything in a Mage's life revolves around the &quot;heat of the moment&quot;. Tell me how &quot;useless&quot; this is next time your Mage turns sand into water in the middle of a desert.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>i.e. your matter 3 is only of use in niche situtations<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're lacking in imagination about the real possibilities. In pre industrial societies, this would create abundance, and in industrial societies, this could create at scale.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>which your version of Matter 3 cannot create because they all count as unnatural creations<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> <br /> You can also carve entire fortresses out of sand for example. This is far far away from being useless.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>you can do that with your Matter 2\u2019s reshape and fuse capabilities, making the sand as strong as any steel. Changing it to a material like wood or copper doesn\u2019t actually make the fortress stronger since strength can be handled by your matter 2. If anything it makes it more vulnerable since wood can be burned and copper can be electrified. So I don\u2019t see the benefit your version of matter 3 offers in this case over matter 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Granted, it is much weaker than current Matter 2, but that's exactly the point, Matter 2 as it is, is absurdly overpowered. Turning the floor bellow your enemies into sulfuric acid is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>that is not possible with canon Matter 2, as such a thing requires changing state.<br /> <br /> so I\u2019ll assume you meant to write matter 3. And in theory yet it is possible to make the floor sulphuric acid. But doing so would require a number of successes to make it concentrated enough to do any damage and the area deep enough to be more than a small puddle. And depending on what the floor is made of, it might not be possible at all.<br /> <br /> but your version of Matter 2 is far more powerful as you could for a similar amount of successes just cause the ground beneath them to become a pit of spikes just by shaping and fussing. Something that wouldn\u2019t be possible until cannon Matter 4. So if you believe the acid under foot is over powered at canon matter 3, well\u2026you have made something equatable at matter 2 now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Now, a medieval Mage that can turn the mountainous soil his tribe lives in into highly fertile soil, that can create a spring of water from rock, open the mountains to create an underground fortified city, turn useless silicates into iron ore, he would turn his backwards hillmen shepherds into conquerors.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>you would probably need Life for that since much of what makes soil fertile are life patterns.<br /> <br /> but in any case, all of those things are still possible with canon matter 3. But with far less inflexibility. And again if your main argument is that \u2018it is very useful when you aren\u2019t in the modern setting\u2019 then that is another example of how niche you have made this sphere rank<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> A Technocrat can use this to mine rare earth elements from mud.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Something which canon matter 2 could do far better\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> And this also gives an amazing economic power to the Mage. Mages are also social creatures, and money is also power. It's even one of the backgrounds, you actually have it on your sheets.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason this wasn\u2019t terribly viable using canon Matter 2 is because transmutation is temporary by default, rare elements are harder to transmute things in to than more common substances (rarity being a metaphysical property based on expectation rather than literal abundance), and actually trying to sell anything like this would quickly catch the attention of the NWO and Syndicate who do bot take kindly to anything that could destabilise their economy<br /> <br /> alchemist mages who try these get rich quick schemes soon find themselves getting visits from the \u2018IRS\u2019.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> The ability to &quot;conjure money&quot; should not be taken so lightly. &quot;Simply&quot; turning lead into gold is something massive! I cannot fathom how so many people treat this as just some minor thing.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>because the technocracy make this far more trouble than it is worth to do long term. That and why exactly do you need money if you can sustain your needs with magic?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> It is also much more within the spirit of the Sphere of Matter. That's the sphere of &quot;Stuff&quot;. With a capital &quot;S&quot;. It is literally the sphere for hoarding. Not the Sphere for &quot;at the heat of the moment&quot; being able to throw additional dices of damage on enemies.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>if you\u2019re trying to argue that Matter is only really a downtime sphere then that really does explain why your version of the Matter sphere has been slanted so far in that direction. I imagine most players would be somewhat frustrated to hear when they get to matter 3, their only real use for it is to start downtime projects, especially compared to what the canon sphere provides.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> A Mage with Matter 3 is basically set for life; he could in fact forget about Ascension entirely and just focus on creating Stuff. Anything else he needs he could build himself or hire someone qualified to do it for him. Does he needs armors and weapons? Hire a blacksmith, here's the iron ore and take that gold as payment. Need food? My lands are the most fertile that are, hire the serf farmer and take this gold as payment. And the rival barons don't dare to invade me because mine are the best castles in the kingdom. I also produce tons of milk and honey, that pour out of rocks, which I use to export to the other barons (not that I really need anything from them). My baronate also has the best water in all the kingdom, because I simply turn sea water into &quot;volcanic mineral water&quot; with my &quot;holy purifier&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>riveting gameplay\u2026<br /> <br /> let\u2019s ignore how quickly the technocracy would shut that down, and how the stuff your people would make are things you at Matter 3 would then be unable to transmute as they are now man made.<br /> <br /> none of what you are describing is neseccarily impossible with canon matter 3, but again cannon matter 3 is less restrictive. You could for example turn the stone in to the armor directly, or change rocks in to water, or sand in to grain. Putting the effort in to make it last long enough for the nutrients to become part of the life pattern and you are all good.<br /> <br /> i do not see how these arguments show that your version is better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> Technocrats can turn pollutants into volcanic rocks for fertilizers. They can turn trash into soil, dangerous chemical wastes from industries into clean water and toxic fumes into clean air.<br /> <br /> With this you could breath toxic gases for example.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>All of which is possible with canon Matter 3, and canon matter 2 is all you need to transform your breath in to toxic gas. Not that that is advisable as it means you are now breathing toxic gas, but that would be true regardless of how you divvy up the spheres.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539403#post1539403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> There are many, many many uses for this, and it is a lot more balanced than what we have, and you can still do plenty of stuff with it - and getting rich is just one of the things, which is a very very hard thing to be able to do even with Magic - other than Matter, the only other ways to do it would be with Entropy to know how to do it and to get some helping hand into it, or with Mind to become the best &quot;con artist&quot; in the world, &quot;convincing&quot; people to throw their money into your feet.<br /> <br /> But Matter is still the best and easiest way to get rich.<br /> <br /> Again, it is still insanely powerful but not completely broken as it is.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You haven\u2019t done much to express why your system is better. The problems you claim it fixes are still present in your version of the rule, and your insistence that Matter is more of a downtime sphere and thus you will now mechanically enforce only makes it far less appealing a sphere to invest experience towards.<br /> <br /> I get being defensive about a thing you have designed, but if you are trying to bill it as better than the default, it has to be more than just better for you, it has to actually feel like an improvement, and in its current incarnation, I don\u2019t think your reinterpretation is for a number of reasons, many of which I have already voiced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-28-2024, 04:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T11:14:57-07:00","id":1539434,"title":"","content":"Just a quick note:<br /> <br /> You don't need Life patterns to make fertile soil. You just need a couple chemicals, the main one being Nitrogen. The biggest challenge is to break Nitrogen in the atmosphere, were it is overabundant, and put it in the soil.<br /> <br /> Living beings are good at doing that, but unless you'll argue that we need Life to make bird poop, it isn't outside even his version of Matter 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-28T12:34:26-07:00","id":1539438,"title":"","content":"Also.. I kinda remember Saikou arguing about how the Technocratic paradigm where soil is a complex matrix of inert matter and organisms isn't' &quot;truth&quot; when we were talking about the interaction of chemicals and energy.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, yes, Magus Maximus's revised Matter has some issues and needs work. It's also a proposed house rule that was just posted, and likely hasn't been heavily developed. The thinking behind it, even if not the details, is hard to dismiss as wrong-minded. Constructive refinement is better for people that want a more functional Matter Sphere than the current rules, not holding the RAW as needed to be defended as holy writ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T07:39:13-07:00","id":1539470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539414#post1539414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> i.e. your matter 3 is only of use in niche situtations</div> </div> </div> </div>No it is not. But you may think as you wish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> which your version of Matter 3 cannot create because they all count as unnatural creations </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand. My version Matter 3 can be used to create raw materials at scale - particularly rare ones. Then you just need to manufacture.<br /> <br /> That in my opinion is a pretty amazing power by itself. I really think that the game designers AND players gloss over that fact.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you can do that with your Matter 2\u2019s reshape and fuse capabilities, making the sand as strong as any steel. Changing it to a material like wood or copper doesn\u2019t actually make the fortress stronger since strength can be handled by your matter 2. If anything it makes it more vulnerable since wood can be burned and copper can be electrified. So I don\u2019t see the benefit your version of matter 3 offers in this case over matter 2. </div> </div> </div>Errr.... No, you can't. I think you misunderstood what Matter 2 would do. It would change shape or the state. It cannot change properties - like density or resistance. It cannot change sand. You could make a sand castle... But that wouldn't be of much use right?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> that is not possible with canon Matter 2, as such a thing requires changing state. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but you can turn the floor into TNT which is solid. Then you just need a spark.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> so I\u2019ll assume you meant to write matter 3. And in theory yet it is possible to make the floor sulphuric acid. But doing so would require a number of successes to make it concentrated enough to do any damage and the area deep enough to be more than a small puddle. And depending on what the floor is made of, it might not be possible at all.<br /> <br /> but your version of Matter 2 is far more powerful as you could for a similar amount of successes just cause the ground beneath them to become a pit of spikes just by shaping and fussing. Something that wouldn\u2019t be possible until cannon Matter 4. So if you believe the acid under foot is over powered at canon matter 3, well\u2026you have made something equatable at matter 2 now. </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThat frankly is the least of my concerns to be honest. MtA is not D&amp;D hack and slash, and the Spheres aren't just a bunch of tables for different forms to give extra dice of damage.<br /> <br /> Matter is insanely powerful because of it's ability to conjure stuff out of thin air (or turning mud into valuables). This is something that is hugely powerful. A player with vanilla Matter 2 only need some skills and/or Contacts to turn manufacturing a bunch of cool toys - computers, weapons, security systems, tracking devices, you name it. Add more Magik shenanigans to it and it gets insane.<br /> <br /> And with the ability to turn mud into gold, it is pretty easy to find people willing to accept your gold in exchange for these manufactured items.<br /> <br /> Hell, with Matter 2 you can open up a drug cartel...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> you would probably need Life for that since much of what makes soil fertile are life patterns. </div> </div> </div>No you don't. The life patterns turn the soil fertility, but the fertile soil is matter.<br /> <br /> Besides, one of the most fertile types of soil comes from volcanic ashes. It is the best thing for plants.<br /> <br /> By the way, milk, honey, saliva, sweat, nectar, amber, anything that is produced by living beings but is not inside of one, is matter. And is natural too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but in any case, all of those things are still possible with canon matter 3. But with far less inflexibility. And again if your main argument is that \u2018it is very useful when you aren\u2019t in the modern setting\u2019 then that is another example of how niche you have made this sphere rank </div> </div> </div>It is you that is saying it is &quot;niche&quot;, not me. I just think you lack the imagination to see it. My examples were just so you wouldn't think that it would just be a Sphere made for industry.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Something which canon matter 2 could do far better\u2026 </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no kidding, I know that Sherlock, and that's PRECISE THE POINT.<br /> <br /> Your problem is that you don't see the many countless problems present throughout the entirety of the game, because to you, the &quot;canon&quot; books are the holy gospel of perfection. We've been there already. You don't see the problems, instead you try to fit circular solutions into these square problems so that the holy canon remains unchallenged.<br /> <br /> Problem is, most people I have ever seen don't think that way.<br /> <br /> I know canon Matter 2 can do that, and do it better, AND THAT'S A PROBLEM.<br /> <br /> Matter is not only completely unbalanced and broken, it is also a mess. But you cannot see it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason this wasn\u2019t terribly viable using canon Matter 2 is because transmutation is temporary by default, rare elements are harder to transmute things in to than more common substances (rarity being a metaphysical property based on expectation rather than literal abundance), and actually trying to sell anything like this would quickly catch the attention of the NWO and Syndicate who do bot take kindly to anything that could destabilise their economy<br /> <br /> alchemist mages who try these get rich quick schemes soon find themselves getting visits from the \u2018IRS\u2019. </div> </div> </div>Really? Oh my, who would've thought?<br /> <br /> And what about if the one trying to get rich is the Syndicate itself huh?<br /> <br /> Look, I am well aware that the NWO and the Syndicate exist.<br /> <br /> I wasn't suggesting trying to sell 1000 tons of cocaine into the black market tomorrow.<br /> <br /> I mean, there is a certain expectation that a Mage should be at least somewhat smart.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is using it for giving a little push. You buy a farm and oh my, it is super productive. You buy a mine and of my, rare earth minerals in it. Plus a few kilograms of gold as a bonus.<br /> <br /> There are margins that can be improved and edges to push that are still safe from catching the notice of the NWO or Syndicate.<br /> <br /> If you're dumb enough to conjure a ship filled with gold, trying to smuggle it into China or Russia, then you deserve what you get.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> because the technocracy make this far more trouble than it is worth to do long term. That and why exactly do you need money if you can sustain your needs with magic? </div> </div> </div>Again, you lack imagination. That is self evident now.<br /> <br /> Why do you think that there is the Resource background at your sheet?<br /> <br /> You definitely CAN get rich without attracting too much trouble if you're careful and smart. Vampires do this all the time for heck's sake!<br /> <br /> And why do you need money for? Well, let's see:<br /> <br /> Lands: do you like to have your Arcane Fortress in a secluded place on the countryside, or would you rather having to hide your esoteric paraphernalia every time your neighbor from the floor bellow comes knocking at your door because of the loud noise from your apartment?<br /> <br /> Buildings: there's a difference between having your Sanctum in a tiny apartment and a huge Mansion. It is not only due to comfort or opulence (which you as the player may not care about, let your character suffer), but there's many practical aspects to it - in order to practice your Magik, you need tons of trinkets. It's easier to do it in a huge Palace (get better bonuses and what not)<br /> <br /> Influence: money opens doors. Money is a tool of social control. You can use it to control (or at least influence) authorities, the media, police and so on. You can use it to hire qualified people - and I'm not just talking armed security for your chantry. I'm talking about stuff like a Software company working for you. I'm talking about &quot;professional New Agers&quot; that you cynically hire in order to attract gullible people for whatever end.<br /> <br /> Seriously, if you can't see how or why money is more than just useful, it is almost essential, then I honestly don't know what to do with you.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if you\u2019re trying to argue that Matter is only really a downtime sphere then that really does explain why your version of the Matter sphere has been slanted so far in that direction. I imagine most players would be somewhat frustrated to hear when they get to matter 3, their only real use for it is to start downtime projects, especially compared to what the canon sphere provides. </div> </div> </div>Again, you lack imagination.<br /> <br /> And no, I never implied that Matter is only a &quot;down time Sphere&quot;. But the thing is thou, that Matter is SUPER insane for that down time. Absolutely unbalanced for it.<br /> <br /> And that's perhaps not what &quot;players would think&quot;, but rather what YOU think because, again, you have a personal issue of taking the canon as absolutely perfect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> riveting gameplay\u2026<br /> <br /> let\u2019s ignore how quickly the technocracy would shut that down, and how the stuff your people would make are things you at Matter 3 would then be unable to transmute as they are now man made.<br /> <br /> none of what you are describing is neseccarily impossible with canon matter 3, but again cannon matter 3 is less restrictive. You could for example turn the stone in to the armor directly, or change rocks in to water, or sand in to grain. Putting the effort in to make it last long enough for the nutrients to become part of the life pattern and you are all good.<br /> <br /> i do not see how these arguments show that your version is better.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> All of which is possible with canon Matter 3, and canon matter 2 is all you need to transform your breath in to toxic gas. Not that that is advisable as it means you are now breathing toxic gas, but that would be true regardless of how you divvy up the spheres. </div> </div> </div>Oh really Sherlock? Yeah, you don't say.<br /> <br /> I know that all that is ALREADY done by canon Matter. No shit.<br /> <br /> What do you think Matter would do?<br /> <br /> That was not my point, I wasn't trying to breed levels of Matter that would throw magic monkeys at enemies, I was pointing out that even by restricting things up, there's still plenty of uses for it to remain useful and worth it. Because, again, as it is, Matter is just simply too insane and unbalanced. It really doesn't even begin to compare to any other Sphere except at the higher levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You haven\u2019t done much to express why your system is better. The problems you claim it fixes are still present in your version of the rule, and your insistence that Matter is more of a downtime sphere and thus you will now mechanically enforce only makes it far less appealing a sphere to invest experience towards. </div> </div> </div>That's your opinion. If you were to play at my table, you would be welcomed to choose other Spheres if that's your wish. You're not forced to pick any one of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I get being defensive about a thing you have designed, but if you are trying to bill it as better than the default, it has to be more than just better for you, it has to actually feel like an improvement, and in its current incarnation, I don\u2019t think your reinterpretation is for a number of reasons, many of which I have already voiced. </div> </div> </div>I'm not defensive about it. I don't care if you like it or not, that's your right to like or dislike whatever you will. I liked it, and I'll use it. That's all that matters to me. You do you. If you continue to believe that the holy book of Mage the Ascension is the Gospel from heavens, you do that in your games and that's fine. Meanwhile, I'll do my own stuff, and that's fine too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T07:47:24-07:00","id":1539471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539438#post1539438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also.. I kinda remember Saikou arguing about how the Technocratic paradigm where soil is a complex matrix of inert matter and organisms isn't' &quot;truth&quot; when we were talking about the interaction of chemicals and energy.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, yes, Magus Maximus's revised Matter has some issues and needs work. It's also a proposed house rule that was just posted, and likely hasn't been heavily developed. The thinking behind it, even if not the details, is hard to dismiss as wrong-minded. Constructive refinement is better for people that want a more functional Matter Sphere than the current rules, not holding the RAW as needed to be defended as holy writ.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think that Matter needs some refinement and balancing - as it is, that sphere is both confusing and soooo broken.<br /> <br /> The problem is... How. And by how, what I mean is &quot;how to do this in a simple and concise way&quot; rather than a total clusterfuck way that would require a PhD into &quot;pseudo-bullshittery&quot;.<br /> <br /> I thought upon the division between &quot;natural&quot; and &quot;artificial&quot; because it is simple, easy to understand and makes sense in terms of progression (after all, manufactured stuff is more useful than raw stuff).<br /> <br /> But I am all ears to any other type of suggestions. Because, perhaps I lack the imagination to do it. Imagine having to summon the periodic table for this task... Yeah, that wouldn't be any good.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that we need something that is &quot;Paradigm Neutral&quot;. We can't have something based on the Periodic Table of chemistry any more than we could make it based on &quot;percentage of earth, water, wind and fire&quot;. The division between &quot;natural&quot; and &quot;artificial&quot; is pretty paradigm neutral thou.<br /> <br /> But if anyone could make a few suggestions, I would appreciate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T12:18:17-07:00","id":1539489,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28035\" data-vbnamecard=\"28035\">Magus Maximus</a><br /> Look, if you're going to start going in to personal insults and strawman arguments then you become someone who is very unappealing to discuss ideas with.<br /> <br /> Saying that your opponent has a lack of imagination in response to them seeing flaws in your idea is just insulting and really does come across as dismissive at best, and incredibly arrogant at worst.<br /> To say that my only position is &quot;book material is gospel&quot; is a strawman argument which is equally dismissive and tells me you have no actual interest in what it is I am saying, where I am coming from, or even why it is I am making these observations.<br /> I gave you the benefit of the doubt last time, but if this pattern of discourse proves to be a trend, I might save you the trouble of discussion in future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 07-29-2024, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-29T12:45:15-07:00","id":1539490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539471#post1539471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But if anyone could make a few suggestions, I would appreciate</div> </div> </div> </div>I was tinkering with it in my head. What about composites? Level 3 could cover only homogeneous substances, at most splitting successes to conjure more than one thing and let them mix uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> Level 4 would be for complex constructs, where pieces made of several substances interact in complex ways.<br /> <br /> So Matter 3 would be able to conjure simple materials and assemble them into an object, but Matter 4 would be necessary to make any electronics, bombs, etc.<br /> <br /> Just throwing the idea, does it sticks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-31T22:57:25-07:00","id":1539623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1539490#post1539490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was tinkering with it in my head. What about composites? Level 3 could cover only homogeneous substances, at most splitting successes to conjure more than one thing and let them mix uncontrolled.<br /> <br /> Level 4 would be for complex constructs, where pieces made of several substances interact in complex ways.<br /> <br /> So Matter 3 would be able to conjure simple materials and assemble them into an object, but Matter 4 would be necessary to make any electronics, bombs, etc.<br /> <br /> Just throwing the idea, does it sticks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it has to be something like that. It has to be simple to both understand and explain, it has to make sense and to give a sense of progression (and in here we can add &quot;progression&quot; in the meaning of both complexity and usefulness) and it must also be &quot;Paradigm Neutral&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's what I think that all Spheres should adhere to so... Yeah, such a simple task lol.<br /> <br /> But &quot;homogeneous&quot; is a good start. How about properties? That's Matter 4?<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's actually not bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-01T14:31:59-07:00","id":1539663,"title":"","content":"I think properties should be 4, yes. Even if homogeneous, this level 3 is already quite potent, messing with &quot;common&quot; properties seems right to be at 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T10:51:43-07:00","id":1545056,"title":"","content":"So what can Matter 5 do alone? Radioactive materials were mentioned here. But can it make alone things that affect other spheres? A helmet that isolates from mind contact for example? Or a shield that negates all vibrations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T13:02:48-07:00","id":1545064,"title":"","content":"You can do stuff like playing with the properties of matter in ways that aren't natural. Like, you can create liquids that act like a solid on certain circumnstances, make transparent metal, create substances with 0 mass, create ice that never melts, make bullets that treat bulletproff vests as air .<br /> <br /> This does interact with forces a lot. And you most definitely can do some &quot;forces related&quot; shenanigans with pure matter. A pretty blatant example would be Antimatter (Matter 5, creates big boom in contact with matter). On Revised there's two interesting examples that use pure matter: Weigth Alteration (it is what it sounds like), and changing how patterns interact each other (this can do stuff like making pattern matters insubstantial in regards to other patterns, but also allows to do things like giving anything the properties of a superconductor)<br /> <br /> Considering the examples I think it would be within reason to allow stuff like creating a floating surfoard (like back to the future) by changing how the matter of the table interact with solids and liquids by &quot;repelling&quot; (as magnets), instead of making the board insubstantial as per the &quot;changing how patterns interact&quot; rule, with a dash of &quot;radioactive implies Matter can go a bit into Forces&quot;<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't allow to diverge too much into the realm of ephemeral spheres. Like, I wouldn't allow &quot;a helmet that isolates from mind contact&quot; w/o Mind.<br /> <br /> Primium does still need Prime 3 added to Matter 5, after all. Same with creating a Matrix (Matter 5 (inanimate) or Life 5 (living) + Prime 3. Effect fuses Tass into foundation, creating permanent vessel for Quintessence.)<br /> <br /> But, by combining Spheres, you can totally create a substance that would protect against psychic assaults by simply existing, which can then be used to make whatever such a substance could make. Which it's still pretty special, I would say, normally you would need Prime skill to make a &quot;Wonder&quot; to do anything remotely similar, and I'm not sure average Wonders can be changed form freely w/o loosing their properties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T13:26:54-07:00","id":1545067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545064#post1545064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can do stuff like playing with the properties of matter in ways that aren't natural. Like, you can create liquids that act like a solid on certain circumnstances, make transparent metal, create substances with 0 mass, create ice that never melts, make bullets that treat bulletproff vests as air .<br /> <br /> This does interact with forces a lot. And you most definitely can do some &quot;forces related&quot; shenanigans with pure matter. A pretty blatant example would be Antimatter (Matter 5, creates big boom in contact with matter). On Revised there's two interesting examples that use pure matter: Weigth Alteration (it is what it sounds like), and changing how patterns interact each other (this can do stuff like making pattern matters insubstantial in regards to other patterns, but also allows to do things like giving anything the properties of a superconductor)<br /> <br /> Considering the examples I think it would be within reason to allow stuff like creating a floating surfoard (like back to the future) by changing how the matter of the table interact with solids and liquids by &quot;repelling&quot; (as magnets), instead of making the board insubstantial as per the &quot;changing how patterns interact&quot; rule, with a dash of &quot;radioactive implies Matter can go a bit into Forces&quot;<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't allow to diverge too much into the realm of ephemeral spheres. Like, I wouldn't allow &quot;a helmet that isolates from mind contact&quot; w/o Mind.<br /> <br /> Primium does still need Prime 3 added to Matter 5, after all. Same with creating a Matrix (Matter 5 (inanimate) or Life 5 (living) + Prime 3. Effect fuses Tass into foundation, creating permanent vessel for Quintessence.)<br /> <br /> But, by combining Spheres, you can totally create a substance that would protect against psychic assaults by simply existing, which can then be used to make whatever such a substance could make. Which it's still pretty special, I would say, normally you would need Prime skill to make a &quot;Wonder&quot; to do anything remotely similar, and I'm not sure average Wonders can be changed form freely w/o loosing their properties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah here is the problem cant you do the antigravity thing with matter 3 forces 2? sounds way more cost effective than matter 5, same with primium it sound like a matter 2 prime 3 effect. Spend 2x the needed successes and its permament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-31T07:10:36-07:00","id":1545092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545064#post1545064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Same with creating a Matrix (Matter 5 (inanimate) or Life 5 (living) + Prime 3. Effect fuses Tass into foundation, creating permanent vessel for Quintessence.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I'd keep this one as an example. The writing is all over the place when it comes to matrices/periapts. In the actual Prime writeup it isn't even clear that Matter is needed or what it would be used for. The effects listed immediately before and immediately after call for other spheres, but the one for periapts does not. That said, the Prime 3 writeup also makes it sound like it is describing filling a periapt instead, which is actually a capability of Prime 2. So we either have the indication that Prime 3 doesn't need help making a periapt, or there is no guidance from the writeup at all. And Matter 5/Prime 3 makes it sound like it is Matter is doing the heavy lifting and Prime is just extending Matter's capabilities (much like how you suggested Mind for the shielding helmet, or like Primium), but in this case Create Periapt is supposed to be Prime's ability, not Matter's.<br /> <br /> Your mileage may vary, of course, but I think this one muddies the waters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545067#post1545067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah here is the problem cant you do the antigravity thing with matter 3 forces 2? sounds way more cost effective than matter 5, same with primium it sound like a matter 2 prime 3 effect. Spend 2x the needed successes and its permament.</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter 2/Forces 2 for antigravity if Matter is only there for the locking effect.<br /> <br /> I'll add that one ability I've been considering for [Pattern Sphere] 5 is the creation of permanent patterns. That is, mages can always create permanent spells/effects, but at [Patttern] 5 they can create things that last permanently without magic. Some of the text in M20 makes it sound like this was the intention, but it isn't very clear. Practically, though, I don't know how often this distinction would come up in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T07:38:54-07:00","id":1545134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545092#post1545092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure I'd keep this one as an example. The writing is all over the place when it comes to matrices/periapts. In the actual Prime writeup it isn't even clear that Matter is needed or what it would be used for. The effects listed immediately before and immediately after call for other spheres, but the one for periapts does not. That said, the Prime 3 writeup also makes it sound like it is describing filling a periapt instead, which is actually a capability of Prime 2. So we either have the indication that Prime 3 doesn't need help making a periapt, or there is no guidance from the writeup at all. And Matter 5/Prime 3 makes it sound like it is Matter is doing the heavy lifting and Prime is just extending Matter's capabilities (much like how you suggested Mind for the shielding helmet, or like Primium), but in this case Create Periapt is supposed to be Prime's ability, not Matter's.<br /> <br /> Your mileage may vary, of course, but I think this one muddies the waters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the descriptions for older editions (up to revised) were always unnecessarily confuse, to the point that Prime alongside Entropy has always been one of the most misunderstood Spheres of all.<br /> <br /> From what I could always get, you can *technically* make Periapts (or even other wonders) using Prime alone - in the case of Periapts, Prime 3 if you have Tass with appropriate Resonance, Prime 4 otherwise (increase 1 lvl to each in case you're turning a living being into one)<br /> <br /> Addendum: you'll still to spend lots of Quintessence to make it, the only thing is that with Prime 4 you can do it with any kind of Quintessence (not necessarily Tass).<br /> <br /> This has always been rather... Strange to me. Because this implies that Prime 4 can change Resonance.<br /> <br /> But you can already change Resonance with Prime 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> The implications for changing Resonance with Prime 1 or 2 thou would be huge for the game.<br /> <br /> Back to Periapts (and Wonders in general), the descriptions given was that you needed Matter to &quot;fuse&quot; the pieces of Tass into your Wonder. But that... That is a weird requirement. As in, Prime alone cannot &quot;transfer&quot; the energy, if you don't physically fuse the materials together, it doesn't work. Makes no sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> I'll add that one ability I've been considering for [Pattern Sphere] 5 is the creation of permanent patterns. That is, mages can always create permanent spells/effects, but at [Patttern] 5 they can create things that last permanently without magic. Some of the text in M20 makes it sound like this was the intention, but it isn't very clear. Practically, though, I don't know how often this distinction would come up in play. </div> </div> </div>For one thing, permanent changes cannot be magically dispelled. Also, using Prime 1 wouldn't identify an ongoing effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T04:33:56-07:00","id":1545206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I could always get, you can *technically* make Periapts (or even other wonders) using Prime alone - in the case of Periapts, Prime 3 if you have Tass with appropriate Resonance, Prime 4 otherwise (increase 1 lvl to each in case you're turning a living being into one)<br /> ....<br /> Back to Periapts (and Wonders in general), the descriptions given was that you needed Matter to &quot;fuse&quot; the pieces of Tass into your Wonder. But that... That is a weird requirement. As in, Prime alone cannot &quot;transfer&quot; the energy, if you don't physically fuse the materials together, it doesn't work. Makes no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. You and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"758\" data-vbnamecard=\"758\">Ramnesis</a> are right. Prime alone should suffice. Non the least because energy transfer and generation it's one of the things Prime alone does.<br /> <br /> It IS a weird requisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah here is the problem cant you do the antigravity thing with matter 3 forces 2? sounds way more cost effective than matter 5, same with primium it sound like a matter 2 prime 3 effect. Spend 2x the needed successes and its permament.</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding about this it's that using Matter 5 youre making a magical <i>material</i>, whereas locking spells on a pattern you're making a magical <i>object</i>.<br /> <br /> A helmet made with Matter 5 + Mind, and one made with Matter 2 + Mind, would both protect your mind the same.<br /> But the second case it's a Trinket, and you can't, say, melt it and forge a batch of mind-protecting jewlery with the metal.<br /> Whereas in the first case you absolutely can, tho the psychic protection may be lessened if the substance it's on lesser quantities (one cold argue if a magical material looses it's properties when melted, or similarly altered, but I would argue that's something the Matter 5 mage has to decide)<br /> <br /> Granted, this is more of an advantage for the likes of the Technocracy that can, say, make a huge lump of &quot;mind protecting alloy&quot; and then distriute it so other agents do whatever they want with it (from helmets to covering a room)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-02-2024, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T09:38:12-07:00","id":1545213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545206#post1545206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My understanding about this it's that using Matter 5 youre making a magical <i>material</i>, whereas locking spells on a pattern you're making a magical <i>object</i>.<br /> <br /> A helmet made with Matter 5 + Mind, and one made with Matter 2 + Mind, would both protect your mind the same.<br /> But the second case it's a Trinket, and you can't, say, melt it and forge a batch of mind-protecting jewlery with the metal.<br /> Whereas in the first case you absolutely can, tho the psychic protection may be lessened if the substance it's on lesser quantities (one cold argue if a magical material looses it's properties when melted, or similarly altered, but I would argue that's something the Matter 5 mage has to decide)<br /> <br /> Granted, this is more of an advantage for the likes of the Technocracy that can, say, make a huge lump of &quot;mind protecting alloy&quot; and then distriute it so other agents do whatever they want with it (from helmets to covering a room)</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems kinda useless for player characters without a giant organisation to disribute and utilise. 5 should not beat the same lvl of usefullness as a combination of two lvl 3 spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T12:47:38-07:00","id":1545217,"title":"","content":"Perhaps at Matter 5 you don't need to spend successes on duration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T13:41:58-07:00","id":1545221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545213#post1545213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That seems kinda useless for player characters without a giant organisation to disribute and utilise. 5 should not beat the same lvl of usefullness as a combination of two lvl 3 spheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need Mind 3 to make the &quot;mind protection alloy&quot; alongside either Matter 2 or 5.<br /> <br /> The thing is, with Matter 5 the material will have the &quot;mind protecting&quot; properties even if broken into tiny pieces. It becomes a property of the material, while with Matter 2 you're simply locking an effect on an object, thus if said object is destroyed, the spell is dispersed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Citrakayah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545217#post1545217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps at Matter 5 you don't need to spend successes on duration.</div> </div> </div> </div>You still need to allocate successes for duration. But you can make it permanent with enough successes <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T15:10:42-07:00","id":1545225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545221#post1545221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You still need Mind 3 to make the &quot;mind protection alloy&quot; alongside either Matter 2 or 5.<br /> <br /> The thing is, with Matter 5 the material will have the &quot;mind protecting&quot; properties even if broken into tiny pieces. It becomes a property of the material, while with Matter 2 you're simply locking an effect on an object, thus if said object is destroyed, the spell is dispersed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and not much gain for the exp buck. Anything thats actually useful to the players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T04:31:18-08:00","id":1545243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545225#post1545225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and not much gain for the exp buck. Anything thats actually useful to the players?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol ok, I respect the way you see it. But that's not the only use of Matter 5. It goes far, far beyond that, to the point that what you can do is only a matter of imagination. Matter 5 is perhaps the most OP power of Mage, at least on par with Entropy 5. You can create &quot;adamantium&quot; and &quot;vibranium&quot; or &quot;orichalcum&quot;, you can create materials hard as a neutron star and as light as a plume and much much more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T05:00:29-08:00","id":1545244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545243#post1545243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol ok, I respect the way you see it. But that's not the only use of Matter 5. It goes far, far beyond that, to the point that what you can do is only a matter of imagination. Matter 5 is perhaps the most OP power of Mage, at least on par with Entropy 5. You can create &quot;adamantium&quot; and &quot;vibranium&quot; or &quot;orichalcum&quot;, you can create materials hard as a neutron star and as light as a plume and much much more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why then no one can give example what it does what you cant do with lower spheres?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T06:59:37-08:00","id":1545247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545244#post1545244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why then no one can give example what it does what you cant do with lower spheres?</div> </div> </div> </div>Matter 5 is to change properties of the Matter. Anything you can think of. You can for instance make Matter that don't interact with a certain type of material. Creating bullets that don't interact with metal for instance could make bullets that are intangible by any sort of armor. You could shoot a tank's crew directly with it for instance. You could make super glue that glues anything that it touches - and never leaves (a bounded target would probably need Life magic to &quot;shed&quot; the glued skin). You can make an acid that dissolves EVERYTHING without ever stoping (it would probably end at the center of the Earth) - what's the use of that would be hard to tell... But perhaps you could make this acid dissolve anything EXCEPT... Glass for instance could be an exception (so that you can store this). You can create a poison that kills by mere contact with it in a fraction of a second. You can create a substance that freezes everything it touches. You can create indestructible materials. You can create a space suit that is invulnerable to external temperatures - technically allowing you to &quot;walk&quot; over the Sun's surface.<br /> <br /> And on and on, these are just a few examples. Any sort of absurd idea you might have, you can make it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-03T09:09:19-08:00","id":1545255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545247#post1545247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Matter 5 is to change properties of the Matter. Anything you can think of. You can for instance make Matter that don't interact with a certain type of material. Creating bullets that don't interact with metal for instance could make bullets that are intangible by any sort of armor. You could shoot a tank's crew directly with it for instance. You could make super glue that glues anything that it touches - and never leaves (a bounded target would probably need Life magic to &quot;shed&quot; the glued skin). You can make an acid that dissolves EVERYTHING without ever stoping (it would probably end at the center of the Earth) - what's the use of that would be hard to tell... But perhaps you could make this acid dissolve anything EXCEPT... Glass for instance could be an exception (so that you can store this). You can create a poison that kills by mere contact with it in a fraction of a second. You can create a substance that freezes everything it touches. You can create indestructible materials. You can create a space suit that is invulnerable to external temperatures - technically allowing you to &quot;walk&quot; over the Sun's surface.<br /> <br /> And on and on, these are just a few examples. Any sort of absurd idea you might have, you can make it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally something.<br /> <br /> As for the acid, poison and armor. Could i just claim the poison kills, armor is indestructible, acid goes through everything or is it still more armor points and more damage points? Cause if its the latter then its no different than matter 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T11:26:17-08:00","id":1545331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545247#post1545247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could make super glue that glues anything that it touches - and never leaves (a bounded target would probably need Life magic to &quot;shed&quot; the glued skin). You can make an acid that dissolves EVERYTHING without ever stoping (it would probably end at the center of the Earth) - what's the use of that would be hard to tell... .</div> </div> </div> </div>Pandoritane, the worlds most adhesive substance. Originally unveiled to the public with the famous picture of a semi truck stuck to the side of a bridge. This was initially thought to be a viral marketing campaign but was later revealed that a truck carrying Pandoritane had an accident. No known substance can remove Pandoritane once it has been applied. Warning: Do not attempt to use Pandoritane Remover to remove Pandoritane from your skin as you will end up permanently gluing an extremely caustic substance to your flesh...<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T17:42:52-08:00","id":1545353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545255#post1545255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally something.<br /> <br /> As for the acid, poison and armor. Could i just claim the poison kills, armor is indestructible, acid goes through everything or is it still more armor points and more damage points? Cause if its the latter then its no different than matter 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can definitely create the &quot;True Essence Substance&quot;. In classical (real life) Alchemy, there is the Alkhalest (something like that), which is the &quot;true acid&quot; or the &quot;essential acid&quot;. &quot;Orichalcum&quot; is the &quot;true gold&quot; or the &quot;essential gold&quot;. There's also one for true Silver, which name I have forgotten, but it exists. All of those are mythical theoretical substances from the medieval times of European Alchemy - much like the idea of the &quot;Philosopher's Stone&quot; - which very few people know, would be a &quot;rock&quot; or non-biological matter that is alive. I claim that our smartphones are all philosopher stones, but I digress.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with Matter 5 you can, indeed, create any and all of these mythical substances. &quot;True Poison&quot; or &quot;The Essence of Poison&quot; simply kills; if you so much as smell it, you're instantly dead. &quot;The Essence of Acid&quot;, or Alkhalest if you want to sound Nerdy and New Age at the same time, corrodes. Without ever stopping. And if you decide to create Adamantium, it is absolutely unbreakable.<br /> <br /> What &quot;Orichalcum&quot; (True Gold) does is up to you to decide. In fact, these mythic substances could be a part of your gameplay, then all you need to do is to determine their properties. And their place on your games.<br /> <br /> A &quot;Essence of Termic Resistance&quot; for example could be a material that is simply 100% immune to any and all sorts of Termic Energy. This &quot;Ceramichalcum&quot; (or &quot;True Ceramic&quot; - which I just invented right now) would allow you to walk over the surface of the Sun. Maybe an &quot;Ironchaulcum&quot; (&quot;True Iron&quot;, but don't use that name, I'm pretty sure there is one historical name for &quot;the essence of iron&quot; from the alchemists of old, I would just need to research) could be a material that is absolutely immune to ANY kinds of energy - that would be basically like Adamantium + Vibranium. A metal that is completely indestructible and that also protects against ANYTHING. You could walk inside a Black Hole wearing an hermetic suit made of that thing, since it would even protect you from the gravity itself.<br /> <br /> And yes, with Matter 5, all of those go. Any sort of &quot;Unobtainium&quot; is possible with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T17:44:26-08:00","id":1545354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545331#post1545331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pandoritane, the worlds most adhesive substance. Originally unveiled to the public with the famous picture of a semi truck stuck to the side of a bridge. This was initially thought to be a viral marketing campaign but was later revealed that a truck carrying Pandoritane had an accident. No known substance can remove Pandoritane once it has been applied. Warning: Do not attempt to use Pandoritane Remover to remove Pandoritane from your skin as you will end up permanently gluing an extremely caustic substance to your flesh...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I heard about that one once some time ago; I didn't know the name of the material. That thing is undoubtedly a Matter 5 product of the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T17:55:38-08:00","id":1545355,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, the medieval Alchemists all had that idea of the &quot;true essence of things&quot;. That's because Alchemy is basically a Gnostic religion; in a very shallow explanation, they believe in Plato's allegory of the cave. Thus, this world would be a fallen, lesser world, and there's a &quot;true world&quot; outside of the reach of our senses; the entire effort of alchemists was to reach this &quot;real world&quot;, to shed the veil of falsehood of our fake fallen world and reach the world of the true divine. No wonder Alchemy was persecuted by the Church. It was 100% Gnostic heresy.<br /> <br /> But for them, there's this &quot;true essence&quot; of everything. And that was the gist of their work, to try to &quot;distill&quot; stuff into its &quot;true essence&quot;.<br /> <br /> Water would be an interesting thing for one to reach its &quot;true essence&quot;. What would &quot;true water&quot; have as its properties? I'll leave that idea to you, but whatever it might be, Matter 5 can do. Maybe its the perfect purifier, removing all impurities that it touches? Maybe something weirder and more arcane? I don't know, I'll let you yourself create. But that is a good starting point to think about strange new materials based on their &quot;true essence&quot;, so use it so that you can play with Matter 5","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-05T12:35:02-08:00","id":1545401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545354#post1545354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, I heard about that one once some time ago; I didn't know the name of the material. That thing is undoubtedly a Matter 5 product of the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I got the name from a British radio comedy called Bigipedia, so if there is some folkloric or alchemical glue, its probably not called Pandoritane. The universal solvent was one of the prize goals of alchemy, though, or so I've heard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-06T06:03:20-08:00","id":1545461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1536501-matter?p=1545401#post1545401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I got the name from a British radio comedy called Bigipedia, so if there is some folkloric or alchemical glue, its probably not called Pandoritane. The universal solvent was one of the prize goals of alchemy, though, or so I've heard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes well, I do think that the Solificati deserved a bit more lore over their metaphysics, like for example what I just described, that &quot;Alchemy&quot; was actually a derivation of the Gnostic creed and an attempt to leave this fallen world and reach the true divine existence. Thus, the Solificati are much more than just the &quot;Alchemy guys&quot;. Alchemy was NEVER a materialistic discipline, it follows much more the ideas of Immanuel Kant about &quot;Immaterialism&quot; or the idea that the entire existence is a figment of imagination - which is 101% Gnostic fantasy. In that sense, Alchemy is the perfectly exact opposite of chemistry. Alchemy is pure fantasy, pure subjective reality, while chemistry is purely materialistic. So it's so fun that one originated from the other.<br /> <br /> These special substances, particularly of the Alchemy-Fantasy type, could be incredible additions to any Mage game. Much like Primium already is for the Technocrats, Primium is basically the &quot;Adamantium&quot; of MtA, AKA the &quot;mystic/magic substance&quot; of the setting. Adding things like Orichalcum or Alkhalest would enrich the setting even further - Orichalcum for instance was said to be used to cover the temples of the Gods in Atlantis by the ancient Greeks philosophers - yeah, that's how mythical that thing was. Imagine trading the metal that was present in freaking Atlantis, how cool is that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}